// Generated by parse_book.py — do not edit by hand.
var BOOK = {"meta":{"title":"AI Sales Secrets","subtitle":"100 Questions That Turn AI into Real Money","heroLines":["Say Goodbye to AI Anxiety","Start Closing Deals & Making Real Money with AI","Use AI to boost efficiency, close more deals, and monetize. Even ordinary people can pull off a comeback."],"author":"Sifu Yik Chan","authorRole":"Author","badges":["Mindset - Strategy - Tactics - Tools, fully broken down","From “Understanding AI” to “Making Real Money”","13 years of entrepreneurial experience, 1,000+ livestreams.","100 of the most practical questions that solve your biggest AI sales bottlenecks."],"generated":"2026-09-05","stats":{"questions":100,"parts":5,"prompts":257,"moneySecrets":98,"dialogues":494,"sifuTurns":246}},"parts":[{"n":1,"title":"Mindset","from":1,"to":18},{"n":2,"title":"Strategy","from":19,"to":30},{"n":3,"title":"Practical Application","from":31,"to":80,"sections":[{"idx":1,"title":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","from":31,"to":50},{"idx":2,"title":"Handling Objections and Closing","from":51,"to":60},{"idx":3,"title":"Relationship Maintenance and Referral","from":61,"to":70},{"idx":4,"title":"Short Video and Livestream Sales","from":71,"to":80}]},{"n":4,"title":"Tools","from":81,"to":98},{"n":5,"title":"The Road Ahead","from":99,"to":100}],"questions":[{"n":1,"title":"Will Sales Reps Be Replaced by AI?","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, AI can now chat with customers, write copy, even run livestreams. Honestly, I'm getting nervous. Is AI going to replace sales as a profession?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Let me ask you something first. Have you ever seen an ATM completely replace a bank teller?"},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"No... but there are definitely fewer of them now."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. What got replaced was the \"cash counter\" job, but the \"financial advisor\" job stayed. Same thing's happening in sales. AI is going to wipe out the reps who just send info packets, quote prices, and pass along messages. But it's going to make the reps who actually understand customers and create real value even more valuable."},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"How do I know which one I am?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Ask yourself: do customers come to you because you have information, or because you solve their problems? If it's just information, AI can already do that faster, cheaper, and better. But if you're the one figuring out their pain points, designing solutions, and even catching what they haven't said out loud, AI becomes your superpower, not your replacement."},{"t":"p","html":"There's a stat from IDC's sales report: by 2026, <strong>75% of sales teams worldwide<\/strong> will be swimming in data but short on actual insight. What that really means is customers don't need more information. They need someone who can turn that information into a decision. That's the salesperson of the future."},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So I need to reposition myself?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Yep. Stop being the guy who just delivers information. Start being the person who helps them decide. Let AI do the heavy lifting. You do the thinking."},{"t":"ms","items":["AI won't replace salespeople. It will replace salespeople who don't know how to use AI.","Your value isn't in what you know. It's <strong>what you can solve<\/strong> for the customer.","The future sales role: <strong>decision partner + human connector<\/strong>.","Ask yourself every day: which tasks can I hand off to AI today, and what absolutely needs my touch?"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":2,"title":"Performance Dropped After Using AI? Watch Out for \"AI Dependency\"","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Morgan","role":"Business Owner","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I took your course and immediately equipped my team with every AI tool I could find. Three months later, performance didn't improve. It dropped by 10 percent. Did I buy the wrong tools?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"If you bought your child the best piano money can buy, would they automatically become a pianist?"},{"t":"d","who":"Morgan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"No. They'd still need a teacher and plenty of practice."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. A tool is just a tool. What matters is how you use it. I've seen too many people fall into <strong>AI dependency<\/strong>. They think that once they have AI, they can coast. The result is copy that lacks a human touch, follow-ups that feel cold, and performance that eventually drops."},{"t":"d","who":"Morgan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"What does that actually look like?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Three common symptoms. First, <strong>lazy thinking<\/strong>, asking AI for answers instead of working through the problem yourself. Second, <strong>lazy optimizing<\/strong>, using whatever AI generates without touching it. Third, <strong>lazy connecting<\/strong>, letting AI handle all the communication so you can hide behind it."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's an example. We coached a company where the sales team used AI to write sales letters. Their efficiency went up, but their response rate fell from <strong>15 percent to 3 percent<\/strong>. Why? The letters were too polished, so polished they didn't sound human anymore. Customers could tell it was a mass email and deleted it on sight."},{"t":"d","who":"Morgan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So what's the right approach?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Treat AI like an intern. Would you send out a draft an intern wrote without reading it first? Of course not, you'd edit it. AI works the same way. It gives you a first draft, and you polish it using your own experience and your read on the customer. Whatever you finally send has to carry your fingerprints."},{"t":"p","html":"One more thing to keep in mind: AI gives you efficiency. You deliver the warmth. AI can help you write 100 emails, but only you can send a heartfelt voice message on a customer's birthday. AI can help you crunch the numbers, but only you can offer sincere advice when a customer is anxious."},{"t":"ms","items":["Three symptoms of AI dependency: <strong>lazy thinking, lazy optimizing, lazy connecting<\/strong>.","Treat AI like an <strong>intern<\/strong>, not a replacement.","Let AI handle efficiency. <strong>You<\/strong> handle the warmth.","Look at your recent customer conversations: how much came from AI, and how much came from you?"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":3,"title":"How Can I Turn AI Into My \"Super Sales Assistant\"?","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I want AI to do the work for me, but I don't know how to work with it. Every time I ask it to write something, it gets it wrong. Fixing it over and over ends up taking longer than just doing it myself."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"How would you train a new hire?"},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"I'd start with training. Walk them through our products, our customers, our pitch. Then have them shadow me for a while before letting them handle things on their own."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"And have you trained your AI the same way?"},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Wait, AI needs training too?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Of course it does. If you handed a brand-new hire who knows nothing a client proposal to write, you can't be surprised when they get it wrong. AI needs an onboarding process too."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's a three-step method for onboarding AI."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Feed it data.<\/strong> Give AI your product manuals, success stories, FAQs, even copy you've written before that worked well. Let it absorb your knowledge base."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Set the rules.<\/strong> Tell it your writing style, your preferred tone, and any words to avoid. Something like, \"When writing to clients, keep it as natural as a conversation between friends. Skip the corporate fluff.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Give it feedback.<\/strong> When AI produces something, praise what works and correct what doesn't. Help it learn your preferences."},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"That sounds like it'll eat up a lot of time."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"You spend time now to save time later, same as training any new hire. The first three months are tiring, then it gets easier. And AI learns faster than people do. Train it for a week, and it can already perform at an intern's level."},{"t":"p","html":"Once it's trained, your AI becomes a super assistant. It never sleeps, and it's always ready to write emails, analyze clients, and draft proposals. All that's left for you is the work that matters most: judging, deciding, and connecting."},{"t":"ms","items":["AI needs onboarding too: <strong>feed it data, set the rules, give it feedback<\/strong>.","Invest time early for a <strong>tenfold return<\/strong> later.","A well-trained AI is a super assistant that never rests.","Your job shifts from <strong>doing the work<\/strong> to <strong>managing it<\/strong>."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":4,"title":"Sales Pros vs. AI: Who Understands the Customer Better?","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Leo","role":"Sales Director","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, our top salesperson has such a strong relationship with clients that they come to him for everything. Can AI ever learn that kind of understanding?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Great question. Let me put it this way: AI understands data. People understand people."},{"t":"p","html":"AI can analyze a customer's purchase history, browsing habits, how often they reach out to you. It can even predict when a client is about to walk away. In that sense, AI understands customers better than any salesperson could, because it processes far more data than a human ever could and spots patterns we'd miss."},{"t":"d","who":"Leo","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"But our top guy knows that a client's kid is taking the college entrance exam this year, or that the client hasn't been feeling well lately."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly, that's the human side of understanding. That kind of information only comes from lunches, casual chats, and genuine care. AI can never replace you sitting down with a client for a meal, or putting a hand on their shoulder when they're stressed."},{"t":"p","html":"One of our students used AI to comb through client data and noticed one client kept searching for information on severance packages. He guessed the client might be job hunting, so he took them to lunch right away. Sure enough, the client was weighing new offers. The student helped them through the transition smoothly. Later, the first thing that client did at the new company was introduce the student to their procurement department."},{"t":"d","who":"Leo","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So AI spots the opportunity, and the person does the actual work?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Right. AI handles discovery, you handle connection. AI tells you who might need something, and you go find out what. AI tells you who might be leaving, and you're the one who shows up with genuine care. That's the ideal partnership."},{"t":"ms","items":["AI understands <strong>data<\/strong>. People understand <strong>hearts<\/strong>.","AI finds the leads. People build the connections.","The best salesperson combines <strong>AI's insight<\/strong> with <strong>human empathy<\/strong>.","Check the data insights AI gives you every day, then pick up the phone and call the person who \"needs your attention.\""]}],"minutes":3},{"n":5,"title":"Will Customers Think I'm Insincere for Using AI in Sales?","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I've never dared to send customers anything written by AI. I'm scared they'll notice and think I'm being insincere. Is that a real concern?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"When you order takeout, do you rate it based on \"sincerity\"?"},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"No. I just care if it tastes good."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. Customers want their problem solved, not proof of who wrote it. If an AI-drafted solution actually fixes their problem, do you think they care who wrote it?"},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"But what about emotional communication? Like comforting a customer or showing you care?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Good question. There are two types here. <strong>Informational communication<\/strong>, which AI can handle for you. And <strong>emotional communication<\/strong>, which you have to handle yourself."},{"t":"p","html":"What counts as informational communication? Sending product materials, scheduling meetings, confirming order details. AI can do all of this quickly and accurately."},{"t":"p","html":"What counts as emotional communication? Comforting a customer going through a hard time, a heartfelt thank you after closing a deal, a genuine birthday message. These have to come from you, because no matter how advanced AI gets, it can't fake real sincerity."},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So how do I balance efficiency with sincerity?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Here's a formula for you: <strong>AI writes the first draft, you add the warmth<\/strong>. Let AI draft it, then rewrite it in your own words, adding in what you know about this specific customer and any shared history between you. That way you get AI's speed and your own warmth."},{"t":"p","html":"One more tip: show up in person at the key moments. Use AI for routine follow-ups, but when it's time to close the deal, when the customer runs into a problem, or on important occasions, you need to be there yourself. Think of it like a movie. AI is the screenwriter, but you're the director and the lead actor."},{"t":"ms","items":["Use AI for <strong>informational communication<\/strong>. Handle <strong>emotional communication<\/strong> yourself.","The test: if the customer can tell it was written by AI, they'll think you're being lazy.","Efficiency formula: <strong>AI writes the draft, you add warmth<\/strong>.","Show up in person at key moments. Let AI handle the routine follow-ups."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":6,"title":"How Can New Salespeople Use AI to Outpace the Competition?","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"New Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I'm only three months into this job and feel like I don't know anything. None of the senior salespeople want to mentor me. Can AI help me grow faster?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"You're actually in luck. AI is the \"super mentor\" built for beginners."},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Really? AI can teach me how to sell?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Of course. Think about why senior salespeople are so good. It's because they carry a \"case library\" in their heads. They've seen every type of customer and handled every kind of objection. That's exactly what you're missing right now, and AI can help you build it fast."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me design an <strong>AI Growth Plan for New Hires<\/strong> for you."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Week one: AI sparring partner.<\/strong> Have AI role-play different types of customers: the pushy one, the hesitant one, the picky one, the silent one. Practice your opening, your questions, your objection handling. AI will give you feedback on what worked and what needs improvement."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Week two: AI mentor.<\/strong> Tell AI about the real customers you're dealing with and let it help you analyze them. Ask it, \"Why is this customer hesitating? How should I follow up?\" AI will suggest strategies for you to try."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Week three: AI copilot.<\/strong> Before sending an email, have AI review it. Before meeting a client, have AI help you prepare a list of questions. After the meeting, have AI help you debrief."},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"If I train like this for a month, how much of a head start would I get?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Six months to a year ahead of everyone else. Because you're not just \"accumulating experience,\" you're \"absorbing everyone else's experience.\" AI has taken in sales cases from across the entire industry, plus your company's product knowledge. It's basically a top salesperson's brain that you can borrow."},{"t":"p","html":"We had a student use this exact method and become the company's top salesperson within three months. He put it this way: \"I'm not smarter than the senior salespeople. I just have a mentor who's online 24 hours a day, and they don't.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["AI is a new hire's <strong>super mentor<\/strong> and personal case library.","New Hire AI Growth Plan: <strong>sparring partner, then mentor, then copilot<\/strong>.","AI can compress a year of growth into <strong>three months<\/strong>.","You're not accumulating experience. You're <strong>absorbing it<\/strong>."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":7,"title":"What If Senior Salespeople Refuse to Use AI?","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Chris","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, a few of my senior salespeople perform great, but they flat-out refuse to use AI. They say their old methods work just fine. I can't get them on board."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"If you told a driver who's spent twenty years driving a manual car to switch to automatic, what do you think they'd say?"},{"t":"d","who":"Chris","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"They'd say it's unnecessary, that they're doing just fine as they are."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. Here's what senior salespeople are worrying about: \"My old methods are working just fine, so why change anything? What if I can't pick it up? Will it make me look incompetent?\""},{"t":"p","html":"A senior's biggest asset is their experience, and AI feels like a threat to that asset. So it's completely natural for them to resist the change."},{"t":"d","who":"Chris","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"How do we fix that?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Four words: <strong>sweet first, bitter later<\/strong>. Don't ask them to learn before they use it. Let them try it first, and they'll want to use it more once they see it actually helps."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Find the pain points.<\/strong> What repetitive task do your seniors hate most? Writing reports? Organizing data? Digging up customer information? Let AI handle those first. Let them taste the benefit."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Set a benchmark.<\/strong> Find one senior on the team who's open to new things and coach them into an \"AI top salesperson.\" Once the others see that person performing better with less effort, they'll naturally want in."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Give them face.<\/strong> When you train them, don't frame it as \"you're outdated.\" Frame it as \"You already have an incredible track record, AI is going to help you 10x that.\" Position AI as a tool that amplifies their experience, not one that replaces it."},{"t":"p","html":"There's one more move worth trying: let the data speak for itself. Have AI analyze their past wins and extract what actually made them successful. Then tell them, \"AI studied your deals and found these three things are why you win. Now AI can help you apply those same three things to every customer you talk to.\" What senior salesperson could resist that?"},{"t":"ms","items":["The root of senior resistance to AI: fear of being replaced, fear of failing to learn.","The fix: <strong>find pain points, set a benchmark, give them face<\/strong>.","Position AI as something that <strong>amplifies experience<\/strong>, not something that replaces it.","Use data to prove AI can make them even better."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":8,"title":"The First Principle of AI Sales: The Efficiency Revolution in Value Creation","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Morgan","role":"Entrepreneur","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, you keep saying sales is really about creating value. So where does AI actually come in?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Quick question: between a chef with years of experience and a cookbook that has every recipe under the sun, who's going to cook something the customer actually loves?"},{"t":"d","who":"Morgan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"The chef, for sure. He knows the customer's mood, how salty they like their food, even when to bring out each course."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. AI is that cookbook. It knows all the standard recipes, but it has no idea how to adjust for this customer, right now. You're the chef in this picture."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's the thing about value creation: your product has 100 features. Your customer cares about maybe 3 problems. Your whole job is turning those 100 features into an answer for those 3 problems, in a way the customer actually understands."},{"t":"p","html":"In that process, AI can help with three things."},{"t":"p","html":"First, <strong>quick analysis<\/strong>. Hand it your product info and it'll list out every possible selling point. Give it a customer profile and it'll guess at their pain points. Think of it as prepping your vocabulary."},{"t":"p","html":"Second, <strong>batch generation<\/strong>. For different types of customers, have AI generate different versions of your pitch, like creating multiple versions of the same message for different audiences."},{"t":"p","html":"Third, <strong>ongoing optimization<\/strong>. Which version gets better feedback? Which one converts better? Let AI track that and keep improving it. That's your quality control."},{"t":"p","html":"But the part that really matters, picking the right pitch for the person in front of you and knowing exactly how to say it, that's on you. Because only you know their tone, your history together, how their day's going."},{"t":"d","who":"Morgan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So AI does the \"prep work,\" and I do the \"live performance\"?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. AI can make you 10x faster at creating value, but the soul of that value always comes from you. That's the first principle of AI sales."},{"t":"ms","items":["Let AI write the recipe. <strong>You hold the spoon<\/strong>: automate the standard stuff, keep the personal touch for yourself.","AI boosts your speed. The <strong>soul of the sale<\/strong> is still all you.","Your job's shifting from \"translating info\" to \"reading the room,\" knowing the right time, person, and way to deliver value."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":9,"title":"Feeling More Tired After Using AI? Time to Upgrade from \"Doer\" to \"Commander\"","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, honestly, I feel more exhausted since I started using AI. Every day I'm writing prompts, cleaning up AI outputs, learning new tools. I'm busier than before."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Sounds like you're not using AI. You're babysitting it."},{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"What do you mean?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Does your daily routine look like this: open AI, type a prompt, wait, feel disappointed, rewrite the prompt, wait again, tweak, repeat? That's not using AI, that's babysitting AI. You've become the AI's assistant, instead of the other way around."},{"t":"p","html":"The real pros run things like a commander. Commanders set the goal, delegate the work, review the output, and give feedback. They don't do the grunt work themselves."},{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So how do I go from babysitter to commander?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Four shifts."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>One: From one-off prompts to a system.<\/strong> Stop writing prompts from scratch every time. Build templates for tasks you do often, sales outreach, handling objections, whatever it is. Next time, just pull it up and tweak it."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Two: From single-use to ongoing training.<\/strong> Treat AI like an employee who's still learning. Praise it when it does well, correct it when it doesn't. Train it for a month, and it'll understand you better and start reading your mind."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Three: From doing it yourself to delegating.<\/strong> Think of AI as a team: one handles copywriting, another analyzes data, a third drafts proposals. Learn to run them in parallel. Assign tasks to all of them at once, then review the results together."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Four: From doer to decision-maker.<\/strong> Your time should go toward deciding \"which plan is best\" or \"which client to follow up with,\" not \"how do I phrase this sentence.\""},{"t":"p","html":"How do you test it? If using AI means more of your time goes to thinking and less to doing, you're on the right track. If it's the reverse, you're still stuck babysitting."},{"t":"ms","items":["Babysitting AI vs. commanding AI: who's really the assistant here?","Four shifts: <strong>templates → ongoing training → parallel delegation → focus on decisions<\/strong>","The real test: thinking time up, execution time down.","The goal: stop doing the grunt work, start running the crew."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":10,"title":"Sales Champion vs. AI Champion: Who Wins the Future?","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Leo","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, last question. What do you think the top salesperson of the future will look like? Someone with the strongest sales skills, or someone who's best at using AI?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Think about an F1 champion. Are they the best driver, or the one who understands the car's engineering best?"},{"t":"d","who":"Leo","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"Probably both."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. The future sales champion will be a mix of two things: sales skill and AI skill."},{"t":"p","html":"Someone with perfect sales skills but zero AI skills might lose to someone with average sales skills but strong AI skills. Why? Because the second person can use AI to multiply what they've already got."},{"t":"p","html":"But it doesn't work the other way either. If your sales skills are weak, even perfect AI skills won't save you. AI is an amplifier. It only makes bigger what you already have. If you can't spot what your customer really needs, AI can write you a hundred pitches and none of them will land."},{"t":"d","who":"Leo","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"So it's multiplication, not addition?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Right. <strong>Final value = Sales skill × AI skill.<\/strong> If either one is zero, your result is zero."},{"t":"d","who":"Leo","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"So what should we do now?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Work on two things at once."},{"t":"p","html":"First: master the basics of sales. Understanding customers, building trust, handling objections, closing deals. These skills never go out of style. Practice them every day. Learn from them every day."},{"t":"p","html":"Second: get good at using AI. Learn how to ask it the right questions, how to train it, how to make it part of your workflow. Turn it into your second brain."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's your goal: in one year, become the salesperson who knows AI best, and the AI user who knows sales best. That combination is your real edge, one that's hard to copy."},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>Final value = Sales skill × AI skill<\/strong>","It's multiplication, not addition.","Build two skills at once: <strong>master the basics + master AI<\/strong>.","Goal: be the best at AI among salespeople, and the best at sales among AI users."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":11,"title":"How to use AI to rebuild your entire sales process?","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Chris","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, our current sales process is still old school: find a list, make cold calls, send materials, and wait for a reply. It feels really inefficient. I want to use AI to fix it up. Where should I start?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Are you trying to fix the <strong>process<\/strong>, or just swap out a <strong>tool<\/strong>?"},{"t":"d","who":"Chris","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Is there a difference?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Of course there is. Using AI to replace one step in your old process is a <strong>tool upgrade<\/strong>. Using AI to design a whole new process from scratch is a <strong>process rebuild<\/strong>. Which one do you want?"},{"t":"d","who":"Chris","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Rebuild, obviously. But how do I actually do that?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Let me give you an <strong>AI Sales Process Rebuild Map<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Old process:<\/strong> Find a list, call, send materials, wait for a reply, follow up, then hope for a sale."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>New process:<\/strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: AI lead generation.<\/strong> Stop searching blindly. Let AI analyze your <strong>ideal customer profile<\/strong>, scan the whole internet for matching leads, and score them. Only follow up on leads scoring <strong>80 or above<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: AI warm-up.<\/strong> Don't call right away. Let AI create <strong>personalized warm-up content<\/strong> based on each customer's profile, maybe an industry insight they'd care about, or a success story from someone in their field. Let the customer get to know you first."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: AI-assisted communication.<\/strong> Before you pick up the phone, have AI build a <strong>communication strategy<\/strong> for that specific customer: what they care about most, what objections they might have, and which case studies will actually move them. Go into the call armed with a plan."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: AI automated nurturing.<\/strong> If a deal doesn't close, don't just file the contact away. Hand it to AI for <strong>automated nurturing<\/strong>, sending useful content on a regular schedule, tracking opens and clicks, and alerting you the moment the customer shows interest again."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: AI closing support.<\/strong> Once you're in negotiations, let AI analyze the customer's objections, draft your responses, and even simulate the negotiation. Bring AI along as your <strong>advisor<\/strong> at the table."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 6: AI referral design.<\/strong> After the deal closes, let AI design your <strong>referral process<\/strong>, write the thank-you note, and plan your repeat-purchase strategy."},{"t":"d","who":"Chris","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"This sounds like two completely different worlds!"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly! In the old process, you chase the customer around. In the new one, AI helps you <strong>weave a net<\/strong>, and customers walk right into it on their own. You go from being a <strong>hunter<\/strong> to being a <strong>net weaver<\/strong>."},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>Old process:<\/strong> the \"hunter\" model (you chase the customer)","<strong>New process:<\/strong> the \"net weaver\" model (AI draws the customer in)","<strong>Six rebuild steps:<\/strong> lead gen → warm-up → communication → nurturing → closing → referral","<strong>Your role:<\/strong> upgrade from a task doer to a <strong>process designer<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":12,"title":"The sales funnel is too long. How can AI fix it?","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"Entrepreneur","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, we work with big B2B clients, and our sales funnel is really long. It takes six months from first contact to closing, and customers seem to forget us after three months. What can we do?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Why do you think the customer \"forgot\" you?"},{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"It's just too much time. They meet so many people every day, they can't remember us."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"That's not quite right. The customer didn't forget you. You simply never took up space in their mind. Over six months, you only showed up three times. A competitor showed up thirty times. Who do you think they'll remember?"},{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"But we can't bug them every day either."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"That's exactly why you use AI for <strong>invisible nurturing<\/strong>. It's not harassment, it's giving them <strong>continuous value<\/strong>. Let me design an \"AI funnel-shortening plan\" for you."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Stage 1 (Awareness):<\/strong> Have AI send the customer a weekly industry insight or report they'd actually care about. It's not a sales pitch, it's a gentle reminder that you're still around. AI generates the content, you just point it in the right direction."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Stage 2 (Interest):<\/strong> When a customer opens the same article more than three times, AI flags it for you: \"They're really interested in this topic, suggest setting up a call.\" Use that as your reason to reach out, and your success rate doubles."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Stage 3 (Decision):<\/strong> Have AI analyze every interaction you've had with the customer to build a <strong>Customer Focus Report<\/strong>. Bring this into the meeting, and the customer will feel like you understand them better than they understand themselves."},{"t":"p","html":"One of our students used this method to shrink a six-month sales cycle down to three months. The secret is this: AI handles the <strong>high-frequency, low-pressure contact<\/strong>, and you handle the <strong>precise strikes at key moments<\/strong>."},{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So it sounds like AI is helping me \"stay visible\"?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"It's not about staying visible, it's about staying valuable. Every time you show up, you need to give the client a reason to actually open your message. That's where AI's real value is. It can create these \"reasons\" at scale."},{"t":"ms","items":["A funnel that's too long means <strong>you have no space in the client's mind<\/strong>.","AI strategy: <strong>invisible nurturing<\/strong> through consistent value.","Three stages: <strong>Awareness<\/strong> (content reach) → <strong>Interest<\/strong> (precise outreach) → <strong>Decision<\/strong> (deep insight).","Goal: make sure that no matter who they forget, <strong>they never forget you<\/strong>."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":13,"title":"In B2B sales, how can AI help you win over big clients?","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Owen","role":"Key Account Manager","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I handle major B2B accounts, deals worth millions. The client's decision chain is complicated: decision-makers, influencers, end-users, and gatekeepers. How can AI help me handle all these different people?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Have you heard how special forces operate? They don't send one person charging in alone. It's a whole team working together: scouts, snipers, demolition experts, commanders, each with their own job."},{"t":"d","who":"Owen","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So you're saying I need to build my own \"combat team\"?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. Except your team members are <strong>AI avatars<\/strong>. For each person in the decision chain, train a different AI assistant to work alongside you."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's how it breaks down:"},{"t":"p","html":"First, for <strong>end-users<\/strong>. They care about whether the product actually works and solves their problem. Train an <strong>AI product expert<\/strong> to answer usage questions and generate case studies and how-to guides. Your job is just to introduce this \"expert\" to them."},{"t":"p","html":"Second, for <strong>influencers<\/strong>. They care about industry trends and new technology. Train an <strong>AI industry analyst<\/strong> to generate fresh updates and reports every day. Use this content to keep feeding the influencers."},{"t":"p","html":"Third, for <strong>decision-makers<\/strong>. They care about ROI, risk, and strategic value. Train an <strong>AI business consultant<\/strong> to analyze the client's business data and generate ROI models and risk assessments. Bring these with you when you meet decision-makers."},{"t":"p","html":"Fourth, for <strong>gatekeepers<\/strong>. They care about compliance, process, and risk. Train an <strong>AI compliance officer<\/strong> to pre-check contract terms and prepare compliance materials. Make the gatekeeper feel that working with you is the easiest, safest choice."},{"t":"d","who":"Owen","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"With that many AI tools running, how do I keep track of it all?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"You just give the task to one main AI. It calls on the other AIs to get the work done, then hands you a complete plan. All you have to do is one thing: bring that plan to the meeting."},{"t":"p","html":"We had a B2B student use this method to close, in three months, a client they couldn't close in a whole year before. He said, \"It's not that I'm so great. It's that my AI team is great.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["Winning big accounts means <strong>winning over everyone in the decision chain<\/strong>.","Your AI team: <strong>product expert + industry analyst + business consultant + compliance officer<\/strong>.","The AIs coordinate with each other. You only need to <strong>bring the plan and show up<\/strong>.","Goal: make everyone in the decision chain feel like <strong>you understand them best<\/strong>."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":14,"title":"How do B2C salespeople use AI to achieve personalized service at scale?","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Lina","role":"eCom Store Owner","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, we run an online store and get hundreds of customer messages every day. If I use templates, customers feel like I'm just brushing them off. But if I try to reply to everyone personally, I can't keep up. Can AI fix this?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"You've heard the phrase \"a thousand faces for a thousand people,\" right? That's basically what AI can do here: send out replies in bulk that still feel personal to each customer."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's a <strong>three-step method for AI bulk personalization<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Segment your customers.<\/strong> Have AI look at each customer's history, past questions, and purchase records, then tag them automatically. For example: new or returning, big spender or small spender, hesitant or decisive, price-sensitive or quality-focused."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Build a template library.<\/strong> For each combination of tags, get AI to generate ten different reply styles. For a new customer who's hesitant and price-sensitive, you might create a template that pushes value for money and a limited-time deal."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Smart matching.<\/strong> When a new message comes in, AI reads the customer's tags and pulls the best-fitting template from your library, then adjusts it based on how the customer responds. Your only job is to check the templates AI generates and make sure they still sound human."},{"t":"d","who":"Lina","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"How much time does this actually save?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our e-commerce students used this method and cut their customer service team from ten people down to three. But here's the thing: their conversion rate actually went up 15 percent. Why? Because AI replies fast and accurately, which makes for a better customer experience. And the people freed up from routine chats now focus on landing big clients."},{"t":"p","html":"The key is this: <strong>AI handles the volume, you handle the personal touch<\/strong>. Set aside one day a week to personally reply to your \"special cases,\" people who complained, repeat buyers, or anyone with potential for a big order. Let AI take care of the routine stuff so you can focus on what really matters."},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>B2C's core challenge<\/strong>: volume versus personal touch","<strong>AI's solution<\/strong>: customer segmentation + template library + smart matching","<strong>Your job<\/strong>: review templates and handle key clients","<strong>Result<\/strong>: 10x efficiency, and conversion rates go up, not down"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":15,"title":"High-ticket products are hard to sell. How can AI help?","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Ryan","role":"Entrepreneur","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I run a high-end consulting business. Each deal is worth hundreds of thousands. Customers always hesitate, they think it's too expensive. I've already explained the value clearly, but I still can't close them. Can AI help?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"When a customer says it's too expensive, is that because they think it's not worth it, or because they're afraid to commit?"},{"t":"d","who":"Ryan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Probably afraid to commit. It's a lot of money, and they don't want to make the wrong call."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. The biggest barrier for high-ticket products isn't the <strong>price<\/strong>, it's the <strong>risk<\/strong>. So your job isn't to prove it's worth it. Your job is to lower their fear."},{"t":"p","html":"AI can help you cut down that sense of risk in three ways:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>First, make your case studies visual.<\/strong> Use AI to turn your past success stories into a \"customer journey animation\" or a \"before and after comparison chart.\" Let the customer see, with their own eyes, the gap between working with you and not. A picture hits ten times harder than words."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Second, use a risk simulator.<\/strong> Get AI to help the customer picture what happens if they don't hire you. Feed in their business numbers, and have AI generate a report estimating potential losses over the next six months. Once they see that <strong>not choosing you costs more than choosing you<\/strong>, the decision becomes easy."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Third, personalize the guarantee.<\/strong> Find out their biggest worry, something like \"what if it doesn't work,\" and use AI to build a custom guarantee around it. Skip the generic \"not satisfied, get a refund\" line. Instead, spell it out: \"If A happens, we'll do B to make it right.\" That makes them feel like the plan was built specifically for them."},{"t":"d","who":"Ryan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"That's a fresh way to think about it. I'll try it."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One more thing you can do: use AI for <strong>decision support<\/strong>. People buying high-ticket products often feel alone while making up their minds. Train an AI to act as a neutral advisor who just answers their questions, no selling involved, just talking things through. A lot of doubts disappear once someone has a chance to talk it out."},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>The real barrier for high-ticket products<\/strong>: not the price, the risk","<strong>Three AI tools to lower risk<\/strong>: case visualization + risk simulation + personalized guarantees","<strong>High-ticket tactic<\/strong>: AI as a \"neutral advisor\" for decision support","<strong>The goal<\/strong>: make the customer feel that not choosing you costs more than choosing you"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":16,"title":"How can I use AI to nurture clients for low-frequency, high-ticket products?","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I work in villa renovation. A client might only do this once in their life. How can I use AI for follow-up business?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Have you heard of <strong>lifetime value<\/strong>? For low-frequency, high-ticket products, the logic isn't <strong>repeat purchases<\/strong>, it's <strong>referrals<\/strong>."},{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"We do ask for referrals, but once the project's done, the client stops talking to us. How do I get them to refer people?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Use AI to keep delivering value, so the client still <strong>needs you<\/strong> even when they're not buying from you."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me design a <strong>low-frequency, high-ticket AI nurturing system<\/strong> for you:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Phase 1: Delivery period.<\/strong> Have AI turn the renovation process into a \"documentary.\" Daily progress, material choices, design thinking, all packaged into polished content and sent to the client. They'll think, \"You care about my home more than I do.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Phase 2: Move-in period.<\/strong> Have AI send the client \"home care tips\" and \"interior design inspiration\" regularly. It's not a sales pitch, it's a signal: \"I still care about your home.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Phase 3: Bragging period.<\/strong> When a client posts photos of their home on social media, use AI to quickly draft a \"professional comment\" you can copy and paste: \"This lighting design is really tasteful, we specifically chose a 3000K color temperature to create that warm feeling.\" It helps the client show off while quietly reminding everyone of your expertise."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Phase 4: Referral period.<\/strong> When AI detects friends praising the client's home on social media, it flags it for you automatically: \"Consider inviting the client to host an open house and bring their friends.\" You can turn leads naturally during that event."},{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Won't this feel too forced?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"When you genuinely help a client take care of their home, what they feel is care, not a sales tactic. AI just helps you turn that care into a service you can keep delivering."},{"t":"ms","items":["The core of low-frequency, high-ticket sales isn't <strong>repeat purchases<\/strong>, it's <strong>referrals<\/strong>","<strong>AI nurturing system:<\/strong> Delivery phase (documentary) → Move-in phase (tips) → Bragging phase (professional comments) → Referral phase (social events)","The essence: make sure the client <strong>still needs you<\/strong> after they've stopped paying","The goal: the client's <strong>social feed<\/strong> is your new battlefield"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":17,"title":"How do I use AI to design a scalable sales SOP?","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Leo","role":"Sales Director","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, my team's skill levels are all over the place. The top performers are great, the weaker ones really struggle. I want to build a standardized sales SOP, but I'm worried it'll be too rigid and hold back my best people. Can AI solve this?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Ever listened to jazz? It has a fixed chord progression, but every musician improvises within that structure. The pros improvise beautifully, and beginners can still play just by following the chords."},{"t":"d","who":"Leo","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So AI is that \"chord progression\"?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. AI isn't a set of rigid rules, it's a <strong>living framework<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me walk you through building a <strong>scalable SOP<\/strong> with AI:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Extract expert experience.<\/strong> Feed your top performers' closed deals, conversation logs, and objection handling into the AI. Ask it to find the common patterns: what do these top sellers do the same way when facing different types of clients?"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Generate a \"strategy tree.\"<\/strong> Have AI map out a sales decision tree: if the client says A, you can choose response B1, B2, or B3, depending on the situation. Beginners follow the tree and never get lost. Experts know when to step off the tree and improvise."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Build an \"AI sparring partner.\"<\/strong> Have AI play different types of clients so new hires can practice. Every time they make a choice, AI gives feedback: \"This response works well for scenario B1, but the client's mood right now is C, so try B2 instead.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Keep optimizing.<\/strong> Every week, feed the team's wins and losses back into the AI so it can update the strategy tree. The SOP isn't set in stone, it evolves every week."},{"t":"d","who":"Leo","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Won't the top performers feel restricted by this?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Not at all. When they see the patterns AI pulls out, \"Oh, so this is why I succeed,\" they get a clearer picture of their own strengths. And when they see their own instincts baked into the AI-generated strategy tree, they're more willing to share."},{"t":"p","html":"One of our clients used this method and cut new-hire ramp-up time from six months to two, all within three months. Team performance went up 30 percent on average. The secret: AI turns <strong>personal experience<\/strong> into <strong>team assets<\/strong>."},{"t":"ms","items":["A scalable SOP = <strong>fixed framework<\/strong> + room to <strong>improvise<\/strong>","<strong>Four-step AI method:<\/strong> Extract experience → Generate a strategy tree → Build a sparring partner → Keep optimizing","Goal: beginners can get up to speed, experts can still shine","The essence: turn <strong>personal experience<\/strong> into <strong>team assets<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":18,"title":"How can sales teams use AI to \"replicate experience\"?","part":1,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Casey","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, we have a top performer who's incredible, but he won't share his secrets. He says it's just a feeling he can't explain. How can I get him to pass his experience on to others?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"It's true, a pro's intuition really is hard to put into words. But AI can see it clearly."},{"t":"d","who":"Casey","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"How does AI see it?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Take his chat logs, emails, and call recordings from the past year, strip out any private data, then feed it all to the AI. Ask the AI to do three things."},{"t":"p","html":"First, <strong>extract keywords<\/strong>. AI will notice that when he talks to hesitant clients, he uses phrases like \"don't worry,\" \"I understand,\" or \"many people feel the same way.\" With aggressive clients, he switches to \"data,\" \"case studies,\" and \"you might consider.\" This is called a <strong>language pattern<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Second, <strong>analyze the rhythm<\/strong>. AI will notice how many days he waits before following up, what he sends, and when he decides to call instead. This is called a <strong>rhythm pattern<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Third, <strong>identify the timing<\/strong>. AI will notice how he responds when a client says things like \"let me think about it\" or \"I need to discuss this.\" This is called a <strong>timing pattern<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Put these together, and you get a <strong>repeatable playbook<\/strong>. New hires don't have to learn a \"feeling,\" they just learn the patterns."},{"t":"d","who":"Casey","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Won't the patterns feel too rigid?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Not at all. You can ask AI to generate <strong>patterns plus variations<\/strong>. For example, if a client says they need to think it over, the standard response is A. If the client is price-sensitive, adjust to A1. If they're worried about results, adjust to A2. New hires learn A first, then pick up the variations once they're comfortable."},{"t":"p","html":"One of our students did this. After passing the top performer's methods to the team, overall performance went up <strong>40 percent<\/strong>. Even the top performer was surprised. He said, \"Is that really how I do it?\""},{"t":"ms","items":["The <strong>intuition<\/strong> a pro can't explain is something AI can see clearly.","AI decodes pros in three ways: <strong>language patterns<\/strong>, <strong>rhythm patterns<\/strong>, and <strong>timing patterns<\/strong>.","Output: a <strong>repeatable pattern library<\/strong> plus situational variations.","Goal: give every team member a piece of the <strong>top performer's playbook<\/strong>."]},{"t":"p","html":"022"}],"minutes":3},{"n":19,"title":"How can I use AI for sales forecasting?","part":2,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Owen","role":"Sales Director","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I get a headache at the end of every month. I ask the team how much they'll close, they say \"no problem,\" and we always miss the mark by a lot. Is there a way to use AI for more accurate forecasts?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Have you asked your salespeople why they think it's \"no problem\"?"},{"t":"d","who":"Owen","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"They say they just have a feeling the client's intent is strong."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Feelings aren't always reliable. The whole point of AI forecasting is turning <strong>feelings into data<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me teach you the <strong>three-step AI forecast method<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Define intent signals.<\/strong> Have the AI analyze past deals to find common behaviors before closing. Things like opening a message three or more times, scheduling two or more meetings, asking about price three times, or mentioning a competitor. These are all <strong>intent signals<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Score the leads.<\/strong> Have the AI scan every active lead and give each one a score based on those signals. Leads above <strong>80 points<\/strong> are \"ready to close.\" <strong>60 to 80<\/strong> \"need nurturing.\" Below <strong>60<\/strong>, \"put on hold.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Generate a forecast report.<\/strong> Have the AI use the number of high-score leads, average deal size, and historical conversion rate to build a <strong>monthly forecast report<\/strong>, showing expected deals closed, expected revenue, and forecast accuracy."},{"t":"p","html":"The key is that this score keeps updating. If a client opens an email today, the score goes up by 1. If they book a meeting tomorrow, it goes up by 5. If they say \"let me think about it\" the day after, it drops by 3. By the end of the month, the forecast keeps getting sharper."},{"t":"d","who":"Owen","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"How do the salespeople take this?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"When you show them the report and ask, \"This client is only at 65 points, why do you think we can close them?\" the salesperson starts to think. They realize the client hasn't shown clear intent yet, and they start asking themselves what it would take to push that score up to 80. That's the shift from <strong>going on a hunch<\/strong> to <strong>working off a strategy<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"One of our clients used this method, and their forecast accuracy jumped from <strong>50 percent to 85 percent<\/strong>. Salespeople stopped guessing. Instead, they'd say, \"I have five clients over 80 points this month. We'll hit the target.\""},{"t":"p","html":"023"},{"t":"ms","items":["The core of AI forecasting: turning <strong>feelings into data<\/strong>.","The three-step method: <strong>define intent signals<\/strong>, <strong>score leads<\/strong>, and <strong>update forecasts dynamically<\/strong>.","The salesperson's role shifts: from <strong>guessing numbers<\/strong> to <strong>driving with strategy<\/strong>.","The result: <strong>more accurate forecasts<\/strong> and <strong>easier management<\/strong>."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":20,"title":"What can AI do during the off-season?","part":2,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Chris","role":"Entrepreneur","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, our industry has clear busy and slow seasons. During the off-season, my salespeople have nothing to do and lose focus. Is there a way to make the off-season productive?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"What do farmers do when they're not planting in the winter?"},{"t":"d","who":"Chris","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"They repair tools, pick seeds, and nourish the soil."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. The off-season isn't about having nothing to do. It's about <strong>doing what you can't do during the busy season<\/strong>. AI can help you do these three things better."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me design an <strong>AI Action Plan for the off-season<\/strong> for you:"},{"t":"p","html":"First, <strong>repair tools<\/strong> (optimize your toolkit). Let AI review your sales data from the past year to find which parts are least efficient and which scripts perform poorly. Then use AI to upgrade your script library, refresh your case studies, and build new sales materials. Use the off-season to perfect what you never have time for during the rush."},{"t":"p","html":"Second, <strong>pick seeds<\/strong> (nurture leads). During the busy season, you only chase high-intent clients. Use the off-season to nurture the low-intent ones you usually ignore. Let AI send them valuable content automatically and monitor their reactions, flagging anyone who shows interest. By the time the busy season hits, those seeds have already sprouted."},{"t":"p","html":"Third, <strong>nourish the soil<\/strong> (develop the team). Let AI generate a <strong>personal growth report<\/strong> for each salesperson: Is your conversion rate 10 percent below the team average? Where's the bottleneck? What do your client profiles look like? What skills need work? Then have AI build a personalized training plan. Learn in the off-season, apply it in the busy season."},{"t":"d","who":"Chris","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So the off-season ends up busier than the busy season?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Busy isn't the goal, productive is. The busy season produces <strong>revenue<\/strong>, the off-season produces <strong>systems<\/strong>. Build the system now, and next year's busy-season revenue doubles."},{"t":"p","html":"One of our students used AI to optimize his system for three off-seasons in a row. By the third year, his busy-season revenue was <strong>triple<\/strong> what it was the first year. He said, \"I used to dread the off-season. Now I look forward to it, because I know I'm planting seeds for the season ahead.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["The off-season is not about having nothing to do. It is about <strong>doing what you cannot do in the busy season<\/strong>.","Three AI actions: <strong>repair tools<\/strong>, <strong>pick seeds<\/strong>, and <strong>nourish the soil<\/strong>.","Off-season output: not revenue, but a <strong>system<\/strong>.","Goal: use <strong>one off-season<\/strong> to win <strong>three busy seasons<\/strong>."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":21,"title":"How can I use AI to analyze competitors?","part":2,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Ethan","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, clients always use competitors to pressure me on price. They say others are cheaper. I want to study my competitors, but I don't have enough time. Can AI help me with competitor analysis?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Do you want to know what your competitors are doing, or do you want to know why clients think they're better?"},{"t":"d","who":"Ethan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Is there a difference?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Of course. The first is <strong>watching the opponent<\/strong>. The second is <strong>watching the client<\/strong>. Watch only the opponent, and you'll end up a copy of them. Watch the client, and you get to become the only version of yourself."},{"t":"p","html":"Still, it's useful to know the competition. Let me teach you how to use AI for a <strong>client-focused competitor analysis<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Step one: <strong>Collect information<\/strong>. Let AI scan competitor websites, content channels, social media, and job postings every day. You don't need to read it all yourself. Let AI summarize the key changes: new products launched, new case studies posted, new roles being hired. Get a weekly report."},{"t":"p","html":"Step two: <strong>Analyze client feedback<\/strong>. Let AI crawl client reviews of competitors across different platforms and analyze what people like and complain about. Wherever clients praise your competitors, that's where you need to improve. Wherever they complain, that's exactly where you can strike."},{"t":"p","html":"Step three: <strong>Generate a comparison strategy<\/strong>. When clients use a competitor to pressure you on price, don't panic. Let AI use what you know about the client to build a <strong>Differentiation Comparison<\/strong>. Don't just list specs. Instead, say something like:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Mr. Ryan, you mentioned Competitor A is cheaper. That's true. But our clients tell us Competitor A runs into issues with Y in X scenarios. Our solution has a unique edge in Z, which is exactly what you care about. Want to run a test?"},{"t":"d","who":"Ethan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So the point of this comparison isn't to show \"we're better.\" It's to show \"we're a better fit for you.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly! AI helps you find that fit. You're responsible for making the client believe this point matters to them."},{"t":"ms","items":["Competitor analysis core: not \"how they perform,\" but <strong>why the client chose them<\/strong>.","Three things AI does: <strong>collect information<\/strong>, <strong>analyze reviews<\/strong>, and <strong>generate comparisons<\/strong>.","Strategy: not \"we are better,\" but <strong>\"we are a better fit for you.\"<\/strong>","Goal: turn a <strong>price war<\/strong> into a <strong>value war<\/strong>."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":22,"title":"I keep missing my sales targets. How can AI help me break them down?","part":2,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Lina","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I set goals every month, but I never hit them. It's not that I'm not trying hard, I just don't know how to try in the right direction. The goal feels too big to break down."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"If I gave you 100 pounds of rice and told you to eat it all in one day, what would you do?"},{"t":"d","who":"Lina","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"That's impossible. I'd have to split it into a bunch of meals."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Goals work the same way. A million-dollar target isn't \"I need to hit a million.\" It's \"I need X Type A clients, Y Type B clients, and Z new leads.\" AI can automate that breakdown for you."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me teach you the <strong>Four-Step Goal Breakdown Method<\/strong> using AI:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Break down the goal.<\/strong> Give AI your past data: out of your last 100 leads, how many turned into Type A clients? How many Type A clients led to a sale? What's your average deal size? Let AI calculate exactly how many leads and Type A clients you need to hit a million."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Spread it across the week.<\/strong> Have AI divide those leads and client needs across your work days. For example: this week you need 20 new leads, and you need to move 5 Type B clients up to Type A. AI will also tell you how many calls and emails that means per day."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Build a daily checklist.<\/strong> Ask AI to turn \"what you need to do each day\" into an actual list. Not \"make more calls,\" but \"at 3:00 PM today, call Mr. Zhang and follow up on the case study you sent last week.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Adjust as you go.<\/strong> Every week, feed AI your real numbers. It'll compare them to your target and tell you if you're falling behind and what you need to do more of next week."},{"t":"d","who":"Lina","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Now I actually know what I'm supposed to do every day."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly! A goal isn't something you stare at from far away, it's something you see one step at a time, right under your feet. AI turns \"the distance ahead\" into \"the step in front of you.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["Missing your target usually isn't about lack of effort. It's about never breaking it down to \"<strong>which call to make at 3 PM today<\/strong>.\"","AI's job is to turn \"<strong>$1 million in sales<\/strong>\" into \"<strong>20 calls plus 5 follow-ups a day<\/strong>.\" Your job is to execute and report back.","The new basic skill in sales: shift from <strong>carrying a target<\/strong> to <strong>breaking down a target<\/strong>, until every step is clear, doable, and adjustable."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":23,"title":"How can I use AI to design a sales incentive plan?","part":2,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Leo","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, designing team incentives is so tough. Raise the payout and the company can't afford it. Lower it and the team loses motivation. Is there a practical way to do this?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Ever heard of gamification? Good games get players to pour in time and energy without expecting anything back. Why do you think that happens?"},{"t":"d","who":"Leo","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Because there's instant feedback, a sense of achievement, and social recognition."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly! The core of motivation isn't money, it's <strong>being seen<\/strong>. AI can help you build an incentive system where everyone feels seen."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me teach you how to design a <strong>personalized incentive plan<\/strong> using AI:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Figure out what each person actually wants.<\/strong> Let AI analyze each salesperson's behavior data: who cares more about money, who cares more about recognition, who cares more about growth. Based on their past performance and communication history, AI builds an <strong>incentive preference profile<\/strong> for each person."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Design multiple reward tracks.<\/strong> Have AI set up incentives across different categories: top performer (<strong>Results Award<\/strong>), fastest improvement (<strong>Growth Award<\/strong>), most positive customer feedback (<strong>Reputation Award<\/strong>), and best newcomer (<strong>Potential Award<\/strong>). This way, almost everyone has a shot at being seen."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Build an instant feedback system.<\/strong> Have AI design a <strong>points system<\/strong>. Every time someone hits a small goal, like making 50 calls in a day, they earn points automatically and see their ranking update right away, just like a game."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Keep optimizing.<\/strong> Every month, have AI review how the incentives are working. Which ones are actually driving behavior? Who isn't responding no matter what you offer? Adjust the plan based on what you find."},{"t":"d","who":"Leo","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So it's not really about how much money you hand out, it's about making sure everyone feels valued."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly! AI lets you deliver <strong>personalized incentives for everyone<\/strong>, instead of just one flat commission rate for the whole team."},{"t":"ms","items":["The core of any incentive plan: it's not about money, it's about <strong>being seen<\/strong>.","AI's four-step process: <strong>analyze preferences → design multiple reward tracks → give instant feedback → keep optimizing<\/strong>.","The result: everyone gets a chance to <strong>feel seen<\/strong>.","The goal: make salespeople as into their work as they are into a game."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":24,"title":"Sales meetings take too long. Can AI replace them?","part":2,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, we have a weekly meeting every Monday that runs half a day, and people just repeat the same things over and over. Can AI replace it?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Do you want AI to <strong>replace<\/strong> the meeting, or do you want to <strong>make the meeting more efficient<\/strong>?"},{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"More efficient, of course."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Good. Let me design an <strong>AI-powered meeting efficiency plan<\/strong> for you."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: AI pre-meeting preparation.<\/strong> Before the meeting, have AI pull everyone's weekly reports and data into a <strong>briefing<\/strong> covering just three things: progress on last week's goals, key tasks for this week, and issues that need discussion. Everyone reads it in five minutes before the meeting starts, so you're not stuck listening to reports for half an hour."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: AI support during the meeting.<\/strong> While the meeting's running, let AI record and summarize key points in real time. If someone drifts off-topic, it flags this automatically: \"This discussion has been off-topic for 10 minutes, recommend returning to the issue at hand.\" If the group gets stuck, AI can suggest a fix based on historical data: \"A similar situation was solved this way before. Want to consider it?\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: AI follow-up after the meeting.<\/strong> Afterward, AI automatically generates the meeting minutes and turns them into <strong>to-do lists<\/strong> for everyone. The next day, it follows up: \"You promised to call Mr. Zhang yesterday at the meeting. You haven't done that yet.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So the meeting goes from <strong>information updates<\/strong> to <strong>problem-solving<\/strong>."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Right! AI handles the information updates, and you focus on solving the hard problems. Face-to-face time is still necessary, but AI frees it up for the things <strong>only humans can do<\/strong>, like boosting morale, working through complex problems, and building trust."},{"t":"ms","items":["AI does not <strong>replace<\/strong> meetings, it makes them <strong>more efficient<\/strong>","<strong>Three-step method:<\/strong> prepare a briefing beforehand, assist the discussion during, follow up afterward","Result: shift from <strong>information sharing<\/strong> to <strong>problem-solving<\/strong>","Goal: spend face-to-face time on things <strong>only humans can do<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":25,"title":"How do I use AI to run a sales review?","part":2,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, we do a review every month, but it feels like a formality. Everyone reports numbers, mentions problems, and next month looks exactly the same. How do we make these reviews actually useful?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Are you reviewing the <strong>data<\/strong>, or are you reviewing the <strong>decisions<\/strong>?"},{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"The data. Things like how many deals we closed and the total amount."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Reviewing data only tells you <strong>what happened<\/strong>. Reviewing decisions helps you understand <strong>why it happened<\/strong> and <strong>what to do next<\/strong>. AI can help you upgrade from a <strong>data review<\/strong> to a <strong>decision review<\/strong>. Let me teach you the AI-powered <strong>three-step deep review method<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: AI automatically generates a data report.<\/strong> Have AI turn your sales data into a <strong>heat map<\/strong>: which stage has the lowest conversion rate, which customer type closes fastest, which time of day is most efficient. It's clear at a glance, no manual counting required."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: AI analyzes the decision points.<\/strong> Have AI compare closed deals against failed ones to find the <strong>key differences<\/strong>. What different decisions did the salesperson make at each step? What did they say differently? What strategy did they use? AI turns this into a <strong>success decision list<\/strong> and a <strong>failure decision list<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: AI generates an improvement plan.<\/strong> For every item on the failure list, ask AI for specific advice. For example: \"When a client says 'I'll think about it,' you choose to wait 70% of the time. Top performers instead ask about their concerns 90% of the time. Next time, try this script...\""},{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"This actually makes the review worth having."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly! AI <strong>finds the patterns<\/strong>. You <strong>verify them<\/strong> and <strong>build new methods<\/strong> from there. That's the real point of a review."},{"t":"ms","items":["The core of a review isn't <strong>looking at data<\/strong>, it's <strong>finding patterns<\/strong>","<strong>AI three-step method:<\/strong> generate heat maps, analyze decision points, propose improvement plans","Review meeting focus: discuss AI insights and share validation experiences","Goal: turn every review into a <strong>team upgrade<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":26,"title":"How to build a sales script library? An AI-driven dynamic update mechanism","part":2,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Ryan","role":"Sales Director","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, we have a sales script library, but nobody uses it. It's too outdated, the questions clients actually ask aren't even in there. How do we build a \"living\" script library?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Are you building a <strong>library<\/strong>, or a <strong>Wikipedia<\/strong>?"},{"t":"d","who":"Ryan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"What's the difference?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Books in a library are static, they sit unchanged for years. Entries on Wikipedia are alive, people edit them constantly. Your script library needs to work like Wikipedia, with AI as the <strong>automatic editor<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me teach you how to use AI to build an <strong>auto-updating script library<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Initial input.<\/strong> Feed all your existing scripts, cases, and FAQs to the AI to build a <strong>base library<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Real-time capture.<\/strong> Let AI scan every sales chat and call recording daily, looking for <strong>new questions<\/strong>. If three clients ask something today that's not in the library, AI automatically tags it as a <strong>new high-frequency question<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Automatic generation.<\/strong> For that new question, AI pulls from historical success cases and product info to generate <strong>three responses in different styles<\/strong>, then pushes them to the team: \"This new question has been showing up a lot. We suggest these scripts, please test them and share feedback.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Feedback and optimization.<\/strong> Once salespeople use these scripts, they feed the client reactions back to AI. It <strong>increases the weight<\/strong> of scripts that work, and <strong>optimizes or drops<\/strong> the ones that don't."},{"t":"d","who":"Ryan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So the script library is always updating?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Yes! A script library isn't something you build once and use for a year. It <strong>evolves every day<\/strong>, and the more salespeople use it, the smarter it gets."},{"t":"p","html":"One of our clients used this method. Their script library usage rate went from <strong>20% to 90%<\/strong>. A salesperson told me, \"I use it because I know that if I ask a new question today, the answer will be in the library by tomorrow.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["A script library is not a <strong>library<\/strong>, it is a <strong>Wikipedia<\/strong>","<strong>AI four-step method:<\/strong> initial input, real-time capture, automatic generation, feedback optimization","Result: the script library <strong>evolves every day<\/strong>","Goal: make salespeople <strong>want to use it<\/strong> and <strong>rely on it<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":27,"title":"How to Use AI to Filter High-Intent Clients","part":2,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Ethan","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, we get tons of inquiries every day, but most people just ask for the price and never follow up. How do we quickly tell who actually wants to buy?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"When you go on a blind date, how do you tell if the other person is serious about dating you?"},{"t":"d","who":"Ethan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"It depends on what they ask. If they just ask, \"Do you own a house?\" they're probably just making small talk. But if they ask, \"What are your hobbies?\" they probably want to actually get to know me."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly! Clients work the same way. The questions they ask and how they act both reveal their <strong>level of interest<\/strong>. AI can help you catch those signals."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me teach you how to build an <strong>intent scoring system<\/strong> with AI."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Define \"high-intent behaviors.\"<\/strong> Have AI study your past closed deals and find the behaviors clients showed before buying. For example: asking about price more than three times, requesting a meeting, comparing you to competitors, or checking your materials late at night. These are all <strong>high-intent signals<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Set up scoring rules.<\/strong> Let AI assign points to each behavior. A price question is worth <strong>+5 points<\/strong>, a meeting request <strong>+20<\/strong>, mentioning a competitor <strong>+10<\/strong>, a late-night product review <strong>+15<\/strong>. Total score out of <strong>100<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Monitor scores in real time.<\/strong> When a new lead comes in, AI automatically scans all their actions and keeps updating their <strong>intent score<\/strong>. Once it passes <strong>80 points<\/strong>, AI alerts you: \"Client Morgan has hit 85 points. Suggest following up today.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Generate follow-up advice.<\/strong> AI also tells you why the score is high, what the client cares about most, and how you should approach them. For example: \"This client asked about price repeatedly and browsed the product page late at night. Focus on value for money. Here's a suggested script.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Ethan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So I should just focus on the leads scoring above 80?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Right! Only chase the ones above <strong>80 points<\/strong>. Let AI automatically nurture the ones between <strong>60 and 80<\/strong>, and leave anything below 60 alone for now. Spend <strong>80 percent of your time on the top 20 percent of high-intent clients<\/strong>."},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>High-intent clients<\/strong> aren't \"felt,\" they're <strong>identified through signals<\/strong>","The <strong>AI four-step method<\/strong>: define signals → set rules → monitor in real time → generate advice","Result: <strong>80 percent of your time<\/strong> goes to the <strong>top 20 percent<\/strong> of clients","Goal: go from \"searching for a needle in a haystack\" to <strong>precision fishing<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":28,"title":"Client Churn Is Rising, How Can AI Give Early Warning?","part":2,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Leo","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, we're losing more and more longtime clients, and by the time we notice, they're already gone. Is there a way to know in advance who's about to leave?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Have you heard of marriage counseling? A good counselor doesn't wait until a couple is about to divorce to step in. They pick up on small clues in everyday interactions and raise a warning early."},{"t":"d","who":"Leo","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Can AI actually catch clues that subtle?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"It can, and it catches them even earlier than a person would."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me teach you how to build a <strong>client churn warning system<\/strong> with AI."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Define \"warning signs.\"<\/strong> Have AI study clients who've already left and find the behaviors they had in common right before leaving. For example: checking messages less often, shorter support calls, more complaints, or a change in the main contact person. These are all <strong>warning signals<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Set a warning threshold.<\/strong> Let AI assign points to each signal. Once the total score passes a set number, it triggers an alert. For example: no messages checked in three months <strong>(+20 points)<\/strong>, a recent complaint <strong>(+30 points)<\/strong>, a contact person change <strong>(+40 points)<\/strong>. A total of <strong>80 or above<\/strong> means a <strong>red alert<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Automatic alerts plus advice.<\/strong> When a client gets close to the threshold, AI automatically notifies the sales rep: \"Client Casey has a 75 percent churn risk. Recommend a deep follow-up visit this week. Based on past data, this client cares most about support response time, focus on that.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Track how well the fix works.<\/strong> After the rep takes action, AI keeps watching the client's behavior to see if things improve. If they do (say, the client starts checking messages again), the risk score drops. If not, the alert level goes up."},{"t":"d","who":"Leo","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So we can pull them back before they actually leave?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly! The point of a churn warning isn't to explain things after the client is already gone, it's to <strong>step in before that happens<\/strong>. AI helps you catch that window while there's still time to fix things."},{"t":"ms","items":["The core idea of churn warnings: don't wait until the client leaves to figure out why, <strong>pull them back before they go<\/strong>","The <strong>AI four-step method<\/strong>: define warning signs → set thresholds → alert plus advice → track results","Result: go from \"explaining after the fact\" to <strong>stepping in beforehand<\/strong>","Goal: keeping old clients is the same as <strong>keeping your profits<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":29,"title":"How do I use AI for customer segmentation?","part":2,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Owen","role":"Operations Director","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, we have hundreds of thousands of customers, but we treat them all the same way, mass messages, mass coupons. The results keep getting worse. How can I use AI to run more precise, segmented operations?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Have you ever been to a department store? Do they treat customers at the luxury counter the same way they treat shoppers in the discount aisle?"},{"t":"d","who":"Owen","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Of course not. The luxury counter gets one-on-one service, the discount aisle is self-service."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Customers work the same way. Different value levels need different treatment. AI helps you deliver that kind of <strong>personalized service at scale<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me teach you how to build a <strong>customer segmentation system<\/strong> with AI:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Automatic segmentation.<\/strong> Have AI sort your customers by purchase history, engagement, and lifecycle stage into groups like high-value active, high-value dormant, mid-value active, low-value new, and at-risk of churning. AI will tell you how many people are in each group and what makes them different."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Design tier strategies.<\/strong> For each group, have AI generate a different approach:"},{"t":"ul","items":["<strong>High-value active:<\/strong> One-on-one service, birthday gifts, early access to new products","<strong>High-value dormant:<\/strong> AI sends automated \"wake-up\" content, tracks how customers respond, and hands off to a human once interest shows up","<strong>Mid-value active:<\/strong> AI pushes relevant product recommendations to encourage upgrades","<strong>Low-value new:<\/strong> AI guides them toward core products to build trust quickly","<strong>At-risk:<\/strong> AI watches for warning signs and triggers a recovery process"]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Automatic execution.<\/strong> Hand the strategies to AI and let it run them. For example, it can send personalized recommendations to mid-value active customers every day, or send a wake-up article to dormant high-value customers every week."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Analyze and optimize.<\/strong> Once a month, have AI review conversion results for each tier. Which tier's conversion rate is dropping? Which tier's budget isn't being spent well? Let AI suggest fixes."},{"t":"d","who":"Owen","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So I don't have to manage hundreds of thousands of customers one by one, I just manage a handful of strategies?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. AI turns your strategy into automated action."},{"t":"ms","items":["Core idea of segmentation: <strong>different value, different treatment<\/strong>","The <strong>four-step AI method<\/strong>: automatic segmentation -&gt; design strategy -&gt; automatic execution -&gt; optimize","Result: moving from <strong>mass messaging<\/strong> to <strong>precise service<\/strong>","Goal: make high-value customers feel <strong>valued<\/strong>, and guide everyday customers along the way"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":30,"title":"Sales and traffic teams keep fighting. Can AI fix this?","part":2,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Chris","role":"Entrepreneur","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, my sales team and my traffic team fight every single day. Traffic says, \"We're giving you plenty of leads.\" Sales says, \"The lead quality is terrible.\" How do I solve this?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Where do you think the real problem is?"},{"t":"d","who":"Chris","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"I think their goals are just different. Traffic cares about <strong>lead volume<\/strong>, sales cares about <strong>closed deals<\/strong>."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. When the goals don't match, fighting is inevitable. AI can help align them. Let me show you how to build a <strong>traffic-sales synergy system<\/strong> with AI:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Speak the same language.<\/strong> Have AI analyze historical data to define what actually counts as a <strong>high-quality lead<\/strong>. It's not up to traffic, and it's not up to sales, it's up to the data. AI will show you the three traits shared by customers who actually closed in the past. From now on, that's your standard for a quality lead."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Build a two-way feedback loop.<\/strong> After sales follows up on a lead, they report back to AI: did it close? If not, why not? AI collects and analyzes this automatically, then sends a <strong>lead quality report<\/strong> back to the traffic team. That way, traffic knows which channels are producing the best leads and which customer profiles are the most accurate."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Set shared KPIs.<\/strong> Have AI design a set of <strong>shared metrics<\/strong>, like lead-to-close conversion rate or the number of high-value leads. Tie the traffic team's bonus to sales results, and tie the sales team's performance to lead quality feedback. That way both sides want the same thing."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Automatic lead distribution.<\/strong> Let AI assign leads based on customer traits and each salesperson's strengths. A salesperson who's great with B2B won't get handed consumer leads, and someone who's good at big-ticket deals won't get low-value leads. This way, good leads never get wasted."},{"t":"d","who":"Chris","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So traffic and sales aren't stuck in an upstream-downstream relationship anymore. They're more like a left hand and a right hand."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. AI is what keeps the two hands working together."},{"t":"ms","items":["Root cause of the fighting between traffic and sales: <strong>misaligned goals<\/strong>","The <strong>four-step AI synergy system<\/strong>: unify the standard -&gt; two-way feedback -&gt; shared KPIs -&gt; automatic distribution","Result: moving from <strong>blaming each other<\/strong> to <strong>sharing responsibility<\/strong>","Goal: traffic owns the <strong>percentage of high-quality leads<\/strong>, sales owns the <strong>lead-to-close conversion rate<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":31,"title":"How can I use AI to write cold emails that double my response rate?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I send out dozens of prospecting emails every day, but my response rate is under 1 percent. It feels like they just vanish into thin air. Can AI help boost that?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"What do your emails look like right now?"},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Just the standard template: \"Dear Mr. X, hello! I'm a sales rep from XX Company. We focus on... and I hope we can find an opportunity to work together...\""},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Clients get dozens of emails like that every single day. They delete them on sight. AI isn't there to help you write a \"nicer template,\" it's there to help you write something that doesn't feel like a template at all."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's a <strong>four-step method<\/strong> to boost your reply rate using AI:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Have AI analyze the target client.<\/strong> Feed it public info about the client, their website, founder interviews, recent news, and use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Analyze this company's activity over the last three months. Identify the three business pain points they're most likely facing. List them in plain, conversational language."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Have AI generate a personalized hook.<\/strong> Based on those pain points, use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Write an opening line, no more than 20 words, tied to the client's specific situation, so they immediately feel like 'this was written for me.' Keep the tone like a greeting between friends."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI write the main body.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Based on the pain points and opening line above, write an email of about 300 words. It should include: an understanding of the client's pain points, how we've helped similar clients solve them, a brief case study, and one low-pressure next step, like a 15-minute call. Keep the tone genuine and professional, no empty phrases."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Fine-tune by hand, then let AI polish the subject line.<\/strong> Read it yourself and adjust it to sound like you. Then have AI generate 10 subject line options and pick the one that feels most natural."},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"If every email is different, won't that slow me down a lot?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"You can still do this in batches. Say you want to reach 20 companies in the same industry today. First, have AI create a \"common industry pain point\" version. Then, for each company, fine-tune it using the analysis from step one. AI can even automate that fine-tuning part, you just type in the company name, and it pulls the analysis and generates a customized version."},{"t":"p","html":"One of our students used this method and saw their reply rate jump from 0.8 percent to 7.3 percent. The secret is simple: make the client feel like \"this email was written just for me.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["The core of a good cold email isn't \"looking polished,\" it's <strong>feeling personal<\/strong>","<strong>AI four-step method:<\/strong> analyze pain points, generate a \"hook,\" write the body, optimize the title","<strong>Batch approach:<\/strong> industry template plus AI fine-tuning","Goal: get the client to decide <strong>within 3 seconds<\/strong> that your email is worth replying to"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":32,"title":"When a client says \"not interested,\" how can AI help me find a way in?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"B","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I call a client, and the second I say my company name, they say \"not interested\" and hang up. I don't even get a chance to mention the product. How do I break through this?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"When a client says \"not interested,\" do they really not need it, or do they just not want to talk to you?"},{"t":"d","who":"B","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Probably the second one. I hadn't even said anything about the product yet."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. What they're rejecting isn't your product, it's the lack of <strong>a reason to keep talking<\/strong>. AI can help you find that reason."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's an <strong>AI three-step icebreaker method<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Do your homework beforehand.<\/strong> Before you call, have AI spend 30 seconds researching. Input the company name and any personal info you have, like LinkedIn, and use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Find three topics this client is likely paying attention to right now: 1. Something tied to recent company news; 2. A hot topic in their professional field; 3. An angle that could build rapport, like a shared alma mater or mutual connection."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Design the opening line.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Based on the info above, design an opening line under 15 seconds long. It should lead naturally into a conversation, not sound like a pitch. For example: 'I saw you all have been making moves in XX area recently, and I actually have an observation about XX I'd love to share...'"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Rehearse your response.<\/strong> If the client says \"not interested,\" use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"After the client says 'not interested,' generate three different responses: A. A sincere request for advice; B. A value teaser; C. A light, easy deflection. Keep them short and natural."},{"t":"d","who":"B","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So this way, I'm already prepared before I even pick up the phone."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"We had a student use this method to call a CEO. His opening line was: \"Mr. Zhang, I saw your company just closed a Series B round. I've been helping a few similar companies with growth, and there's some data you might find interesting...\" The client replied, \"Oh? Go on.\" That call ended up lasting 15 minutes."},{"t":"ms","items":["\"Not interested\" isn't the end, it just means <strong>you haven't found the right topic yet<\/strong>","<strong>AI icebreaker in three steps:<\/strong> research first, design the opening, rehearse the response","The key is giving the client <strong>a reason that's relevant to them<\/strong>","Goal: turn a client who wants to hang up into one who says, \"tell me more\""]}],"minutes":3},{"n":33,"title":"How Can I Use AI to Analyze a Client's Social Feed and Find Conversation Topics?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I added a client on a messaging app, but I don't know what to say. Their social feed looks pretty active, but I can't find a way in. Can AI help me figure this out?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Of course. A social feed is a window into someone's real life. It's full of conversation clues. AI can help you decode them."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you an <strong>AI Social Feed Analysis Method<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Extract the info.<\/strong> Gather the client's social feed content from the last three months (text, photos, shared links). If there are a lot of photos, use an AI image recognition tool to pull out keywords."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Let AI analyze their interests.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please analyze the following social feed content. List this person's interest tags, areas of focus, and frequent topics. Also guess their personality traits (for example: logical vs. emotional, career-focused vs. lifestyle-focused). Finally, suggest 3 topics that would work best for starting a conversation."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Generate a natural opening.<\/strong> Pick an angle and use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I want to reach out to a client based on something they shared about xx. Please generate 3 different styles of opening messages: A. Asking for their opinion; B. Showing empathy; C. Light and playful. Keep it natural, not too forced."},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Say he shared an industry article. What should I say?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"AI might generate something like:"},{"t":"ul","items":["<strong>Asking for opinion:<\/strong> \"Ryan, I saw the article you shared. The point about xx was really insightful. What do you think this means for our industry?\"","<strong>Empathy:<\/strong> \"I just finished reading the article you recommended. It really hit home. We've actually been discussing this same issue lately. I'd love to hear your thoughts sometime.\"","<strong>Playful:<\/strong> \"Ryan, are you turning into an industry analyst? Every post you share is so hardcore!\""]},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"That way it won't feel so awkward."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. The key is being genuinely interested in them, not just pretending to be. AI just helps you find the real point of connection."},{"t":"ms","items":["A social feed is a client's <strong>life map<\/strong>, and AI helps you navigate it","<strong>Three-step method:<\/strong> extract content, analyze tags, generate an opening","Rule for finding an angle: be <strong>sincere, specific, and relatable<\/strong>","Goal: make the client feel like <strong>\"this person gets me\"<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":34,"title":"Before a Cold Visit, How Can I Use AI to Build a Client Profile in 3 Minutes?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I often have to do cold visits, but before each meeting all I have is a company name and a person's name. There's no time for real research. Is there a faster way to do this?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Three minutes is enough time for AI to sketch out a client profile for you. The key is asking the right questions."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you an <strong>AI Lightning Profile<\/strong> prompt template:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Gather basic info.<\/strong> Type in the company name and contact name you have, and let AI search for public information first. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please quickly summarize the following: basic info on [Company Name] (main business, size, recent news), and the position and background of [Contact Name] if any public info exists. Time is tight, just give me the key points."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Predict deeper needs.<\/strong> Based on the basic info, use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Based on the information above, guess 3 business challenges this company might be facing, and 2 career-related concerns this contact might have personally. Factor in common industry patterns."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Build a communication strategy.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please create a short 15-minute meeting strategy: an opening icebreaker (based on company news or personal background), 1 to 2 core value points that match their pain points, possible objections and how to respond, and a suggested next step."},{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So I could actually do this on the subway?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Yes. One of our students ran this in the car on the way to a meeting and found out the client's company had just launched a new product. He walked in and opened with: \"I heard you just launched xx product. I actually looked into it and had a few ideas I wanted to run by you...\" The client's eyes lit up. What was supposed to be a 15-minute meeting turned into an hour."},{"t":"ms","items":["A successful cold visit is <strong>50% preparation, 50% improvisation<\/strong>","<strong>AI Lightning Profile<\/strong> in three steps: search basics, predict pain points, set strategy","Time needed: <strong>3 minutes<\/strong>, can be done on your commute","Goal: make the client feel like <strong>you're not a stranger<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":35,"title":"I've Got a Pile of Business Cards From a Trade Show. How Can AI Help Me Follow Up Fast?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, every time I come back from a trade show I have a stack of business cards, but I don't know who to reach out to first or how. A few days go by and I just forget about them. Can AI help with this?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Trade show cards are <strong>gold leads<\/strong>, but handled badly, they're just scrap paper. AI can help you sort and follow up fast."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you an <strong>AI Trade Show Follow-up System<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Enter the info.<\/strong> Use an OCR tool to turn the cards into a spreadsheet, name, company, title, phone, email. Plenty of AI tools now (like scanning apps) can export this directly for you."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Let AI rank the leads.<\/strong> Have AI score each lead based on job title and company size: C-level decision makers (Class A), department heads (Class B), regular staff (Class C), and incomplete info (Class D). Also flag any leads that closely match your ideal client profile."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Generate personalized follow-up emails in bulk.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I have 50 trade show leads: 10 Class A, 20 Class B, and 20 Class C. Please write 10 highly personalized follow-up emails for the Class A leads (use what we talked about at the show if I have notes, otherwise base it on their company background). For Class B, create one general template I can tweak. For Class C, write a short, simple version. Make the subject lines catchy."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Set up AI follow-up reminders.<\/strong> Log the email send times and expected reply windows into an AI calendar. If a client hasn't replied in 2 days, have AI remind you to switch channels, like adding them on a messaging app or calling."},{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So I don't have to think through each one myself."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students used this system after a trade show. He followed up with 200 leads in 3 days and landed 12 meetings with interested clients. He told me: \"Before, the show would end and that was it, nothing happened after. Now, the real work starts once the show ends.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["The key to trade show leads: <strong>fast, accurate, personalized<\/strong>","<strong>AI Follow-up System:<\/strong> digitize, rank, personalize in bulk, smart reminders","The <strong>golden 72 hours<\/strong>: your first round of follow-up must happen within 3 days","Goal: make <strong>every single card count<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":36,"title":"How do I use AI to find a customer's \"pain point keywords\"?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I feel like whenever I talk about my product's selling points, the customer just doesn't care. How do I find the pain point keywords they actually care about?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Pain points aren't something you guess at. You have to dig them out. AI can help you pull high-frequency <strong>keywords<\/strong> out of huge piles of data. Let me give you the \"<strong>AI Pain Point Mining Method<\/strong>,\" three steps:"},{"t":"p","html":"Step one: <strong>Analyze public industry data<\/strong>. Find the forums, communities, and Q&amp;A platforms where your target customers spend time (like Zhihu, Baidu Tieba, or industry-specific forums). Have AI scrape the most-upvoted answers and most common questions. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please analyze these 100 user questions and answers about the [industry name]. Pull out the 20 most frequent pain point keywords and rank them by how often they show up."},{"t":"p","html":"Step two: <strong>Analyze competitor reviews<\/strong>. Have AI scrape customer reviews for your competitors from shopping sites and social media. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please analyze the customer reviews for competitor [name]. Find the top 5 things customers complain about and the top 5 things they're happiest with. Pull out keywords using the customers' own words."},{"t":"p","html":"Step three: <strong>Analyze your internal service records<\/strong>. Feed AI your company's past support chats and records of deals that fell through. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please analyze these failed deals and find the top 3 concern keywords customers mention when they hesitate near the end. Then analyze the successful deals and find the top 3 keywords customers mention right before they decide to buy."},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So then I just plug these keywords into my sales pitch?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly! When you open with the exact words the customer's already thinking, they'll feel like you get them. Say you sell corporate training. Your pain point keywords might be \"employees checked out,\" \"training doesn't work,\" or \"too expensive.\" Build your pitch around those words."},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>Pain point keywords<\/strong> = the customer's inner voice","<strong>AI mining process<\/strong>: industry data → competitor reviews → internal records","Goal: make the customer feel like \"you're saying exactly what's bothering me\"","Use these keywords in your opening, questions, case studies, and proposals"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":37,"title":"A customer won't accept my friend request on WeChat. How do I use AI to break the ice?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I've sent this customer a WeChat friend request several times and they keep ignoring it. Is there any hope left?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"They're not accepting because your request message didn't grab them. You only get one line to make your case. AI can help you write a line they can't say no to. Here's the \"<strong>AI Friend Request Generator<\/strong>\":"},{"t":"p","html":"Step one: <strong>Find the hook<\/strong>. Have AI look at what's public about this person and find something that would catch their interest. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Customer [name], director at [company]. From the following info, find the best hook for a friend request: 1. an article they recently shared; 2. recent news about their company; 3. a standout point in their career background. Give me 3 different hook options."},{"t":"p","html":"Step two: <strong>Write the request message<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Based on this hook, write 3 friend request messages in different styles, each under 20 characters. Styles: A. professional inquiry; B. sharing value; C. casual connection. Keep it natural, not salesy."},{"t":"p","html":"Sample results:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Professional: \"Hi, I saw your post about [topic] and had a question for you.\"","Value: \"Hi, I put together some recent data on [topic] you follow. Thought you'd want it.\"","Casual: \"Hi, I felt the same way about what you said about [topic]. Mind connecting?\""]},{"t":"p","html":"Step three: <strong>A/B test it<\/strong>. If the first one doesn't work, try the second one two or three days later."},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"What if none of them work?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Then switch channels. Have AI write you a text message or a message for a professional networking app instead. Different channel, different message. One of our students used this and boosted their acceptance rate from <strong>20% to 65%<\/strong>. The key is making them feel that adding you actually benefits them."},{"t":"ms","items":["The core of a friend request: give them a reason they <strong>have to<\/strong> accept","<strong>AI's three steps<\/strong>: find the hook → write the message → A/B test","Rule: don't say who you are, say <strong>what's in it for them<\/strong>","Mix channels: if WeChat doesn't work, try text, professional networking apps, or email"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":38,"title":"A client's company just raised funding. How do I use AI to write a congratulations email that also introduces my business?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I saw a target client just announced a funding round and wanted to reach out. But my email came across too self-serving, like I was just chasing the news. How do I get the balance right?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Funding news is a great chance to break the ice. They just got money, which means they're about to start spending it. But your email has to feel genuine. It can't just be \"congrats, want to buy something?\""},{"t":"p","html":"Here's an \"<strong>AI Funding Congratulations Email<\/strong>\" template:"},{"t":"p","html":"Step one: <strong>Have AI write the congratulations message<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"The client company [name] just closed a Series B round led by [investor name]. Write a congratulations message, about 100 words, that's sincere and specific (mention what the funding will be used for, or a highlight about the investor). No generic phrases."},{"t":"p","html":"Step two: <strong>Lead naturally into your business<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"After the congratulations, I want to naturally bring up how my company (which does [business]) could help them. Based on what they might need as they grow after this funding, write 3 different value-based openings. These shouldn't sound like a sales pitch, they should sound like 'here's what you might need next.'"},{"t":"p","html":"Step three: <strong>Put together the full email<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Combine all of this into one complete email. Structure: sincere congratulations (2 sentences) + connection to value (2 to 3 sentences) + a low-pressure next step (like 'if it's convenient, I can send over some material for you to look at'). Keep the tone professional and polite."},{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"That way it won't feel like I'm just trying to sell something."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students used this method on a client that had just raised funding. The CEO personally replied: \"Thanks for the congrats, we're actually looking for a supplier in that space, let's set up a time to talk.\" That conversation turned into a major annual deal."},{"t":"ms","items":["Funding is a <strong>golden window<\/strong> for building a relationship, but you have to move the right way","<strong>Three parts of the AI email<\/strong>: sincere congratulations + connection to value + a low-pressure next step","The key: think from the angle of \"<strong>what will they need next<\/strong>,\" not \"come buy my stuff\"","Goal: make the client feel like you're there to help, not just showing up for a handout"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":39,"title":"How can I use AI to batch-generate sales scripts for different industries?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, our clients span so many industries, and every industry has different pain points. I end up rewriting my scripts every single time, and it's exhausting. Can AI batch-generate these for me?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Of course it can. AI is really good at \"template-based batch personalization.\" Let me give you an <strong>industry script generation system<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"Step 1: <strong>Build an industry pain point library.<\/strong> List out every industry you serve, and have AI generate a pain point analysis for each one. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Analyze the three most urgent business pain points for [Industry Name]. Sum up each pain point in one sentence, and phrase it the way the customer would actually say it. For example, use 'Our employees don't want to learn this' instead of 'Low training participation rate.'"},{"t":"p","html":"Step 2: <strong>Build a product value point library.<\/strong> Have AI translate your product features into value points that match each pain point. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Our product has the following features: [Feature List]. For the three pain points in [Industry Name], list one or two matching value points for each. Use language the customer can actually understand."},{"t":"p","html":"Step 3: <strong>Combine everything into a full script.<\/strong> For a specific industry, have AI generate the complete script. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Generate a full sales script for [Industry Name], including: a phone opening (15 seconds), a core value statement (1 minute), responses to three common objections, and one closing script. Base it on this industry's pain points and value points."},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So this covers every industry?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. And it's not just a one-time thing either. You can have AI refresh the industry pain points every quarter to keep everything current. One of our teams used this method and built a full script library covering 12 industries in just one week. Their new-hire training time went from three months down to one."},{"t":"ms","items":["The core of industry scripts isn't being \"<strong>generic<\/strong>,\" it's being \"<strong>adapted<\/strong>\"","<strong>Three-step AI method<\/strong>: pain point library → product value point library → combined generation","<strong>Update regularly<\/strong>: refresh industry insights every quarter","<strong>Goal<\/strong>: let your sales team speak confidently about any industry, right off the top of their head"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":40,"title":"How do I use AI to find the key decision-maker in a company?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I keep finding the wrong contact. I talk to someone for a long time before realizing they don't even have decision-making power. How can I use AI to find the real \"key person\"?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"In B2B sales, talking to the wrong person is the biggest waste of time there is. AI can help you draw out a <strong>decision chain map<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you an <strong>AI Key Person Identification Method<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"Step 1: <strong>Enter the company info.<\/strong> Type in the target company's name and have AI search for public org charts and executive lists. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Help me find the key decision-makers responsible for [purchasing/specific business area] at [Company Name]. List possible job titles, such as Procurement Director or Technical Director, along with any public information you can find. If the information is incomplete, suggest a way to track it down."},{"t":"p","html":"Step 2: <strong>Analyze related information.<\/strong> Have AI look through the company's job postings, press releases, and annual reports for clues about who the key person is. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Analyze this company's recent job postings. Which positions report directly to whom? Who's mentioned as the person in charge in their press releases? Who spoke about this business area at their annual meeting?"},{"t":"p","html":"Step 3: <strong>Build an outreach strategy.<\/strong> For each key person, have AI generate a personalized outreach strategy. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"For [Job Title A], what's the best way to reach out, phone, email, or social media? What should the opening focus on? For example, talk technical details with a Technical Director, but talk ROI with a Finance Director. Give me specific suggestions."},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So this helps me get past the gatekeepers?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"That's right. We had a student who wanted to get into a big company for a partnership deal, but kept ending up talking to junior staff. After using AI to map things out, he found that the real purchasing power actually sat with the Technical Director, who happened to be pretty active on a certain tech forum. He sent a private message there, and within a week, he had a meeting set up."},{"t":"ms","items":["Talking to the wrong person means <strong>100% wasted time<\/strong>","<strong>Three-step AI method<\/strong>: search the org structure → find the connections → set the strategy","<strong>Traits of a key person<\/strong>: has the budget, has the authority, has the pain point","<strong>Goal<\/strong>: say the right thing to the <strong>right person<\/strong>, right from your very first sentence"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":41,"title":"How can AI help me translate complex features into words customers actually understand?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, we sell SaaS software with dozens of features. By the time I finish explaining it to a client, I've talked myself dry, and they still look totally lost. How can I use AI to make complex features easy to understand?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Are you \"explaining the product,\" or are you \"translating the value\"?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Is there a difference?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"A big one. Explaining the product means saying \"I have this feature.\" Translating value means saying \"here's what this does for you.\" AI is amazing at doing exactly that kind of translation."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you the <strong>AI Value Translation Method<\/strong>, in three steps."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Turn features into scenes.<\/strong> List out the complex features that give you the most trouble, then use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please turn these technical features [list 3 to 5 features] into scenes that customers in 5 different industries would easily understand. Every sentence must start with 'This means you can...' For example, turn 'real-time data sync' into 'This means if you change a number in Shanghai, your coworker in Shenzhen sees it the second they look up.'"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Match features to pain points.<\/strong> For each feature, have AI find the exact words a customer would use to describe the pain point it solves. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please match each feature to the exact complaint a customer would most likely say. For example, 'your system is too slow' matches with: 'Our backend runs on X technology, response time is 0.1 seconds. Your report will be ready before your coffee even has time to cool down.'"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Simplify with everyday comparisons.<\/strong> Have AI come up with a simple, relatable comparison for each complex feature. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please come up with an everyday comparison that anyone could understand for these technical terms [list the terms]. For example, compare an 'API interface' to 'a restaurant menu. You just order (send a request), the kitchen (the system) cooks it, and the food (data) comes out. You don't need to know how it's made.'"},{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"That way the customer won't feel lost."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students sold data analysis software. She used to tell clients it had \"multi-dimensional data structures,\" and they'd just stare blankly. Once she used AI to translate it into \"it's like cutting a watermelon, you slice off whatever piece you want, as much as you want,\" the client got it right away and signed on the spot."},{"t":"ms","items":["The fatal mistake in selling complex products: you're speaking <strong>your language<\/strong>, but the customer is only listening for <strong>their problem<\/strong>","The <strong>AI translation process<\/strong>: turn features into scenes + match pain points + simplify with comparisons","The test: could a <strong>fifth grader<\/strong> understand it?","The goal: get the customer to say, <strong>\"Oh, so that's how it works!\"<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":42,"title":"When a customer says \"You're too expensive,\" how can AI help me respond?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, customers keep telling me, \"you're 30 percent more expensive than the competitor,\" and all I've got is \"our quality is better,\" which sounds weak. Can AI help me handle this better?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"When a customer says you're too expensive, they're doing the math in their head. Your job isn't to defend your price, it's to help them do a <strong>different set of math<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you the <strong>AI Price Math Method<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Have AI calculate the cost of not buying.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Our product is 30% more expensive than the competitor's, but we offer these 3 advantages: [list 3 core advantages]. Please help me calculate the hidden cost a customer would face if they picked the cheaper option and lost out on these 3 advantages. Use real numbers or specific scenarios, for example, 'spending 100 extra hours a year fixing errors by hand.'"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Have AI calculate the payback period.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Our product costs X, but it gives the customer these benefits: [list the benefits]. Please build me a simple 'payback period table' that tells the customer, in plain language, how much they save each month, how much they save each day, and how long it takes to earn back the difference."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI write response scripts.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please write 3 different styles of responses to a price objection: A. The Logical Approach (using numbers), B. The Emotional Approach (focusing on peace of mind), C. The Risk Approach (focusing on the dangers of going cheap). Keep it casual, like a normal conversation."},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Can you give me an example?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students does high-end consulting, and a client thought his price was too high. The script AI generated went like this: \"Mr. Wang, I get that price matters to you. But think about it this way, if you go with the cheaper option and something goes wrong during setup, your team could waste three months of work. That loss alone would be ten times the consulting fee. Yes, we're 30 percent more expensive, but we guarantee it gets done right the first time.\" The client went quiet for a moment, then said, \"You're right. Let's sign.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["\"Too expensive\" isn't a rejection, it's the customer saying <strong>\"give me one more reason\"<\/strong>","Three kinds of math AI can help with: <strong>the cost of not buying<\/strong>, <strong>the payback period<\/strong>, and <strong>the cost of risk<\/strong>","The key: help the customer do the math, don't <strong>defend yourself<\/strong>","The goal: make the customer feel that <strong>the cheap option is the riskier one<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":43,"title":"A competitor slashed prices. How do I use AI to write a comparison report for the client?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, a competitor suddenly dropped their price by 30%, and a few clients I'm working on are using this against me. How should I respond?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Price wars are the lowest form of competition. Your move isn't to \"follow\" them down, it's to \"rise above\" them. Let AI help you build a comparison report that wins the deal without ever fighting on price."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's my <strong>AI Elevation Comparison Method<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Have AI build an objective comparison table.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Our product [A] costs 30% more than competitor [B]. Please create an objective comparison table covering these areas: feature completeness, after-sales response speed, quality of case studies, long-term cost of use, and implementation risk. Rate each area on a 1 to 5 star scale, with a one-sentence explanation. Keep it fair and unbiased."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Have AI calculate the total cost of ownership.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please help me calculate a <strong>3-year total cost of ownership<\/strong>. Our product costs 30% more upfront, but it includes free upgrades, support, and training. The competitor charges extra for all of these. If the competitor's starting price is x, what's their real 3-year total cost once those fees are added? Write it out as a clear comparison."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI write a comparison letter.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Write an email to a client with the subject line: 'About the Product Comparison You Asked For.' Structure it like this: 1. Thank the client for being upfront with us. 2. Attach the objective comparison table, without putting down the competitor. 3. Point out two key differences that matter beyond price. 4. Invite the client to a <strong>15-minute value check<\/strong>, so they can see the difference for themselves. Keep the tone confident and easygoing."},{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Won't this make us look defensive?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Just the opposite. Being willing to compare head-to-head and let the data speak actually shows confidence. One of my students sent a message like this, and the client wrote back: \"You're the only salesperson I've ever met who's willing to list the competitor's strengths too. That kind of honesty is rare, let's set up a time to talk.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>Price wars are a dead end<\/strong>: You cut 30%, they cut 40%, and everyone loses in the end.","<strong>AI's three-step elevation<\/strong>: objective comparison table + total cost breakdown + value invitation.","<strong>Rule<\/strong>: Don't tear down the competitor, just build yourself up.","<strong>Goal<\/strong>: Get the client to stop comparing prices and start comparing value."]},{"t":"p","html":"---"}],"minutes":3},{"n":44,"title":"How do I use AI to turn a client case into a \"success story\"?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, we have client case studies too, but they read like manuals: \"Company X used our product and boosted efficiency by 20%.\" Clients read it and feel nothing. How do I make it more compelling?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"A case study isn't a \"data report,\" it's a story. A good story has a main character, conflict, a turning point, and an ending. AI can turn a dry case study into a story people actually want to read."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's my <strong>AI Five-Step Story Method<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Have AI pull out the conflict.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Here's our client case information: [paste case details]. Please identify the three most painful moments this client faced before buying our product. Write them in first person, like 'I stayed late until midnight every day just to sort through these reports.'"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Have AI describe the turning point.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please describe the client's mental journey when they first encountered our product, moving through three stages: doubt, trial, and surprise. Use specific details, like 'At the time I was frustrated, so I figured I'd just try it since it was free anyway.'"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI paint the ending.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please describe how the client's life changed after using the product. Use comparisons and details. For example, 'Now I leave the office right at 6 and get to have dinner with my kids.' Don't just give numbers, talk about real life."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI come up with a strong title.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please give me 10 different title options for this story, in these styles: suspense, numbers-driven, relatable, and unexpected contrast."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Have AI put together the full story.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please combine everything above into one complete case story, around 800 words. Structure: painful opening (hooks the reader) → turning point (feels believable) → surprising change (creates connection) → wrap-up with a call to action. Write it like a friend telling a story."},{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Can you give me an example?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of my students originally had this case: \"Company X saw a 25% boost in efficiency after using our product.\" AI rewrote it as: \"Mr. Zhang used to dread Monday meetings because he had to spend four hours pulling together last week's data. His wife said he looked miserable every weekend. After trying our product for just one week, he was shocked to find that by the time he'd finished his morning coffee on Monday, the report had already generated itself. Now his Monday meetings are the highlight of the department, because he always has fresh insights to share.\" The client read it and said, \"Wait, is this about me?\""},{"t":"ms","items":["A case study is a <strong>mirror<\/strong>, it lets the client picture their future self.","<strong>AI's five-step method<\/strong>: conflict + turning point + ending + title + full story.","<strong>Core idea<\/strong>: Don't write about the product, write about the person's change.","<strong>Goal<\/strong>: Get the client to say, \"This is literally me!\""]}],"minutes":3},{"n":45,"title":"A customer asked a question I couldn't answer. How do I use AI to get a quick answer?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, a customer asked me a technical question today and I had no clue what he meant. I froze on the spot. I hung up to look it up, but by the time I had an answer, the customer had already stopped replying. What should I do?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"A salesperson isn't an encyclopedia. You don't need to know everything, but you do need to be able to <strong>find anything<\/strong>. AI is your <strong>instant search engine<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you the <strong>AI Instant Response Method<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Steady the situation.<\/strong> You can say, \"That's a really specific question. Let me confirm the most accurate info for you. Can I get back to you in five minutes?\" Customers almost always say yes. Those five minutes are your AI time."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Ask fast.<\/strong> Open your AI tool and use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"A customer asked me a technical question: 'xxxx'. I'm in sales, not tech support. Give me an answer in three sentences I can repeat to the customer. First sentence: the core conclusion. Second sentence: a simple explanation. Third sentence: 'If you need more technical detail, our engineer can follow up.' Keep it conversational, not too technical."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Respond on the spot.<\/strong> Say the AI's answer in your own words, then add: \"This is what I can confirm right now. If you want more detailed technical info, I can have an engineer put together a report just for you.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Follow up.<\/strong> Use AI to write a follow-up email. Put the answer in writing and add: \"Feel free to reach out anytime if you have more questions.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Won't the customer think I'm not professional?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Just the opposite. Admitting you need to double-check something, then coming back with an accurate answer in five minutes, that's called being <strong>responsible<\/strong>. It's a hundred times more professional than someone who fakes knowing and rambles on. One of our students used this method and ended up giving a more accurate answer than a competitor. The customer told him, \"You didn't have the answer right away, but what you sent me five minutes later was solid. Way more trustworthy than people who just talk without thinking.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["A salesperson doesn't need to know everything, but must be able to <strong>find the answer<\/strong>","The <strong>AI Four-Step Method<\/strong>: Steady → Ask → Repeat → Follow up","The <strong>Golden Five Minutes<\/strong>: an answer right now beats an answer tomorrow by ten times","Goal: make the customer think, \"This person is reliable. They don't fake it when they don't know.\""]}],"minutes":3},{"n":46,"title":"How do I use AI to make my sales PPT clearer?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, my boss said my sales deck is \"logically messy,\" but I think it looks fine. How can AI help me fix it?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"The biggest trap with a sales deck is <strong>seeing it from your own point of view<\/strong>. You think it's good because you already know all the background. The customer thinks it's a mess because they know nothing. AI can help you shift to the <strong>customer's point of view<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you the <strong>AI PPT Optimization Method<\/strong>, in four steps:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Get AI to pull out the core message.<\/strong> Send your outline to AI with this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Here's my PPT outline: [paste outline]. In one sentence, tell me what this PPT is really trying to say to the customer."},{"t":"p","html":"If AI can't sum it up in one sentence, that means your main message isn't clear."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Get AI to run a customer's-eye test.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Pretend you're a customer seeing our company for the first time. After going through this deck, what questions would you have? List the top 3 to 5 things you'd want to ask."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Get AI to fix the logical structure.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Reorganize this deck's logic using the framework: <strong>Problem, Cause, Solution, Evidence, Action<\/strong>. Tell me what should go on each slide, and what to cut."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Get AI to write your talking points.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Write a script for each slide of the improved deck, no more than one minute per slide. Make it sound natural, with transitions and hooks, like 'Now that we've looked at the problem, let's see how to fix it.'"},{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Can you give me an example?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students had a deck that went: company intro, product features, technical strengths, client cases. AI reworked it into: What problem are you facing right now? (Slide 1) Why is this happening? (Slide 2) We've solved this exact problem for a company just like yours (Slide 3) Here's what our solution looks like (Slide 4) Why can we actually pull this off? (Slide 5) You can get there too (Slide 6) What's the next step? (Slide 7). After hearing it, the customer said, \"That's the clearest pitch I've ever heard.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["A PPT isn't a <strong>product manual<\/strong>, it's a <strong>map for your customer<\/strong>","<strong>AI Four-Step Method<\/strong>: pull out the core message + test from the customer's view + fix the structure + write the script","Success test: the customer can repeat <strong>3 key points<\/strong> after hearing it","Goal: make the customer feel like the deck was <strong>made just for them<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":47,"title":"When a client says \"let me think about it,\" how do I use AI to find their real concern?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, every time I finish talking with a client, they say \"let me think about it,\" and then I never hear from them again. How can I figure out what's actually going through their head?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"\"Let me think about it\" is the biggest black hole in sales. The client isn't really thinking, they just don't want to say no to your face. AI can help you shine a light into that black hole."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you the <strong>AI Concern-Mining Method<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Have AI analyze your conversation.<\/strong> Send your recent chat history to AI with this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please analyze this conversation and figure out what the client might be 'thinking about.' Consider these angles: 1. Price concerns, 2. Doubts about results, 3. Worries about risk, 4. Difficulty with internal decision-making. Give me 3 likely guesses, each backed by a piece of 'evidence' from the conversation."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Have AI write gentle follow-up questions.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Based on the 3 guesses above, write a gentle follow-up message for each one. Requirements: 1. It should feel caring, not like an interrogation. 2. Give the client an easy 'multiple choice' way to answer. 3. Lower their pressure. For example: 'Mr. Chang, are you worried the setup will take too long, or worried your team won't be able to use it well?'"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI design a strategy for silence.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"If the client stays silent even after the follow-up, design a 'retreat to advance' strategy. First give them an easy way out ('take your time'), then leave a low-pressure next step ('I'll send over some materials for you to look at'), and set a gentle reminder to follow up ('I'll check back next Wednesday to see if you have questions')."},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Won't that make me seem pushy?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"The trick is turning \"pressing them\" into \"thinking for them.\" One of our students had a client who kept saying \"let me think about it.\" After running the conversation through AI, he realized the client's real fear was looking bad in front of his boss if he made the wrong call. So he sent this: \"Mr. Wang, are you worried that if this doesn't work out, it'll be hard to explain to your boss? We could run a small test first, and only roll it out company-wide once it proves successful.\" The client replied instantly: \"How did you know? Let's do that!\""},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>\"Let me think about it\"<\/strong> really means \"I have a concern I don't want to say out loud.\"","<strong>The AI three-step method<\/strong>: analyze the concern, script the follow-up, handle the silence.","<strong>Key shift<\/strong>: Turn \"When will you decide?\" into \"What's worrying you?\"","<strong>Goal<\/strong>: Get the client to actually say, \"Honestly, what I'm afraid of is...\""]}],"minutes":3},{"n":48,"title":"How do I use AI to write loss-aversion scripts that make clients feel \"I'll lose out if I don't buy\"?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Ryan","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I've heard that fear of loss moves people more than the promise of gain, but my scripts always come out sounding stiff, like \"buy now or the price goes up.\" How do I actually do this well?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Cheap loss aversion is just scaring people. Real loss aversion is helping them see for themselves what they stand to lose. AI can help you build scripts that make the client scare themselves."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you the <strong>AI Loss Aversion Trio<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Part 1: Have AI calculate the \"sunk cost.\"<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"The client has talked with us X times already and understands our solution. Help me calculate: if they walk away now, how much time, energy, and opportunity cost have they already spent? Describe it in everyday language, like 'You've already spent 3 hours learning about us. If you spend another 3 hours checking out someone else, that's a whole week gone.'"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Part 2: Have AI calculate the \"missed gains.\"<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Help the client work out this math: if they act now, how much sooner can they start benefiting from our solution? What's that extra time worth? For example, 'If you start using this a month earlier, you can clear out that pile of annoying reports and skip 30 days of overtime.'"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Part 3: Have AI write a \"regret story.\"<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Tell a short story about a client who didn't choose us and later regretted it. Make it feel real, with specific details people can relate to. For example, 'Director Li also said he'd think about it, and then his competitor used our solution to steal two of his biggest accounts.'"},{"t":"d","who":"Ryan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Can I combine all three?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Definitely. One of our students sells training courses. Here's the AI-generated script he used: \"Mr. Wang, you've been looking into this for two weeks now. The longer you wait, the longer your team of dozens keeps working the old inefficient way, that's about 100,000 lost this week alone. Last week Director Li was also on the fence, and his competitor learned the new method and stole his clients.\" The client said, \"Say no more, I'm signing up.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>Real loss aversion<\/strong>: not about scaring people, it's about helping them see what they're about to lose.","<strong>The AI Trio<\/strong>: sunk cost + missed gains + regret story.","<strong>Key<\/strong>: Let the client do the math themselves on \"the cost of not buying.\"","<strong>Goal<\/strong>: Get the client to say, \"No, I can't afford to wait any longer.\""]}],"minutes":3},{"n":49,"title":"How do I use AI to create a \"Decision Matrix\" when a client is hesitant?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, a client is stuck between Option A and Option B and asked me to help him decide. I explained everything I could, but he still doesn't know what to choose. What should I do?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"A client hesitates when there are too many options but not enough <strong>decision criteria<\/strong>. AI can help him build a clear <strong>decision framework<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you an <strong>\"AI Decision Matrix Method\"<\/strong> in three steps:"},{"t":"p","html":"Step 1: Have AI list the <strong>decision dimensions<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"A client is torn between two options: Option A [describe A] and Option B [describe B]. Please list 5 decision dimensions the client is likely to care about, such as price, implementation time, risk, long-term return, and difficulty of execution. Explain in one sentence why each dimension matters."},{"t":"p","html":"Step 2: Have AI do the <strong>weighted scoring<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Have the client rate the importance of these 5 dimensions on a scale of 1 to 5 (for example, if price matters most, give it a 5). Then, based on what you know about the two options, score each option on each dimension from 1 to 5. Calculate the weighted total and give a suggested lean. Note: make clear this is just a reference based on the information given, the final call is his."},{"t":"p","html":"Step 3: Have AI generate the <strong>comparison table copy<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Turn the above into a simple, clear decision table. Make it easy to scan, using a table plus short notes. End with this line: 'This is just to help you clarify your thinking. In the end, it depends on what matters most to you.'"},{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Won't this make me look unprofessional?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Actually, the opposite. You're not making the decision for him, you're helping him <strong>see his own choice more clearly<\/strong>. One of our students used this method, and after the client looked at the table, he said, \"Actually, I realize I care more about long-term returns. I'll go with B. Thanks for helping me sort this out.\" Later, that client sent him three new referrals."},{"t":"ms","items":["A client's hesitation isn't about <strong>too many options<\/strong>, it's about <strong>unclear decision criteria<\/strong>","<strong>AI's three-step method<\/strong>: list dimensions, apply weighted scoring, generate the table","Principle: help him think, <strong>don't think for him<\/strong>","Goal: get the client to say, <strong>\"Thanks for helping me clarify this\"<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":50,"title":"How do I use AI on WeChat to reply in a way that's both professional and warm?","part":3,"section":"Customer Acquisition and Breaking the Ice","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I chat with dozens of clients on WeChat every day. Reply too fast, and it feels careless. Reply too slow, and clients get annoyed. If I use AI to help, I worry it'll sound too scripted. How do I find the balance?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"The key to WeChat sales is balancing <strong>speed<\/strong> and <strong>warmth<\/strong>. AI can help you be quick and warm at the same time."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you the <strong>\"AI WeChat Reply Sandwich Method\"<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"Step 1: Have AI build a <strong>reply library<\/strong>. For questions clients ask often, get AI to prepare different reply styles ahead of time. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Clients often ask this question: 'XXXX.' Please generate 3 different reply styles: A. Short and professional (for busy clients); B. Warm and caring (for clients who need reassurance); C. Light and humorous (for clients you're close with). Keep each reply under 50 words."},{"t":"p","html":"Step 2: Pick fast and <strong>fine-tune on the spot<\/strong>. When a message comes in, choose the best fit from your library, then add a <strong>personal touch<\/strong>, something like \"Mr. Zhang, about that issue you mentioned last time...\" or mention their name or something you talked about before."},{"t":"p","html":"Step 3: Have AI set <strong>follow-up reminders<\/strong>. After replying to an important client, set an AI reminder to check back in three days, or remind you before their birthday to send a message."},{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Can you give me an example?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"A client asks: \"Does your plan actually work?\""},{"t":"ul","items":["<strong>A, Professional:<\/strong> \"It does. We've worked with 30 companies in your industry, with an average 25 percent boost in efficiency. I can send you a case study.\"","<strong>B, Warm:<\/strong> \"I totally get why you'd ask that. Most of our clients had the same question at first, but they were happy once they tried it. Want me to connect you with a client in a similar situation?\"","<strong>C, Humorous:<\/strong> \"'Works' is putting it lightly, our clients call it a lifesaver. Just kidding, but it really has saved them a ton of time.\""]},{"t":"p","html":"See? Same question, different styles, but all of them still feel warm."},{"t":"ms","items":["The trap in WeChat sales: <strong>fast replies feel cold, slow replies lose efficiency<\/strong>","<strong>AI Sandwich Method<\/strong>: build a library ahead of time, pick quickly, add a personal touch","<strong>Three backup styles<\/strong>: professional, warm, humorous","Goal: make the client feel you're <strong>\"fast and thoughtful at the same time\"<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":51,"title":"How do I use AI to respond when a client says, \"Your reputation isn't great\"?","part":3,"section":"Handling Objections and Closing","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, today a client said, \"I heard from a friend that your after-sales service isn't good.\" I panicked and didn't know how to respond. How do I handle negative talk like this?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"When a client says your reputation isn't good, it's usually not a fact. It's a <strong>test<\/strong>, or something they heard secondhand. How you react decides whether they stay or walk away."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's an <strong>AI Reputation Crisis Four-Step Method<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"Step 1: Have AI check what's <strong>real<\/strong>. Use this prompt: \"A client said, 'I heard your after-sales service isn't good.' Help me think through a few possibilities: 1. What specific incident might they have heard about? 2. Could this be a competitor spreading rumors? 3. Are they just testing my reaction? Give me some advice on how to respond.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Step 2: Have AI write a <strong>non-defensive response<\/strong>. Use this prompt: \"Give me three ways to respond that don't sound defensive or argumentative: A. Honest style ('Thanks for telling me, this matters to me'); B. Curious style ('Could you tell me more? I'd like to understand what happened'); C. Reframe style ('That kind of feedback is actually why we recently made this improvement'). Keep the tone sincere, don't rush to defend yourself.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Step 3: Have AI put together an <strong>evidence kit<\/strong>. Use this prompt: \"Help me build a 'reputation turnaround kit': 3 recent positive reviews (specific ones), 1 piece of data on after-sales response speed (like 'average 15-minute reply time'), and 1 improvement story ('We used to fall short here, now we offer 24-hour support'). Make sure it's all real and verifiable.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Step 4: Have AI write a <strong>follow-up message<\/strong>. Use this prompt: \"If the client is open to continuing the conversation, write a follow-up line: 'To ease your concerns, let me send you some recent customer reviews so you can judge for yourself.' Keep it natural, not pushy.\""},{"t":"d","who":"U","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"What if he still wants to leave?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Even then, you want to leave a good impression. Have AI write a text like: \"Whether you choose us or not, thank you for this feedback. We'll discuss it internally and keep improving. If you ever need anything, just reach out.\" That kind of attitude means you'll be the first person they think of next time they have a need."},{"t":"ms","items":["Handling a reputation crisis isn't about arguing, it's about <strong>absorbing<\/strong> the feedback well.","<strong>AI Four-Step Method<\/strong>: check what's real + non-defensive response + build an evidence kit + follow-up message.","The key: turn an <strong>attack into a conversation<\/strong>, and <strong>doubt into an opportunity<\/strong>.","The goal: make the client think, \"This person has a big-picture mindset and can be trusted.\""]}],"minutes":3},{"n":52,"title":"A client's team can't agree internally. How do I use AI to map out their decision chain?","part":3,"section":"Handling Objections and Closing","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Vicky","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, we're working with a big client, but tech and procurement disagree. Tech says the product is good, procurement says it's too expensive, and sales says let's wait. I'm stuck in the middle and don't know who to listen to."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"When a client's team can't agree internally, it's the hardest situation but also the biggest opportunity. Disagreement means there's no united front against you. AI can help you draw out a <strong>map of who holds the power<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's an <strong>AI Decision Chain Mapping Method<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"Step 1: Have AI organize <strong>each person's position<\/strong>. Feed in what you've picked up from each contact, using this prompt: \"This client has three key people: Tech Lead Zhang (likes the plan, says 'the product is good'), Procurement Manager Li (thinks it's too expensive, says 'budget doesn't allow it'), and Sales Director Wang (says 'let's wait'). Analyze what each person really wants, what they're worried about, and how they likely relate to each other in terms of power.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Step 2: Have AI find the <strong>shared interest<\/strong>. Use this prompt: \"Help me find one shared interest across these three different positions. For example: Tech wants results, Procurement wants to save money, Sales wants to hit targets. Is there a plan that makes all three feel like it benefits them personally?\""},{"t":"p","html":"Step 3: Have AI design <strong>talking points for each person<\/strong>. Use this prompt: \"Design a short script for each person:"},{"t":"ul","items":["For Tech Lead Zhang: emphasize 'I know you're behind this plan, can you help speak up for it internally?'","For Procurement Manager Li: emphasize 'The price is negotiable, but here's how this plan saves you money elsewhere.'","For Sales Director Wang: emphasize 'If we close this now, your numbers for the quarter are locked in.'"]},{"t":"p","html":"Keep each script short and focused on their core concern.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Step 4: Have AI prepare <strong>internal meeting materials<\/strong>. Use this prompt: \"If they're planning to discuss this internally, help me prepare a one-page summary that highlights the benefit for all three sides. Keep it clean and easy to read, so they can use it to convince the others.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Vicky","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"That way I don't have to guess what they're all thinking."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students used this method and found out that Tech was actually the key decision-maker, but Procurement had a <strong>savings target<\/strong> tied to their KPI. He put together a technical comparison report to help Tech make the case, and gave Procurement a breakdown showing the long-term savings. In the end, all three of them ended up selling the deal internally for him."},{"t":"ms","items":["Disagreement inside a client's team isn't a dead end. It's an <strong>opportunity<\/strong>.","<strong>AI Four-Step Method<\/strong>: analyze positions → find common ground → tackle one by one → prepare materials.","The key: make everyone feel that <strong>being on your side benefits them too<\/strong>.","The goal: turn opponents into <strong>allies<\/strong>."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":53,"title":"Negotiations are stuck on price. How can I use AI to simulate a concession plan?","part":3,"section":"Handling Objections and Closing","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Casey","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I've been talking to a client for a week, and we're stuck on the last 5 percent of the price. If I lower it any more, there's no profit left. But if I don't, the deal falls through. Is there a safe way to make a concession?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Negotiation isn't about whether to concede, it's about <strong>how<\/strong> you concede. Concede carelessly, and the client thinks you still have room to give. Concede smartly, and the client feels you've truly hit your limit."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you an <strong>AI Concession Simulator<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Ask AI to design a <strong>concession ladder<\/strong>. Use this prompt: \"Our floor price is 1 million, our quote was 1.2 million, and the client won't budge from 1.1 million. Help me design 3 different concession paths: A. <strong>All at once<\/strong>: Go straight to 1.1 million, but require full payment upfront. B. <strong>Step by step<\/strong>: Concede 50k, then 30k, then 20k. C. <strong>Trade instead of cut<\/strong>: Keep the price, but add a service package. Break down the pros and cons of each.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Ask AI to simulate the <strong>client's reaction<\/strong>. Use this prompt: \"Act as an experienced buyer reacting to each of these 3 concession paths. Would you think they still have room to move, or that they've hit their limit? How would you keep pushing for a lower price?\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Ask AI to build an <strong>exchange conditions list<\/strong>. Use this prompt: \"If we won't move on price at all, what else can we trade instead? List 10 possible items, like longer payment terms, client referrals, long-term contracts, or dropping certain services. Rank them by value to the client, highest to lowest.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Ask AI to write the <strong>final script<\/strong>. Use this prompt: \"Write a final concession script that includes: 1. Sincerity ('We really want to work with you'); 2. The size of the concession ('I fought for a special exception'); 3. What we need in return ('But I'll need your help with...'); 4. A firm bottom line ('This is the most I can do'). Keep it warm but firm.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Casey","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Can you give me an example?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students used a script AI generated for him: \"Mr. Ryan, I spent three days pushing my company on this. The lowest I can go is 1.12 million, I really can't go lower. But we can shorten the rollout from four weeks to three, so you'll see results sooner. This is everything I can offer. What do you think?\" The client paused for a moment, then said, \"Deal.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["The real issue in a price standoff isn't <strong>how much<\/strong> you give up, it's <strong>how<\/strong> you give it up.","<strong>AI Four-Step Method<\/strong>: Build the ladder -&gt; Simulate the reaction -&gt; List the trades -&gt; Write the final script.","<strong>Rule<\/strong>: Every concession should come with something in return.","<strong>Goal<\/strong>: Make the client feel like <strong>they won<\/strong>, not that you lost."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":54,"title":"The client keeps hesitating at the last minute. How can I use AI to build a \"risk reversal\" script?","part":3,"section":"Handling Objections and Closing","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"Salesperson","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I had a client where everything was set. Plan finalized, price agreed, contract sent. Then out of nowhere he says, \"Let me think about it a bit more.\" How do I break through this kind of last-minute hesitation?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"That last-minute hesitation is <strong>fear of risk<\/strong> kicking in. It's not that they don't want to buy, they're scared of making the wrong choice. Your job isn't to push harder, it's to <strong>take that risk onto yourself<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you the <strong>AI Risk Reversal Four-Step Method<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Ask AI to list <strong>every possible risk<\/strong>. Use this prompt: \"A client is hesitating at the last minute. Guess what they might be worried about across these 4 categories: 1. Implementation risk; 2. Results risk; 3. Decision risk; 4. After-sales risk. For each category, list the most likely worry, written in first person, like 'What if it doesn't work out?'\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Ask AI to design a <strong>risk reversal promise<\/strong> for each worry. Use this prompt: \"For the worry 'what if the results aren't good,' design 3 types of risk reversal promises: A. <strong>Money-back guarantee<\/strong> (with reasonable conditions); B. <strong>Free extension<\/strong> (keep helping for free if results fall short); C. <strong>Pay after results<\/strong> (we work first, you pay once it works). Make them specific and doable.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Ask AI to write a <strong>guarantee statement<\/strong>. Use this prompt: \"Combine these promises into a 200-word 'Customer Guarantee Statement.' Keep the tone firm but warm. Start with something like: 'Morgan, I get why you're worried. To put your mind fully at ease, here's what we promise...'\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Ask AI to design a <strong>pilot plan<\/strong>. Use this prompt: \"If the client is still hesitant, design a small-scale pilot option. Maybe start with just one department, one month, or the basic version. Keep the barrier and risk low, while still proving the value.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Won't this make us look unsure of ourselves?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Actually, it's the opposite. Only the truly confident dare to offer a risk reversal. One of our students sells software. When his client hesitated at the end, he just said, \"Try it for a month. If it works, you pay. If it doesn't, we'll pack up and leave, no charge.\" The client said, \"If you're willing to say that, what do I even have to worry about?\" He signed right there."},{"t":"ms","items":["Last-minute hesitation = <strong>fear of risk<\/strong> kicking in.","<strong>AI Four-Step Method<\/strong>: List the risks + design the reversal + write the guarantee + offer a pilot.","<strong>Key move<\/strong>: Turn the client's risk into <strong>your own risk<\/strong>.","<strong>Goal<\/strong>: Get the client to say, \"If you're willing to do that, what do I have to worry about?\""]}],"minutes":3},{"n":55,"title":"How to use AI to analyze chat logs and know when a client is ready to buy?","part":3,"section":"Handling Objections and Closing","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I keep missing my clients' <strong>buying signals<\/strong>. They're clearly ready to buy, but I don't catch it in time, and they end up going somewhere else."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"A buying signal isn't something you \"feel.\" It's something they actually say, just in a roundabout way. AI can help you translate those hidden signals."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you an <strong>\"AI Buying Signal Detector\"<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Teach AI your \"signal library.\"<\/strong> Feed it your past successful deals, especially the conversations right before closing. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Look at these 10 successful deals. Find the common keywords, questions, and behaviors clients showed 1 to 3 days before they bought. List the 10 most typical buying signals."},{"t":"p","html":"AI might find things like:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Asking \"When can you deliver?\" → Signal","Asking \"What payment options are there?\" → Signal","Saying \"I need to check with X\" → Could be a signal (they're moving things forward)","Asking \"What does ongoing support cost?\" → Strong signal","Saying \"How do you compare to X?\" → They're doing their final comparison"]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Have AI monitor in real time.<\/strong> Feed it new client chat logs regularly with this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Look at this conversation and identify any buying signals the client has already given, ranked from strongest to weakest. If you spot a strong signal, mark it in red and suggest what to do next."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI write your \"closing script.\"<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"The client just showed a strong signal about delivery timing. Write a closing script that sounds natural, not pushy. For example: 'Mr. Chen, if everything looks good on your end, we can schedule delivery for whenever works for you. Should I send over the contract now?'"},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"That way I won't miss it."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students used AI to notice a client had said \"if\" three times in a row. That's a classic <strong>assumptive close signal<\/strong>. He jumped on it: \"Mr. Wang, since you've already thought this through, why wait? Let's kick things off today.\" The client said, \"How did you know I was thinking that?\" Deal closed on the spot."},{"t":"ms","items":["A <strong>buying signal<\/strong> isn't a feeling, it's <strong>language<\/strong>","<strong>AI's three-step method<\/strong>: build a signal library + monitor in real time + generate closing scripts","<strong>10 typical signals<\/strong>: asking about timing, payment, after-sales support, comparing competitors, saying \"if\"...","The goal: show up exactly when the client is ready to buy"]},{"t":"p","html":"---"}],"minutes":3},{"n":56,"title":"How can AI help you say \"no\" gracefully when a client asks for something outside the contract?","part":3,"section":"Handling Objections and Closing","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, clients are always asking for things outside our contract. If I say no, I worry about upsetting them. If I say yes, I worry about overstepping. How do I refuse without damaging the relationship?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Saying no is one of the hardest skills a salesperson has to learn, but you have to learn it. A salesperson who can't say no eventually turns into free customer support. AI can help you make \"no\" sound almost like \"yes.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Here's my <strong>\"Three Moves to Say No Gracefully with AI\"<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Move 1: Have AI figure out what's really behind the request.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"The client is asking us to do X for free, which is outside the contract. Analyze the real reason behind this: 1. Do they genuinely need it? 2. Are they testing our limits? 3. Do they just assume it was already included? Give me some ways to respond."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Move 2: Have AI draft a \"gentle refusal.\"<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Give me 3 different styles of polite refusal:"},{"t":"p","html":"A. Clear boundary: 'This isn't technically covered in the contract, but we can help connect you with a third party.'"},{"t":"p","html":"B. Value trade: 'This normally costs X on its own. If you're willing to..., we can throw it in for free.'"},{"t":"p","html":"C. Relationship first: 'I really want to help you out here, but company policy doesn't allow it. Is there something else I can do for you?'"},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it sincere, not stiff.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Move 3: Have AI come up with an \"alternative solution.\"<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"We can't do X for free, so what alternatives can we offer instead? Give me 3 low-cost options that the client would still see as valuable. For example: a detailed how-to guide, one round of remote support, or an introduction to a supplier who handles this."},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Can you give me an example?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"We had a student whose client wanted free training for their whole team. Here's the script AI came up with: \"Mr. Wang, training isn't part of our contract, but I can record a video walkthrough for your team. They can watch it as many times as they need, and honestly, it works better than a one-time live session. Does that sound okay?\" The client said, \"Sure, that works. Thanks for sorting that out.\" No hard feelings, and the boundary stayed intact."},{"t":"ms","items":["A salesperson who can't say <strong>\"no\"<\/strong> eventually gets taken advantage of","<strong>AI's three moves<\/strong>: figure out the real reason + gentle refusal + alternative solution","The key: you're refusing the <strong>request<\/strong>, not the <strong>person<\/strong>","The goal: make the client feel like <strong>\"you're saying no for my own good\"<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":57,"title":"How to use AI to design \"limited-time offer\" closing scripts?","part":3,"section":"Handling Objections and Closing","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, my company wants to boost sales at the end of the month and told me to send clients a \"limited-time offer.\" But every time I mention an \"end-of-month discount,\" clients think it's just a sales trick. How do I make it sound natural?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"A limited-time offer isn't a trick by itself. Not knowing how to explain it, that's what makes it feel like one. AI can help you turn a discount into a reason your client can't say no to."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you the <strong>\"Four-Step AI Method for Closing with Urgency\"<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Have AI find a <strong>real reason<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"There really is a discount at the end of the month, but just saying 'it ends this month' sounds too blunt. Help me find 3 real, valuable reasons for the customer:"},{"t":"p","html":"Like 'the company is pushing for a sales target this month, so there's an extra discount.'"},{"t":"p","html":"Like 'prices are going up next month because raw material costs increased.'"},{"t":"p","html":"Like 'this is the last batch of discount slots this quarter.'"},{"t":"p","html":"Make it sound real and believable.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Have AI calculate the <strong>cost of waiting<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Help me work out the numbers for the customer: what will they lose if they don't decide by the end of the month? For example, 'missing this offer means spending X more' or 'waiting one more month means losing X in results.' Use specific numbers."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Have AI write <strong>urgency scripts<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Generate 3 different styles of limited-time scripts:"},{"t":"p","html":"A. Honest style: 'Mr. Wang, I'll be straight with you. We have a special deal this month to hit our target, and it's gone once the month ends.'"},{"t":"p","html":"B. Value-focused style: 'What you save is enough to hire another person. It'd be a shame to miss it.'"},{"t":"p","html":"C. Gentle reminder style: 'I just don't want you to regret it later, so I'm giving you a heads-up now.'"},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it natural, don't make it sound like you're rushing them.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Have AI design an <strong>easy way out<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"If the customer is still hesitant, design an 'easy out' option. For example: 'I'll hold the spot for you, can you give me a definite answer tomorrow?' Make sure the customer doesn't feel pressured."},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Can you give me a full example?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students used an AI-generated script like this: \"Mr. Wang, I'll be honest with you. The company's pushing hard for our half-year target this month, and I managed to get you one of the special discount spots. What you save is enough to hire another person. I just don't want you finding out later and regretting it, so I wanted to tell you right away. Should we lock it in today?\" The customer said, \"Well, since you put it that way, let's sign.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["The real goal of urgency closing isn't to <strong>pressure<\/strong> the customer, it's to <strong>help them save money<\/strong>","<strong>The Four-Step AI Method<\/strong>: real reason + cost of waiting + urgency script + easy way out","The key: make the customer feel <strong>you're looking out for them, not yourself<\/strong>","The goal: get the customer to say, <strong>\"Good thing you told me.\"<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":4},{"n":58,"title":"When contract terms cause disputes, how can AI help you understand them and build a communication strategy?","part":3,"section":"Handling Objections and Closing","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I can't make sense of the contract clauses legal sends over. When customers ask about them, I freeze up. How can I quickly understand these legal terms?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Salespeople don't need to be legal experts, but they do need to know how to talk about legal matters. Think of AI as your <strong>legal translator<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's the <strong>\"Three-Step AI Method for Contract Communication\"<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Have AI <strong>translate the clause<\/strong>. Copy the confusing part and use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Translate this contract clause into plain, simple language: [paste clause]. Tell me: 1. What does this actually mean? 2. How does it affect the customer? 3. How does it affect us? 4. What are the common points of dispute?"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Have AI <strong>predict customer questions<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"If a customer read this clause, what are the 3 questions they'd most likely ask? Write them in first person, like 'Why is this clause here?' 'Can we remove it?' 'Can we change it to this instead?'"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Have AI <strong>generate responses<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"For these 3 questions, write responses that:"},{"t":"p","html":"Avoid legal jargon"},{"t":"p","html":"Explain things from the customer's point of view (e.g., 'this clause protects you')"},{"t":"p","html":"Include a backup plan if the clause is genuinely unfavorable to the customer"},{"t":"p","html":"Offer to connect them directly with legal if they're still unsure\""},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So with this, I can actually explain it to my customer?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. One of our students had a customer who didn't understand an \"arbitration clause.\" AI translated it as: \"In plain terms, if there's ever a dispute, we bring in a neutral third party to sort it out instead of going to court. It saves time and money.\" The customer said, \"Oh, that's fine then, no problem.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["A contract isn't an obstacle to closing the deal, it's the <strong>last line of defense for trust<\/strong>","<strong>The Three-Step AI Method<\/strong>: translate the clause + predict questions + generate responses","The key: turn <strong>legal language<\/strong> into <strong>plain human talk<\/strong>","The goal: make the customer feel <strong>you care about their interests more than they do<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":59,"title":"A client keeps saying \"I can't make the decision.\" How can I use AI to find the real decision maker?","part":3,"section":"Handling Objections and Closing","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"Sales","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I've been following up with a client for three months. He keeps saying, \"I can't make the decision, I have to report to someone,\" but won't tell me who's actually in charge. What should I do?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"\"I can't make the decision\" is usually not the truth. It's just a polite way of saying \"I don't want to tell you.\" AI can help you dig out the decision maker hiding behind the scenes."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's an <strong>\"AI Digging Method\"<\/strong> for you:"},{"t":"p","html":"Step 1: Ask AI to analyze <strong>why he won't say<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"A client keeps saying he can't make the decision but won't tell me who can. Please analyze these possibilities:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. He's actually the decision maker and is testing me."},{"t":"p","html":"2. He has decision power but doesn't want the responsibility."},{"t":"p","html":"3. There really is someone else above him, but he can't easily say so."},{"t":"p","html":"4. He doesn't trust me enough yet."},{"t":"p","html":"Give advice on how to respond to each.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Step 2: Ask AI to design <strong>gentle \"digging\" scripts<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Generate three gentle scripts to find the decision maker:"},{"t":"p","html":"A. The Ask-For-Advice Approach: 'Who do you think usually makes the final call on this? Could you point me in the right direction?'"},{"t":"p","html":"B. The Value Approach: 'I need to share some key information with the decision maker, otherwise the proposal can't move forward.'"},{"t":"p","html":"C. The Easy-Out Approach: 'I understand this is awkward for you. What do you think I should do to actually help you here?'"},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it respectful. Don't push too hard.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Step 3: Ask AI to generate an <strong>internal referral strategy<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"If he's willing to share info but can't formally introduce me, design a strategy where he lays the groundwork for me internally. Give him a line he can pass along to the decision maker. For example: 'Boss, I talked to them, their plan is actually pretty solid. Want to meet them?'"},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"Sales","sifu":false,"html":"What if he just won't say anything, no matter what?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Then use the <strong>\"Interest Analysis Method.\"<\/strong> Have AI help you work out why. If he really is the decision maker but won't admit it, he's probably afraid you'll go around him. So put him at ease: \"I'm talking to you, and in the end, you're still the one coordinating everything. I just want to make sure the information is accurate. I won't go around you.\" Make him feel like you <strong>know how the game works<\/strong>."},{"t":"ms","items":["\"I can't make the decision\" can be a <strong>cover story<\/strong>, or it can be a <strong>test<\/strong>","The <strong>AI Three-Step Method<\/strong>: analyze the reason + gentle digging + internal referral","The key: make him feel that <strong>telling you actually benefits him<\/strong>","The goal: move from \"I can't make the decision\" to \"let me introduce you\""]}],"minutes":3},{"n":60,"title":"The client keeps comparing prices. How can I use AI to stop him from hesitating?","part":3,"section":"Handling Objections and Closing","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"Sales","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, a client has already compared four companies and is still asking, \"Is there anything cheaper?\" I'm about to lose it. How do I get him to stop comparing?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"A client who keeps comparing prices isn't looking for the cheapest deal. He's afraid of picking wrong. What you need to fix isn't the \"price comparing,\" it's the <strong>fear<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's an <strong>\"AI Price Comparison Ending Method\"<\/strong> with four steps for you:"},{"t":"p","html":"Step 1: Have AI calculate the <strong>cost of comparing<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"A client has already compared 4 companies and is still going. Help me calculate the real cost: how much is he losing in time, missed opportunities, and energy by continuing to compare? For example: 'You spent a week comparing prices and saved 5%, but that same week could have created 10% more value elsewhere.' Be specific."},{"t":"p","html":"Step 2: Have AI create a <strong>decision fatigue warning<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Write a short message reminding the client about the psychology of 'the more you compare, the harder it is to choose.' For example: 'The more you have to choose from, the easier it is to regret your choice later. Studies show too many options actually make people less satisfied.' Keep the tone gentle, not preachy."},{"t":"p","html":"Step 3: Have AI build <strong>final selection criteria<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Help the client come up with 3 non-price factors to base his decision on, like response speed for support, success rate of implementation, and long-term service quality. Then tell him: 'Price is just the starting point. These are what actually matter.'"},{"t":"p","html":"Step 4: Have AI design a <strong>script to end the comparison<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Write a script to help end the price comparison process. It should include:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. Show you understand him ('I get it, you want the best value for your money.')"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Give him confidence ('I'll say it straight, at this price range, our service is the best out there.')"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Give him a reason to stop ('Comparing more won't beat just trying it. Give it a shot, if it's not right, we'll talk.')"},{"t":"p","html":"4. Give him an easy way out ('If you try it and you're not happy, I'll even help you find another company.')\""},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"Sales","sifu":false,"html":"Can you give me an example?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students used an AI-generated script like this: \"Mr. Ryan, you've compared more companies than most people ever would, so I know you're being careful. But if you keep comparing, your time is worth more than the little bit of money you'd save. At this price point, our service is the best around. And if you try it and aren't happy, I'll personally help you find someone else. Why not just give it a shot?\" The client said, \"Alright, fine. Let's try it.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["Repeated price comparing means <strong>fear of choosing wrong<\/strong>, not \"wanting a deal\"","The <strong>AI Four-Step Method<\/strong>: comparison cost + fatigue warning + selection criteria + closing script","The key: give him a reason to stop that <strong>doesn't make him feel foolish<\/strong>","The goal: move from \"let me compare a bit more\" to \"fine, let's just go with this\""]}],"minutes":4},{"n":61,"title":"After closing a deal, how do I use AI to design a \"Customer Surprise Awakening\" plan?","part":3,"section":"Relationship Maintenance and Referral","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, once a deal closes, I never know how to keep in touch. I don't want to bother the customer, but I don't want them to forget me either. Is there a way to stay on their radar without being annoying?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Closing the deal isn't the finish line, it's the real <strong>start of the relationship<\/strong>. A lot of salespeople treat the close as the end, and that's exactly why their customers turn into one-time buyers. AI can help you build a system that keeps giving customers little surprises."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's the <strong>AI Customer Surprise Awakening Five-Step Method<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Have AI build a <strong>Customer Anniversary Calendar<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I have 50 closed customers. Here's their info: [insert customer list]. Please create a 'Customer Anniversary Calendar' that includes: signing date, birthday, company founding date, and important industry holidays. Sort it by month and remind me who to contact each month."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Have AI design <strong>Surprise Touchpoints<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"For different types of customers (by industry and position), design 10 <strong>low-cost, high-surprise<\/strong> touchpoint ideas. For example:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Six months after signing: send a 'Six-Month Results Review'","Birthday: send an AI-generated handwritten-style greeting card","New industry policy: send an interpretation right away"]},{"t":"p","html":"Each touchpoint should be specific and easy to act on.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Have AI generate <strong>personalized content<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I need to contact Taylor this month, who works in [industry]. Please create a 'Custom Industry Insight' for him. Include: 1. the latest trends in what he cares about; 2. how our product can help him; 3. one interesting piece of industry knowledge. About 200 words, written like a friend sharing something, not a pitch."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Have AI design <strong>low-pressure outreach scripts<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"When I message Taylor, it can't sound like a sales pitch. Give me 3 versions:"},{"t":"p","html":"A. Pure sharing: 'Saw this and thought you might find it useful.'"},{"t":"p","html":"B. Check-in: 'It's been a while, how are things? Also wanted to share something interesting.'"},{"t":"p","html":"C. Asking for input: 'You're the expert here, curious what you think about this.'"},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it natural, no pressure.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5:<\/strong> Have AI <strong>track results and optimize<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"After each outreach, log how the customer responds. Every quarter, have AI analyze which touchpoints get the best response rates and which customer groups are most active, then suggest improvements for the next quarter."},{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"This way I don't have to rack my brain every day trying to figure out who to reach out to."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students used this method, and after a single quarter, referrals from existing customers jumped <strong>40%<\/strong>. One customer told him, \"You're the only salesperson I've met who keeps adding value after the deal closes. Everyone else just disappears once the contract's signed.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["No follow-up after closing = treating the deal as a <strong>one-time transaction<\/strong>","The <strong>AI Five-Step Method<\/strong>: Anniversary Calendar + Surprise Touchpoints + Content Generation + Low-Pressure Scripts + Results Tracking","The key: every touchpoint must <strong>add value<\/strong>, not just remind them you exist","The goal: make customers <strong>look forward<\/strong> to hearing from you"]}],"minutes":4},{"n":62,"title":"How can I use AI to regularly send customers valuable industry news?","part":3,"section":"Relationship Maintenance and Referral","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I want to send my customers industry updates regularly, but digging up material every day takes forever. Can AI screen and generate this for me?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"The core of news-based marketing is simple: you see it <strong>before your customer does<\/strong>, and that saves them time. AI can be your scout and your summarizer."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's the <strong>AI News Service System<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Have AI build a <strong>watch list<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"My customers are in these industries: [insert list]. What are the core topics each one cares about? List the top 3 most important news categories for each industry. For example, manufacturing: automation trends, supply chain shifts, policy subsidies."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Have AI <strong>scout daily<\/strong>. Set it to scan sources like industry media, government policy sites, top blogs, popular Q&amp;A platforms, and competitor updates. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Scan today's news on [industry] and pick out the 3 pieces most worth sending to a customer. For each one, explain why it matters."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Have AI generate a <strong>summary and interpretation<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"For each of these 3 items, write an 80-word summary and interpretation. Format: one sentence on what happened, one sentence on the impact, one sentence of advice. Keep it conversational, not stiff or robotic."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Use AI for <strong>personalized distribution<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Which customers should get today's news? Match it based on tags like industry, job title, and past interests. For example, 'supply chain shifts' fits a Purchasing Director, while 'tech trends' fits a CTO. Give me 5 personalized send recommendations."},{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"How much time does this take each day?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Ten minutes in the morning is plenty. Look over the 3 items AI picked, confirm them, then let AI send them to the right customers. One of our students kept this up for six months, and a customer told him, \"You don't need to sell to me. The news you send every day is reason enough to keep working with you.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["The point of news marketing: <strong>save the customer time<\/strong> and help them stay sharp","The <strong>AI Four-Step Method<\/strong>: Watch List + Daily Scouting + Summary and Interpretation + Personalized Distribution","Frequency: <strong>1 to 2 times a week<\/strong> works best, don't turn it into spam","The goal: make the customer feel like you're their <strong>outsourced brain<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":63,"title":"How do I reactivate silent customers? Let AI help you find the reason and the strategy.","part":3,"section":"Relationship Maintenance and Referral","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I have hundreds of silent customers. I added them on a messaging app, but they've never said a word. How do I reach out without it feeling awkward?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"You need a <strong>gentle wake-up call<\/strong>. AI can help you figure out <strong>why they went silent<\/strong> and <strong>how to wake them up<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you an <strong>AI Silent Customer Reactivation System<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Have AI analyze the <strong>reasons for silence<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I have a list of 200 silent customers. Based on their tags (industry, source, date added), please sort them into categories and guess why each one went silent:"},{"t":"ul","items":["<strong>Category 1:<\/strong> Added me but never had a need (source: scanned a QR code at an event)","<strong>Category 2:<\/strong> Had a need but didn't buy at the time (source: asked questions but never closed)","<strong>Category 3:<\/strong> Bought once but never came back (source: existing customer)","<strong>Category 4:<\/strong> Completely forgot who I am (source: cold add from a stranger)"]},{"t":"p","html":"Give me the ratio and typical traits for each group.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Have AI design a <strong>tiered wake-up strategy<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"For these four groups, design different wake-up strategies:"},{"t":"ul","items":["<strong>Category 1:<\/strong> Value-based wake-up (send useful content so they remember who you are)","<strong>Category 2:<\/strong> Pain-point wake-up (share industry news that reminds them of their original need)","<strong>Category 3:<\/strong> Care-based wake-up (check in like an old customer, ask how they're doing)","<strong>Category 4:<\/strong> Identity-based wake-up (reintroduce yourself, give them a reason to stay connected)"]},{"t":"p","html":"Give two specific actions for each group.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Have AI generate <strong>personalized wake-up scripts<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"For Category 2 customers (asked questions but never bought), they originally asked about XX product. Generate three different styles of wake-up messages:"},{"t":"p","html":"A. Industry update style: 'A new policy on XX just came out, there's a new solution to that problem you asked about.'"},{"t":"p","html":"B. Case story style: 'We recently helped a customer just like you solve XX, want to hear about it?'"},{"t":"p","html":"C. Casual check-in style: 'It's been a while, how's XX going for you these days?'"},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it natural, don't jump straight into selling.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Have AI design a <strong>wake-up rhythm<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Design a <strong>3-round wake-up rhythm<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"Week 1: Send the first value message."},{"t":"p","html":"If no reply, Week 2: Send a second message from a different angle."},{"t":"p","html":"If no reply, Week 3: Send a final message that gives them an easy way out ('If you don't need this right now, no worries, I'll just make a note and reach out whenever you need me')."},{"t":"p","html":"Make the timing and content of each round make sense.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"How high is the wake-up rate?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students used this method and reactivated <strong>30% of their silent customers<\/strong>, and <strong>5%<\/strong> ended up buying again. The secret is this: you're not just popping up out of nowhere, you're <strong>showing up with value<\/strong>."},{"t":"ms","items":["Silent customers just need to be <strong>reactivated<\/strong>","<strong>AI four-step method:<\/strong> analyze the reason + tiered strategy + personalized scripts + wake-up rhythm","Key: every wake-up message needs to give them <strong>a reason worth replying to<\/strong>","Goal: go from \"<strong>who is this?<\/strong>\" to \"<strong>you came at just the right time<\/strong>\""]}],"minutes":4},{"n":64,"title":"What do I do when a long-term customer goes numb? Use AI to design a \"Relationship Refresh\" plan.","part":3,"section":"Relationship Maintenance and Referral","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I have an old customer I've worked with for three years. Lately our conversations feel strictly business, and the warmth we used to have is gone. How do I bring the relationship back to life?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Long-term relationships suffer most from <strong>being taken for granted<\/strong>. Your customer doesn't have a problem with you, they've just <strong>gone numb<\/strong>. You need a <strong>relationship refresh<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you the <strong>AI Relationship Refresh Four-Step Method<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Have AI analyze the <strong>signs of numbness<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Customer Morgan, three years of working together. Here are our interaction logs from the last six months: [paste logs]. Please analyze the signs that they've gone numb, things like shorter replies, slower response times, chat turning into one-line requests, no more personal topics. Guess what might be going on in their head."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Have AI design <strong>out-of-the-ordinary touchpoints<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Design three touchpoints that break the 'strictly business' feeling:"},{"t":"p","html":"A. <strong>Personal care:<\/strong> if they once mentioned their kid taking a big exam, ask about it now"},{"t":"p","html":"B. <strong>Surprise gesture:<\/strong> offer them a free value-added service with no strings attached"},{"t":"p","html":"C. <strong>Role reversal:<\/strong> ask them to be your 'advisor' and get their take on an industry question"},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it sincere, not forced.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Have AI generate a <strong>value review report<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please create a 'Three-Year Partnership Value Review' for Morgan, covering:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. What problems we've helped solve over the past three years (specific examples)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. How far they've come compared to three years ago (use numbers)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. How we can help them in the year ahead (forward-looking)"},{"t":"p","html":"The goal is to help them see your value again. Make it look polished, like a well-designed PDF.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Have AI design a <strong>relationship upgrade ritual<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Design a small ritual that marks a 'relationship upgrade,' for example:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Send them a <strong>VIP Customer<\/strong> certificate","Invite them to a private sharing session","Give them an exclusive title, like <strong>Client Advisor<\/strong>"]},{"t":"p","html":"Make sure they feel like you treat them differently.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Won't that come across as too forced?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"The key is <strong>sincerity<\/strong>. One of our students sent an old customer a three-year review report, and after reading it, the customer said: \"I'd honestly forgotten how much you've helped me. Thanks for these three years.\" The relationship warmed right back up."},{"t":"ms","items":["When a customer feels numb about working with you, it means <strong>they've forgotten your value<\/strong>","<strong>AI four-step method:<\/strong> analyze the signs + break the routine + review the value + upgrade the relationship","Key: help them <strong>see you again<\/strong>","Goal: go from \"<strong>strictly business<\/strong>\" to \"<strong>old friends<\/strong>\""]}],"minutes":3},{"n":65,"title":"How can I use AI to design \"referral\" scripts and incentive plans?","part":3,"section":"Relationship Maintenance and Referral","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I want to ask old clients for referrals, but it always feels awkward, like I'm begging them. Is there a way to do this without feeling so uncomfortable?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"That awkward feeling comes from treating referrals like you're <strong>asking for a favor<\/strong>. A client refers you because sharing gives them something in return, maybe <strong>status<\/strong>, maybe <strong>value<\/strong>, maybe a <strong>real benefit<\/strong>. AI can help you build all three into your approach."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's an <strong>AI Referral System<\/strong> for you:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Have AI analyze the <strong>client type<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I have a long-time client named Taylor. His traits are: job title, industry, personality. Analyze what would most likely make him want to refer someone: A. <strong>Status<\/strong> (recommending something good makes him look sharp); B. <strong>Value<\/strong> (he wants his friends to benefit too); C. <strong>Reward<\/strong> (there's something real in it for him). Give me your analysis and advice."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Have AI generate <strong>low-pressure referral scripts<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Generate 3 different styles of referral scripts, each designed to feel pressure-free:"},{"t":"p","html":"A. <strong>Casual<\/strong>: 'If you know anyone dealing with the same issue, have them add me. I'll take a look for free.'"},{"t":"p","html":"B. <strong>Ask for input<\/strong>: 'You know a lot of people in this space. Who do you think might be a good fit for what we offer?'"},{"t":"p","html":"C. <strong>Reward-based<\/strong>: 'As a thank-you for your support, we have a special perk for loyal clients that you can pass along to a friend.'"},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it natural, not desperate.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Have AI design an <strong>incentive plan<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Design a referral incentive plan that includes:"},{"t":"ul","items":["For the referrer: what reward (cash, service upgrade, gift)","For the new client: what perk (first-order discount, free trial)","How to deliver it (fast and simple)","How to promote it (scripts, flyer copy)"]},{"t":"p","html":"Make sure the numbers work so I don't lose money.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Have AI generate a <strong>thank-you follow-up<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"If a client successfully refers a friend, write a thank-you message. Make it sincere and specific, so they feel good about helping. Example: 'Taylor, the person you referred just signed. He said you gave him a strong recommendation. I really appreciate it, I've got something small for you.'"},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Can you give me an example?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of my students used this AI-generated script: \"Ryan, if you know anyone struggling with hiring, have them add me. I'll take a look for free, no strings attached. Win or lose, it's a chance to make a new friend.\""},{"t":"p","html":"The client replied, \"You seem like a straight shooter. I actually have a friend who needs this, I'll send him your way.\" No awkwardness at all."},{"t":"ms","items":["A referral isn't about <strong>begging<\/strong>, it's about giving someone a <strong>reason to share<\/strong>","<strong>AI Four-Step Method<\/strong>: analyze client type + low-pressure script + incentive plan + thank-you follow-up","Three drivers: <strong>status, value, reward<\/strong>","Goal: get the client to say, \"I have to tell my friends about you\""]}],"minutes":3},{"n":66,"title":"When an old client refers a new one, how do I use AI to write a thank-you note?","part":3,"section":"Relationship Maintenance and Referral","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, an old client referred a new lead to me. I want to write a thank-you note, but I don't know how to make it sound genuine instead of generic. Can AI help?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"A thank-you note is a deposit into the <strong>emotional bank account<\/strong>. Write it sincerely, and the relationship grows stronger. Write it like a template, and you lose all that progress. AI can help you write something that feels <strong>personal and tailored<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's my <strong>AI Thank-You Note Method<\/strong>, in four steps:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Have AI gather the <strong>material<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"An existing client, Morgan, referred a new client, Leo. Help me gather what I need for a thank-you note:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. Highlights from our work with Morgan (when it started, what problems we solved)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Morgan's personal details (any personal topics we've talked about)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. The background of this referral, if known"},{"t":"p","html":"Make the note feel one-of-a-kind.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Have AI choose a <strong>style<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Based on Morgan's personality (if known), recommend the best tone for the note: A. <strong>Warm and enthusiastic<\/strong>; B. <strong>Sincere and simple<\/strong>; C. <strong>Light and humorous<\/strong>; D. <strong>Professional and steady<\/strong>. Explain your reasoning."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Have AI write the <strong>first draft<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Write a thank-you note that includes:"},{"t":"ul","items":["An opening that specifically mentions his referral","A memorable moment from our partnership","A sentiment showing that his referral means he trusts us, and that matters","A promise (not a gift, but 'I'll take care of him the same way I've taken care of you')","A closing"]},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it around 300 words, sincere tone.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Have AI add <strong>personal touches<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Naturally work in these details: [for example, he loves tea, or he was recently promoted]. Make it read like it was written just for him, not copied from a template."},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Can you give me an example?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"\"Morgan, thank you so much! Leo just reached out and mentioned it was you who sent him my way. Honestly, I'm even happier about this than closing a new deal on my own, because it tells me you really trust what we've built together these past three years."},{"t":"p","html":"I still remember when you first tried our product three years ago and said, 'I'll give it a shot, and switch if it doesn't work out.' Now you've trusted us enough to send a friend our way, and that means a lot to me."},{"t":"p","html":"I'll take care of Leo the same way I've taken care of you, I won't let your recommendation down. Let's grab tea soon so I can thank you in person!\""},{"t":"p","html":"Client's reply: \"Your note is making me blush a little. It was nothing, really.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["A thank-you note isn't just a <strong>formality<\/strong>, it's an <strong>emotional deposit<\/strong>","<strong>AI Four-Step Method<\/strong>: gather material + choose style + draft the note + add personal touches","Key: make the client feel your gratitude is <strong>real<\/strong>","Goal: get the client to refer you <strong>again<\/strong> next time they get the chance"]}],"minutes":4},{"n":67,"title":"How can I use AI to manage client birthdays and holiday reminders?","part":3,"section":"Relationship Maintenance and Referral","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I always forget my clients' birthdays and holidays. I only remember after the fact. Is there any way AI can help me track and remind me automatically?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"The heart of building relationships is showing up at the right moment. AI can be your secretary who never forgets."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you an <strong>\"AI Relationship Management System\"<\/strong> in four steps."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Have AI build a <strong>Key Date Database<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I have 200 clients. Here's their information: [import client list, including birthdays, contract signing dates, etc.]. Please create an <strong>Annual Key Date Table<\/strong>, sorted by month, including:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Client birthdays","Contract anniversaries","Important industry holidays","Client company founding dates"]},{"t":"p","html":"Set a reminder on the 1st of every month telling me who to reach out to that month.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Have AI design <strong>differentiated greetings<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Design different greeting styles for different types of clients:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Birthday: warm and personal","Contract anniversary: reflect on the value we've built and thank them for their trust","Industry holidays: professional and useful","Regular holidays: short, not intrusive"]},{"t":"p","html":"Give 3 examples for each.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Have AI generate <strong>personalized messages<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"This month I need to send greetings to Taylor (birthday) and Leo (contract anniversary). Please write:"},{"t":"p","html":"Taylor: a birthday message that mentions a personal topic he brought up last year (like his kid's school exams)"},{"t":"p","html":"Leo: a contract anniversary message that mentions what we've accomplished together this year"},{"t":"p","html":"Keep each under 60 words. Make it sincere, not generic.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Have AI set up <strong>send and follow-up<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please help me set up:"},{"t":"ul","items":["A reminder 3 days ahead to prepare","Send the message at 9 AM on the day","If the client replies within 24 hours, remind me to follow up","If they don't reply, send a follow-up 3 days later saying 'Hope I'm not bothering you, just wanted to wish you well again'\""]},{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"This way I won't miss anyone."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students used this method. Her client got the birthday message and replied, \"I almost forgot my own birthday, thanks for remembering.\" That kind of moment does more than a hundred sales pitches ever could."},{"t":"ms","items":["The core of relationship building: <strong>showing up<\/strong> at the right moment","The <strong>AI four-step method<\/strong>: build a date database + design different greeting styles + generate personalized messages + set up reminders","The key isn't <strong>mass messaging<\/strong>, it's <strong>\"I remember you\"<\/strong>","The goal: make your client feel like <strong>you care about them more than they care about themselves<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":68,"title":"A client posts our product on their social feed. How do I use AI to comment and interact?","part":3,"section":"Relationship Maintenance and Referral","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Lina","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, a client posted our product on their social feed. I want to comment and interact, but I don't know what to say. \"Thanks for your support\" feels too stiff, and I'm worried anything else might come across wrong. What should I do?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"When a client posts about your product, they're handing you an opportunity. But most salespeople either miss it or say the wrong thing. AI can help you catch this golden opportunity."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's my <strong>\"AI Social Feed Interaction Method\"<\/strong> in four steps."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Have AI analyze <strong>what they posted<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"A client posted this on their social feed: [description/screenshot]. Please analyze:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. What's the main focus (the product, the results, the situation)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. What's their mood (happy, showing off, sharing)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. What kind of response are they hoping for (recognition, connection, interaction)"},{"t":"p","html":"Give me suggestions on how to respond.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Have AI generate <strong>comment options<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Based on this analysis, generate 3 different styles of comments:"},{"t":"p","html":"A. Professional recognition: acknowledge how well they're using the product from an expert angle"},{"t":"p","html":"B. Emotional connection: share in their excitement, express that seeing them use it well makes you happy too"},{"t":"p","html":"C. Value-add: build on their situation and offer a small tip"},{"t":"p","html":"Keep each under 20 words. Make it sound natural.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Have AI generate a <strong>follow-up direct message<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"If they reply to my comment, that's a good moment to move to a private message. Please write a message like this:"},{"t":"p","html":"'Seeing you use it so well makes me really happy. You mentioned that situation earlier, actually there's an even better feature for that. Want me to send it over?'"},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it natural, don't make it sound like a sales pitch.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Have AI help you <strong>use the post as social proof<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"If the client's post is really good, you could use it as a case study, but ask permission first. Have AI write something like: 'Morgan, what you posted just now feels really genuine. Would it be okay if we shared it as an example with other clients?'"},{"t":"d","who":"Lina","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Can you give me an example?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"A client posts a photo of themselves working with your product. AI suggests this comment: \"That setup plus that kind of efficiency? Impressive!\" The client replies, \"Haha, all thanks to your product.\" That's your opening to send a private message: \"You mentioned efficiency, there's actually a hidden feature that could make you 30 percent faster. Want to check it out?\" The client responds, \"Wait, that exists? Send it now!\""},{"t":"ms","items":["A client posting about your product is <strong>an opportunity handed to you<\/strong>","The <strong>four AI steps<\/strong>: analyze the content + generate comments + follow up with a direct message + use it as social proof","The key isn't saying <strong>\"thank you\"<\/strong>, it's <strong>riding the momentum<\/strong>","The goal: turn one social media post into <strong>a new order<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":69,"title":"How do I use AI to handle a crisis and turn it into an opportunity when a client complains?","part":3,"section":"Relationship Maintenance and Referral","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, a client called today to complain that our product had a problem. Their tone was really aggressive. How do I handle this without losing them?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"A complaint is a crisis, but it's also a chance to level up the relationship. Handle it well, and the client ends up more loyal than before. AI can help you turn \"putting out fires\" into \"building trust.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Here's a <strong>Six-Step AI Complaint Handling Method<\/strong> for you:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Have AI analyze the <strong>complaint type<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Client complaint content: [Describe it]. Please analyze what type of complaint this is:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. Genuine product defect"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Improper use by the customer"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Expectations set too high"},{"t":"p","html":"4. Just venting emotions"},{"t":"p","html":"Give me a direction on how to respond.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Have AI generate <strong>soothing language<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"The client is upset right now. Please generate a soothing script that includes:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Letting them finish talking first (don't interrupt)","Empathy ('I completely understand how you feel')","Confirming the issue ('You're talking about the XX problem, right?')","A commitment to fix it ('I will make sure this gets sorted out')"]},{"t":"p","html":"Make it sincere, not just going through the motions.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Have AI design a <strong>solution<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Based on this complaint, please design three solutions:"},{"t":"p","html":"A. Quick fix (solve it as fast as possible)"},{"t":"p","html":"B. Compensation-based (fix the issue plus reasonable compensation)"},{"t":"p","html":"C. Service upgrade (fix the issue plus extra service)"},{"t":"p","html":"Each option needs to be specific and doable.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Have AI generate the <strong>solution script<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please turn these solutions into something I can say to the client. Include:"},{"t":"ul","items":["How the problem will be solved","What cooperation is needed from them","The expected timeline","An apology and thanks\""]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5:<\/strong> Have AI design a <strong>follow-up plan<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"After the problem is solved, please design a follow-up plan:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Check if they're satisfied within 24 hours","Ask about how it's going again after a week","Do a check-in call after a month"]},{"t":"p","html":"Make them feel like you've been paying attention this whole time.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 6:<\/strong> Have AI pull out <strong>areas for improvement<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"What can we learn from this complaint? Please give 3 improvement suggestions for the product and after-sales teams."},{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Won't this take a lot of time?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"AI can cut the \"figuring out what to do\" part down to five minutes. One of our students used this method and turned an angry customer into a loyal fan. The customer told him, \"Even though there was a problem, the way you handled it makes me feel like choosing you guys was the right call.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["A complaint is a <strong>relationship checkup<\/strong>. Handle it well and the relationship gets stronger.","The <strong>6-Step AI Method<\/strong>: analyze type + soothe emotions + design solution + write script + follow up + extract improvements","The key: it's not about <strong>\"winning the argument,\"<\/strong> it's about <strong>\"making them feel comfortable\"<\/strong>","The goal: going from <strong>\"I want to complain\"<\/strong> to <strong>\"thank you\"<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":4},{"n":70,"title":"A salesperson is leaving. How can I use AI to hand over clients and avoid losing them?","part":3,"section":"Relationship Maintenance and Referral","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I'm about to quit, and I've got dozens of clients to hand over. How do I keep them from leaving just because I'm gone?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"When a salesperson leaves, that's when client churn spikes. Customers follow the person, not the company. But with AI, you can create a <strong>smooth handover<\/strong> that makes clients feel like the change in staff doesn't really matter."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's a <strong>Four-Step AI Handover Method<\/strong> for you:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Have AI create a <strong>client profile<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I have 20 core clients. Here's their info: [paste client info and follow-up records]. Please create a handover file for each client, including:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Basic client info","History of working together (when it started, what they bought)","Key communication notes (what they care about, their habits)","Personal topics (private things we've talked about)","Next steps (who to reach out to, what to say)"]},{"t":"p","html":"Make it so the person taking over can understand the client in just 3 minutes, almost as well as I do.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Have AI design <strong>handover scripts<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I need to tell clients I'm leaving and introduce my replacement. Please generate 3 different styles of messages:"},{"t":"p","html":"A. Formal (for big clients)"},{"t":"p","html":"B. Warm and personal (for clients I'm close with)"},{"t":"p","html":"C. Smooth transition (emphasizing that service stays the same)"},{"t":"p","html":"Avoid making the client feel like they're being abandoned.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Have AI write a script to <strong>introduce the new colleague<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"The new colleague is named Leo, and has a background in XX. Please write a script introducing him that highlights:"},{"t":"ul","items":["He's even more skilled than me in certain areas","He'll be just as dedicated as I was","I'll stick around for a while to help him get up to speed"]},{"t":"p","html":"Make the client feel reassured.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Have AI design a <strong>transition follow-up plan<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please design a 1-month transition plan:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Week 1: I bring the new colleague along to meet clients","Week 2: The new colleague leads the conversation, I sit in","Week 3: The new colleague handles things independently, I support from behind the scenes","Week 4: I officially step back, the new colleague takes over"]},{"t":"p","html":"Give specific actions for each stage.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So this way, clients won't feel like they've been ditched?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students used this method for a handover. Three months later, the colleague who took over told him: \"Not one client from that batch you handed over left. Actually, two of them even bought more.\" The secret is making the client feel like <strong>\"it's not a change in staff, it's an upgrade in service.\"<\/strong>"},{"t":"ms","items":["The core of a good handover: it's not about <strong>\"dumping the workload,\"<\/strong> it's about <strong>\"passing the torch\"<\/strong>","The <strong>4-Step AI Method<\/strong>: handover files + notification scripts + introducing the new colleague + transition plan","The key: make the client feel that <strong>\"a new person is fine\"<\/strong>","The goal: <strong>you leave, but the client stays<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":71,"title":"I don't know how to start my first sales short video. How can AI help me?","part":3,"section":"Short Video and Livestream Sales","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, my company wants me to make short videos to get customers. I've never done this before. I don't know what to say, how to film it, or if it'll even work. I'm stuck right at the first step."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"A lot of people get stuck on short videos because of perfectionism. They want their first video to go viral, so they never end up filming anything at all. AI can help turn \"I don't know\" into \"I can start right now.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Here's an <strong>AI Five-Step Start Method<\/strong> for short videos:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Ask AI to find your positioning.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I'm a salesperson in [insert industry]. My target clients are [insert demographic]. Please analyze:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. What role could I play in short videos? (Expert, sharer, peer, or someone who's learned from mistakes)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. What kind of content fits me best? (Tips, case studies, opinions, or stories)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. What makes me different? (For example, 'the salesperson who really knows the tech' or 'the salesperson who tells the best stories')"},{"t":"p","html":"Give me 3 positioning options.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Ask AI to build a topic list.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please generate 50 short video topics. They should:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Relate to my clients' biggest pain points","Come from my own experience as a salesperson","Be simple enough to explain in 1 to 2 minutes","Have catchy titles"]},{"t":"p","html":"Sort them into 'pain point,' 'avoiding mistakes,' 'case study,' and 'opinion' types.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Ask AI to write your first script.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I picked this topic: [pain point]. Please write a 1-minute video script with this structure:"},{"t":"ul","items":["First 3 seconds: a hook ('Are you still struggling with...?')","Next 30 seconds: explain the pain point and lead into the solution","Last 15 seconds: give value and ask people to follow or message me"]},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it casual, like I'm actually talking.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Ask AI for filming advice.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"How should I film this script? Give me specific suggestions on:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Where to film (office, outdoors, or just talking to the camera)","What to wear","What tone to use (serious, friendly, or energetic)","What props I might need","Whether to add subtitles or effects\""]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Ask AI to help with posting.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"My first video is ready. Please help me:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Come up with 3 different titles","Write 3 captions in different styles","Pick 3 good hashtags","Suggest the best time to post\""]},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Now I can actually take the first step."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students used this method and filmed their first video on day one. It only got 200 views, but they got 5 new contacts out of it. He told me, \"If AI hadn't helped me get past that first step, I'd probably still be stuck wondering what to film.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["The first step in making short videos isn't going <strong>viral<\/strong>, it's just <strong>getting started<\/strong>","The <strong>AI Five-Step Method<\/strong>: find your positioning + build a topic list + write the script + get filming advice + optimize your post","The key is to <strong>lower the barrier to starting<\/strong>. Film first, worry later","The goal is to go from <strong>\"I can't\"<\/strong> to <strong>\"I can film\"<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":4},{"n":72,"title":"How do I use AI to turn a sales copy into a short video script?","part":3,"section":"Short Video and Livestream Sales","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I have a sales copy that I think is pretty good, and I want to turn it into a short video. But just reading it out loud sounds boring. How do I turn it into a script that actually works on video?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Text and video are two different languages. Text, people can read slowly. Video, people need to understand in a split second. AI can help you turn something meant to be <strong>read<\/strong> into something meant to be <strong>watched<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's an <strong>AI Four-Step Method<\/strong> for turning copy into a script:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Ask AI to pull out the core selling points.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Here's my sales copy: [paste copy]. Please pull out:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. The 3 most important selling points"},{"t":"p","html":"2. The 1 most convincing case study"},{"t":"p","html":"3. The 1 most memorable line"},{"t":"p","html":"The script only needs these. Cut everything else.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Ask AI to turn it into visuals.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please turn the content above into visuals:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Pain point: what image could show this? (For example, 'too many reports' could look like a pile of paper stacked to the ceiling)","Solution: what image could show this? (For example, 'one-click generation' could be a phone tap that makes the paper pile vanish)","Results: what image could show a before-and-after?"]},{"t":"p","html":"Give me specific visual ideas.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Ask AI to build a storyboard.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please create a 60-second storyboard. Format it as:"},{"t":"p","html":"Time | Visual | Dialogue | Subtitles"},{"t":"p","html":"Each shot should last 5 to 10 seconds. Make it flow smoothly and keep a good rhythm.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Ask AI to write the spoken lines.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Based on the storyboard, write out the full spoken script. Make sure it:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Sounds like everyday talking","Keeps each line under 15 words","Marks where to pause and what to emphasize","Ends with a call to action\""]},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Can you give me an example?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Say a copy says \"our software improves efficiency.\" AI could turn that into a script like this:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Visual: someone at their desk, frustrated, staring at a messy spreadsheet","Line: \"Monday morning, and this pile of reports makes me want to disappear.\"","Visual: he taps his phone, and the computer generates the report automatically","Line: \"Now, one tap, and it's done. Wouldn't you rather spend that time on coffee?\"","Visual: he's relaxed, sipping coffee, the software's name shows on screen","Line: \"Want to know how? Message me, I'll send you the guide.\""]},{"t":"ms","items":["Copy is a <strong>product manual<\/strong>, video is a <strong>movie<\/strong>","The <strong>AI Four-Step Method<\/strong>: pull out the core + turn it into visuals + build a storyboard + write the spoken lines","The key is to <strong>tell a story with images<\/strong>, not just read from a script","The goal is to make people <strong>see and understand<\/strong>, not just <strong>listen until the end<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":73,"title":"No One Watching Your Livestream? Use AI to Generate 100 Interactive Topics in Advance","part":3,"section":"Short Video and Livestream Sales","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, when I livestream, people keep leaving halfway through. I feel like I don't know how to interact. I don't know what to say to keep people watching."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"If your livestream can't hold an audience, ninety percent of the time it's because you keep talking and never give them a chance to join in. AI can help you prepare a whole library of topics that get people talking."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you an <strong>AI Livestream Interaction Generator<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Ask AI to design <strong>topic categories<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I run livestreams for [insert industry]. My target audience is [insert audience]. Please design 6 different types of interactive topics:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. Pain point type ('Have you ever run into this...')"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Choice type ('Option A or Option B? Tell me in the comments')"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Experience sharing type ('How did you solve this?')"},{"t":"p","html":"4. Voting type ('Type 1 if you think this matters')"},{"t":"p","html":"5. Guessing type ('Guess how much this costs')"},{"t":"p","html":"6. Giveaway type ('Once we hit 500 likes, I'll give away...')"},{"t":"p","html":"Give me 3 examples for each type.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Ask AI to generate topics in bulk. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Based on the 6 types above, generate 100 interactive topics for my industry and product. Give me 15 to 20 per category. They need to be specific and actually get people to respond, not empty filler like 'how's everyone doing.'"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Ask AI to design a <strong>topic rhythm<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Assume a 60-minute livestream. Design a topic rhythm schedule for me:"},{"t":"ul","items":["First 3 minutes: one warm-up topic","Every 10 minutes: insert 1 to 2 topics","Peak moment: one high-engagement topic","Right before ending: one giveaway topic"]},{"t":"p","html":"Note the expected effect for each one.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Ask AI to write <strong>transition lines<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Write a 10-second transition line for each topic, something like:"},{"t":"p","html":"'Speaking of that, I want to ask you all...'"},{"t":"p","html":"'Don't let me do all the talking, what do you think...'"},{"t":"p","html":"'This one matters, type 1 and I'll keep going...'\""},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"100 topics is a lot. What if I never get through them all?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"That's fine. The point isn't to use every single one, it's to always have something ready. One of our students prepared 100 topics for their first livestream. They only ended up using 8, and their engagement rate still tripled."},{"t":"p","html":"They told me: \"Before, I was the one begging viewers not to leave. Now they're the ones asking me to keep talking.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["The key to keeping people in a livestream: get them to <strong>participate<\/strong>, not just listen","<strong>AI four-step method<\/strong>: design categories + generate in bulk + build a rhythm + write transitions","<strong>Six topic types<\/strong>: pain points, choices, sharing, voting, guessing, giveaways","Goal: move the audience from \"listening to you\" to \"chatting with you\""]}],"minutes":3},{"n":74,"title":"Livestream Going Quiet? Use AI to Save It in Real Time","part":3,"section":"Short Video and Livestream Sales","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, what I fear most is dead air during a livestream. No comments, no interaction, and the longer I talk alone, the more awkward it gets. How do I fix this?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Dead air is the darkest moment of any livestream. But AI can help you prepare \"emergency ammo\" ahead of time, so you always have something to fall back on."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's an <strong>AI Silence-Breaker Kit<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Ask AI to build a <strong>silence-breaker topic bank<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Prepare 20 topics I can use to break a silence. I need:"},{"t":"ul","items":["5 self-Q&amp;A style ('Some of you might be wondering...')","5 audience-invite style ('If you just joined, type 1')","5 giveaway style ('Give it 5 more minutes, there's a prize coming')","5 story style ('Let me tell you a real customer story')"]},{"t":"p","html":"Keep each one short and easy to drop in quickly.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Ask AI to write <strong>silence-breaking scripts<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"If there's silence for more than 30 seconds, give me 3 different styles of recovery lines:"},{"t":"p","html":"A. Self-deprecating: 'Guess I've been too dry up here. You all need some water. Type 1 so I know you're still with me.'"},{"t":"p","html":"B. Redirect: 'No one talking? Alright, let me show you something good.' (then show a product or a document)"},{"t":"p","html":"C. Ask for input: 'Give me your thoughts, do you actually want to hear more about this?'"},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it natural, no panic.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Have AI create <strong>simulated comments<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Give me 20 sample comments I could read out loud myself. For example:"},{"t":"p","html":"'Someone who just joined asks: how much is this?'"},{"t":"p","html":"'A viewer asks: is this good for beginners?'"},{"t":"p","html":"'Someone comments: this is really helpful'"},{"t":"p","html":"Give me 5 for each type, and make them sound real.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Have AI design an <strong>icebreaker move<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"If the silence keeps going, design an icebreaker move:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Pull out a prop and show it off","Demo a feature live","Suddenly raise your voice","Say 'let me grab a sip of water, think of a question for me'"]},{"t":"p","html":"The goal is to break the flat, boring rhythm.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Won't reading fake comments feel fake?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"You're not pretending someone actually commented. You're using \"people often ask\" as a way to bring up a topic naturally. For example, say: \"A lot of people ask me if this works for beginners. Let me answer that right now.\" That sounds natural, and it solves the awkward problem of nobody asking anything."},{"t":"ms","items":["Dead air isn't your fault, but <strong>being unprepared<\/strong> is","<strong>AI four-step method<\/strong>: topic bank + recovery scripts + simulated comments + icebreaker moves","Key rule: you need to act within <strong>30 seconds<\/strong> of going quiet","Goal: go from \"no one's talking\" to \"I've got something to say\""]}],"minutes":3},{"n":75,"title":"How to use AI to analyze livestream data and find why conversion is low?","part":3,"section":"Short Video and Livestream Sales","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I livestream every week, but my conversion rate never goes up. I don't understand the data, and I don't know where the problem is. Can AI help me analyze it?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"If you don't understand your data, you're basically livestreaming blind. AI can turn a pile of numbers into a <strong>map<\/strong> that shows you where the problems are and what to do about them."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you a <strong>Five-Step AI Livestream Data Analysis Method<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Have AI organize the data.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Here is the data from my last 3 livestreams: [Paste data table]. Please organize it into a clear report including:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Overview of each session (viewers, average watch time, interaction rate, conversion rate)","Trend comparison (up/down)","Flagged anomalies (which sessions were unusually good or bad)\""]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Have AI find the drop-off points.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please analyze when viewers left and find the times with the biggest drop-offs. For example:"},{"t":"ul","items":["How many left in the first 3 minutes?","Which time slot had the most exits?","How many stayed until the end?"]},{"t":"p","html":"Guess the possible reasons (boring topics, product intro too long, too little interaction).\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI analyze the conversion path.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please analyze the funnel from viewing to interaction to clicking to buying:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Viewer-to-interaction conversion rate","Interaction-to-click conversion rate","Click-to-sale conversion rate"]},{"t":"p","html":"Which step has the lowest conversion? What might be causing it?\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI compare good sessions with bad ones.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please compare the best and worst performing livestreams and find the key differences:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Differences in topic choice","Differences in interaction frequency","Differences in product explanation length","Differences in host energy"]},{"t":"p","html":"List 3 core differences.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Have AI generate optimization suggestions.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Based on the analysis above, give 5 specific, actionable suggestions for the next livestream. For example:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Bring up the first interaction topic within the first 5 minutes","Keep product explanations under 15 minutes","Remind viewers about the giveaway every 10 minutes","Repeat the link 3 times before ending"]},{"t":"p","html":"And so on.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"Now I know what to do."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students used this method and found that his viewers dropped off the most during the pricing section. AI suggested he move the price to the end and talk about value first. After making that change, his conversion rate went up <strong>50 percent<\/strong>."},{"t":"ms","items":["Data isn't something you just <strong>look at<\/strong>. It's something you <strong>use<\/strong>.","The <strong>AI Five-Step Method<\/strong>: organize data + find drop-offs + analyze conversion + compare sessions + generate suggestions","The key: find that <strong>one change that fixes everything<\/strong>","The goal: make each session better than the last"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":76,"title":"How can I use AI to write a \"product knowledge base\" for a digital avatar host?","part":3,"section":"Short Video and Livestream Sales","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, the company put me in charge of our digital avatar livestreams, but the avatar keeps saying the wrong things or freezing up when it can't answer. How do I make it smarter?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"If a digital avatar seems \"dumb,\" it's not because it's stupid. It's because <strong>you haven't fed it enough<\/strong>. A digital avatar needs a knowledge base, just like a new hire needs a training manual."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you a <strong>Five-Step Method for Building a Digital Avatar Knowledge Base<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Have AI organize the product knowledge.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Our product is [product name], with the following features: [list]. Please organize this into a format the avatar can use:"},{"t":"ul","items":["One sentence explaining each feature","A customer case study for each feature","A common question for each feature","A scenario description for each feature"]},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it conversational, suitable for voice output.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Have AI organize the FAQs.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please compile the 50 most common customer questions, sorted into:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Product questions (20)","Pricing questions (10)","After-sales questions (10)","Comparison questions (5)","Other (5)"]},{"t":"p","html":"Give each question a short standard answer, under 30 words.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI design response strategies.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"How should the avatar respond in these situations:"},{"t":"ul","items":["The customer asks something not in the knowledge base","The customer is upset or complaining","The customer asks for a discount","The customer asks about a competitor"]},{"t":"p","html":"Give a standard response template for each.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI write the persona script.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"The avatar's persona is friendly, professional, and occasionally funny. Rewrite all the scripts above to match this persona. For example, change 'Hello' to 'Hey there, friend.' Change 'this product' to 'this little gadget.' Make the persona feel distinct."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Have AI set up a way to keep updating.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please design an update system for the knowledge base:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Collect the questions the avatar couldn't answer each week","Update the knowledge base once a month","Do a full review every quarter"]},{"t":"p","html":"This keeps the avatar getting smarter over time.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Taylor","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"That's a lot to write. How long would this take?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"AI writes the first draft, you just review and adjust it. One of our students used this method and had a full digital avatar knowledge base built in <strong>three days<\/strong>. After launch, the avatar's accuracy rate jumped from <strong>60 percent to 92 percent<\/strong>."},{"t":"ms","items":["A \"dumb\" digital avatar just means <strong>you haven't fed it enough<\/strong>","The <strong>AI Five-Step Method<\/strong>: product knowledge + FAQs + response strategies + persona script + ongoing updates","The key: the more complete the knowledge base, the more human the avatar feels","The goal: make customers feel like they're chatting with a real person"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":77,"title":"How Can I Use AI to Batch-Generate Short Video Scripts for Product Selling Points?","part":3,"section":"Short Video and Livestream Sales","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, we have dozens of products, and each one needs a short video introduction. Writing scripts one by one is way too slow. Is there a way to produce them in batches?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Sales videos don't need to be \"different every time,\" they need to be \"usable every time.\" AI can help you build a <strong>script production line<\/strong> that churns out solid drafts in bulk."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you the <strong>AI Script Production Line<\/strong> method:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Ask AI to build a <strong>template library<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please design 5 different styles of video scripts:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. Pain point solver: Start with a pain point, introduce the product, show the results, then a call to action."},{"t":"p","html":"2. Case story: Start with a customer story, bring in the product, show the change, then wrap up."},{"t":"p","html":"3. Comparison review: Compare A and B, highlight the advantages, explain why choose us, then a call to action."},{"t":"p","html":"4. Knowledge share: Start with industry knowledge, lead into the product, go deeper, then invite interaction."},{"t":"p","html":"5. Trending hook: Use a hot topic to grab attention, link it to the product, extend the value, then guide the viewer."},{"t":"p","html":"Give one example for each template.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Ask AI to build a <strong>selling point library<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Here are all our product selling points: [List]. Please organize each one using these categories:"},{"t":"ul","items":["One core line","One customer scenario","One data point","One comparative advantage"]},{"t":"p","html":"Turn this into a source material library.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Ask AI to <strong>batch-generate first drafts<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Using Template 1 (Pain Point Solver) and these selling points: [A, B, C], generate 3 scripts for 3 different products. Each should run about 60 seconds and sound conversational. Start with 3 so I can check the quality."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Ask AI to make <strong>differentiated adjustments<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"These 3 drafts are a bit too similar. Please adjust:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Make the first one sound more relaxed","Add more questions to the second one","Add a real customer quote to the third one"]},{"t":"p","html":"Give each one its own distinct feel.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5:<\/strong> Ask AI to generate <strong>supporting materials<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"For each script, give me:"},{"t":"ul","items":["3 title options","1 cover caption","3 hashtags","1 comment-section interaction line"]},{"t":"p","html":"Package it all together.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So how many can we produce in a day with this?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"My team used this method to produce <strong>100 scripts in one week<\/strong>. We filmed 80 videos, posted 60, had <strong>3 go viral<\/strong>, and got <strong>200 inquiries<\/strong> out of it. The key is: <strong>volume is what creates hits.<\/strong>"},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>Batch production<\/strong> = Templates + Materials + Combinations","<strong>AI Five-Step Method<\/strong>: Template library + Selling point library + Batch generation + Differentiation + Supporting materials","Key rule: <strong>quantity first, then quality<\/strong>","Goal: <strong>use volume to raise your odds of success<\/strong>"]},{"t":"p","html":"Part 3: Practical Application A1"},{"t":"p","html":"---"}],"minutes":3},{"n":78,"title":"How Can I Use AI to Answer Customer Questions in Real Time During a Livestream?","part":3,"section":"Short Video and Livestream Sales","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Vera","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I get flooded with questions during livestreams. Talking and checking my phone at the same time is impossible, I keep missing questions or answering wrong. Can AI help me with this?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Doing two things at once during a livestream is normal, but AI can be your <strong>second brain<\/strong>. You talk, AI answers."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's my <strong>AI Livestream Assistant Setup<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Ask AI to build a <strong>real-time Q&amp;A library<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please organize all common questions into a keyword-and-answer format, like this:"},{"t":"p","html":"Keyword: price → Answer: 'Check the little icon in the bottom left, there's a special deal today.'"},{"t":"p","html":"Keyword: how to use → Answer: 'Tap my profile to join the fan group, there's a tutorial there.'"},{"t":"p","html":"Keyword: is this for me → Answer: 'This is mainly for [X] type of people, tell me your situation and I'll help you figure it out.'"},{"t":"p","html":"Generate about 200 of these to cover 80% of the questions I'll get.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Set up <strong>real-time alerts<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please design a livestream alert system for me:"},{"t":"ul","items":["When a keyword shows up in the comments, AI should pop up a reminder","The reminder should include the question and a suggested answer","Rank by urgency, price questions get answered right away, casual chat can wait","Summarize the most common questions every 5 minutes\""]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Ask AI to write <strong>standardized answers<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please rewrite these answers so they work for livestream speaking:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Each line should take under 10 seconds to say","Keep it warm and friendly","Push the viewer toward the next action"]},{"t":"p","html":"For example: 'How much? It's at its lowest price today, check the corner, it's selling fast.'\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Have AI do a <strong>post-stream review<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"After the stream, please help me analyze:"},{"t":"ul","items":["What questions came up today","Which ones I didn't answer well","Which ones should get added to next time's script","Give me a list of suggestions to improve\""]},{"t":"d","who":"Vera","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"This way I won't miss any customers."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of my students used this method and never missed a question again. One time, a customer asked something new that the AI didn't recognize. She remembered it herself and added it to the knowledge base right after the stream ended. The customer told her: \"I figured you wouldn't reply, but you even sent me a private message. That's really thoughtful.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["The core of livestream Q&amp;A: <strong>don't miss, don't get it wrong, don't be slow<\/strong>","<strong>AI Four-Step Method<\/strong>: Build Q&amp;A library + real-time alerts + standardized answers + post-stream review","Key: <strong>let AI watch the comment section for you<\/strong>","Goal: make the customer feel like <strong>you're always paying attention to them<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":79,"title":"How do I use AI to design \"closing\" scripts for my livestream?","part":3,"section":"Short Video and Livestream Sales","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, my livestreams go well. People engage a lot. But the moment I post the product link, everyone disappears. How do I create a closing script that doesn't feel pushy?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Closing feels annoying when you only show up to demand payment. Real closing means <strong>helping the customer decide<\/strong>, not forcing them. AI can help you build a closing system that actually feels comfortable."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's my <strong>AI Four-Part Closing Framework<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Part 1: Have AI calculate the benefits of buying now.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Help me work out the math: what extra benefits does the customer get by ordering right now? For example:"},{"t":"ul","items":["They can start using it a day sooner and see results sooner","There's a free gift today that won't be there tomorrow","Buying now means it arrives in time for a specific event"]},{"t":"p","html":"Use real numbers and real situations.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Part 2: Have AI calculate the cost of not buying.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Help me show the customer what they'll lose if they don't order today. For example:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Miss this deal and wait another six months","Competitors might already be using it","The problem just keeps dragging on"]},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it honest, don't scare them.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Part 3: Have AI build a stepped closing script.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Design 3 levels of closing lines:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Level 1 (Soft): Only 5 spots left, grab one while you can","Level 2 (Medium): The system's already pushing me, I can only hold it for 10 more minutes","Level 3 (Firm): Final 3 minutes, then it's gone"]},{"t":"p","html":"Make each level flow naturally into the next, don't jump.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Part 4: Have AI write a \"way out\" script.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"If the customer's still on the fence, design a way to help them save face:"},{"t":"ul","items":["If today's not convenient, just pay a deposit and I'll hold your spot","Go ahead and place the order, you can cancel within 24 hours, this just secures your spot","Add me and I'll send you the link personally"]},{"t":"p","html":"Make sure they don't feel pressured, but still give them an easy exit.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Can you show me a full example?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students used this AI-generated script:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Everyone, these are the last 10 units at this special price. Once they're gone, the price goes back up. Do the math: buying now saves you $50, basically like getting a free gift. Start using it today, and you'll be earning $100 more by tomorrow. Think it through, because if you miss this, you're waiting three months. Only 5 units left, counting down, 3, 2, 1..."},{"t":"p","html":"The customer said, \"Stop counting, I'll take it!\""},{"t":"ms","items":["Real closing means <strong>helping the customer do the math<\/strong>, not forcing them to pay","<strong>AI Four-Part Framework<\/strong>: benefits of buying now + cost of not buying + stepped scripts + a way out","The key is making the customer feel that <strong>buying now is good for them<\/strong>","The goal: shift from \"you're pressuring me\" to \"I need to buy this now\""]},{"t":"p","html":"---"}],"minutes":3},{"n":80,"title":"How do short videos and livestreams work together? Use AI to design a \"Short Video to Livestream Loop\"","part":3,"section":"Short Video and Livestream Sales","blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Ethan","role":"Sales Rep","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, we handle short videos and livestreams as two separate things. Short videos bring in traffic, livestreams convert it, but the connection between them feels broken. How do we get them working together?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Think of short videos as the <strong>hook<\/strong>, and the livestream as the <strong>net<\/strong>. If you throw the hook but the net's not open, the fish just swims away. AI can help you build a closed loop that connects short videos and livestreams."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's my <strong>AI Six-Step Method for Short Video to Livestream Coordination<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Have AI design traffic-driving short videos.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I want to drive sign-ups for a livestream next Wednesday on the topic of [xx]. Generate 5 short video scripts, 15 seconds each. Requirements:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Grab attention in the first 3 seconds","Build suspense in the next 5 seconds","Push viewers to sign up in the last 7 seconds"]},{"t":"p","html":"Example: 'Wednesday at 8 PM, I'll share a trick 99 percent of people don't know. You have to sign up to see it.'\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Have AI design the livestream opening.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"At the start of the livestream, how do I connect with viewers who came from my short videos? Write a script that:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Thanks everyone for watching the video","Quickly recaps the suspense from the video","Teases what's coming today"]},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it natural, don't just repeat the video.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI plan out highlight clips.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"During the livestream, what moments are worth cutting into short clips afterward? Predict 3 potential highlights:"},{"t":"ul","items":["A surprising insight","A real customer story","A strong interactive moment"]},{"t":"p","html":"For each one, suggest a length, title, and caption.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI plan your posting schedule.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"After the livestream ends, help me plan out a posting schedule for the clips:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Day 1: Post the best clip to drive sign-ups for the next livestream","Day 2: Post a value-packed clip to keep people engaged","Day 3: Post an interactive clip to spark conversation","Day 4: Post a teaser clip to build hype for the next livestream"]},{"t":"p","html":"Make it flow as a complete loop.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Have AI track your results.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Help me track:"},{"t":"ul","items":["How many sign-ups each traffic video brought in","How many viewers said they came from watching the videos","How many new followers the clips brought in","What the overall ROI of this loop is\""]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 6: Have AI generate improvement tips.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Based on this data, give me 5 specific, actionable ways to improve the next round of short video and livestream coordination."},{"t":"d","who":"Ethan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So this way, short videos and livestreams aren't two separate things anymore."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students used this method. Sign-ups from their short videos <strong>tripled<\/strong>, and their livestream conversion rate went up <strong>50 percent<\/strong>. He told me, \"Before, short videos were short videos and livestreams were livestreams. Now, the videos handle getting people to sign up, and the livestream handles closing the sale.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>Short-to-live coordination<\/strong> = short video traffic + livestream conversion + clip re-distribution","<strong>AI Six-Step Method<\/strong>: traffic videos + livestream opening + highlight clips + posting schedule + tracking results + improvement tips","The key is making <strong>every step serve the next one<\/strong>","The goal: build a <strong>flywheel<\/strong> where videos lead to livestreams, and livestreams lead back to more videos"]}],"minutes":4},{"n":81,"title":"ChatGPT vs. Claude vs. Gemini: Which is best for sales?","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, there are too many AI tools now. ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, Perplexity... Which one should I use? Trying them all takes too much time."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"There is no \"best\" tool, only the \"most suitable\" one. Think of a toolbox. It has a hammer and a screwdriver. You can't say the hammer is better than the screwdriver. AI tools work the same way, each one has its own job."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you a <strong>Sales AI Selection Guide<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Get clear on what you actually need. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please help me figure out what type of AI tool works best for each of these sales tasks:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Writing outreach emails or copy (needs strong language skills)","Analyzing customer data (needs data processing skills)","Real-time translation or cross-border communication (needs multi-language skills)","Generating images or videos (needs multimodal skills)","Summarizing long documents (needs a large context window)"]},{"t":"p","html":"List 2 to 3 tools that fit each one.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Have AI compare the mainstream tools. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please compare these mainstream AI tools and score them for sales use (1 to 5):"},{"t":"p","html":"1. ChatGPT (OpenAI)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Claude (Anthropic)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Gemini (Google)"},{"t":"p","html":"4. Microsoft Copilot"},{"t":"p","html":"5. Perplexity"},{"t":"p","html":"6. Grok (xAI)"},{"t":"p","html":"Compare them on: language understanding, copywriting ability, data analysis, multimodal skills, pricing, and context length."},{"t":"p","html":"Give me a 'sales scenario recommendation table.'\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Ask AI to suggest a <strong>combo plan<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please recommend a 'Sales AI Power Combo':"},{"t":"ul","items":["Daily copywriting: which one?","Deep analysis: which one?","Quick replies (mobile-friendly): which one?","Long documents or proposals: which one?","Best free option: which one?"]},{"t":"p","html":"Explain your reasoning.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Ask AI for a <strong>learning priority<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"If I'm a total beginner in sales and only want to learn 1 to 2 tools first, which two should I pick? Why? Give me a 30-day learning plan."},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So which one should I use right now?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Based on what you need, here's my take:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Daily copy, outreach emails: <strong>ChatGPT<\/strong> or <strong>Claude<\/strong> (Claude is excellent at natural-sounding writing and has a solid free tier).","Quick lookups, mobile use: <strong>Perplexity<\/strong> (fast, cites its sources, and has a great mobile app).","Long document analysis, big context: <strong>Gemini<\/strong> (handles a huge context window).","Multimodal image/video generation: use dedicated tools like <strong>Midjourney<\/strong> or <strong>Runway<\/strong>, not chat-based AI."]},{"t":"p","html":"My team's setup: <strong>ChatGPT<\/strong> for first drafts, <strong>Gemini<\/strong> for long documents, <strong>Perplexity<\/strong> for quick research on the go. Together these three cover almost every situation."},{"t":"p","html":"One thing to keep in mind: tools change fast. What I've listed above might not stay the best choice forever, since AI tools keep updating and evolving. What matters is remembering the thinking behind these prompts, so you can ask AI in real time for whatever's best based on your current needs."},{"t":"ms","items":["There's no <strong>best<\/strong> tool, only the <strong>most suitable<\/strong> one","Selection criteria: <strong>task match<\/strong> + <strong>cost<\/strong> + <strong>your habits<\/strong>","Recommended combo: <strong>ChatGPT<\/strong> (copy) + <strong>Gemini<\/strong> (long docs) + <strong>Perplexity<\/strong> (mobile)","Goal: <strong>master 1 to 2 tools first<\/strong>, then expand"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":82,"title":"Which AI Avatar Livestreaming Tool Is Best? A Guide to Avoiding Pitfalls","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I want to try AI avatar livestreaming, but there are so many tools out there, priced anywhere from a few dollars to thousands. How do I choose?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"AI avatar livestreaming really is a hot trend, but it's also full of traps. A lot of people spend big money on tools, only to have them sit unused after a couple of days. Let me give you an <strong>AI Avatar Selection Guide<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Get clear on the type of avatar you need. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"There are several types of avatars for livestreaming. Please break them down:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. 2D real-person clone (generated from your photos)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. 3D cartoon style"},{"t":"p","html":"3. 3D hyper-realistic style"},{"t":"p","html":"4. AI-driven (real-time interaction)"},{"t":"p","html":"What is each type best for? What are the pros and cons?\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> List and compare the mainstream tools. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please compare these mainstream AI avatar tools:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. HeyGen"},{"t":"p","html":"2. D-ID"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Synthesia"},{"t":"p","html":"4. Colossyan"},{"t":"p","html":"5. Elai.io"},{"t":"p","html":"6. DeepBrain AI"},{"t":"p","html":"Compare them on: price, realism, interaction ability, multi-language support, platform compatibility (short video platforms), and customer support."},{"t":"p","html":"Give me a 'recommendation table.'\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3:<\/strong> Have AI run the numbers. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I want to livestream 8 hours a day using an AI avatar. Help me calculate:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Tool cost (monthly fee)","Content cost (time spent writing scripts)","Expected revenue (based on minimum conversion rate)","Payback period"]},{"t":"p","html":"Tell me whether it's worth investing in.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4:<\/strong> Ask AI for a <strong>pitfall checklist<\/strong>. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"List 10 common pitfalls in AI avatar livestreaming, for example:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Platform traffic limits (some platforms don't support AI avatars)","Stiff interaction (only reads scripts)","Unnatural appearance (uncanny valley effect)","Cost traps (looks cheap, but gets expensive to use)"]},{"t":"p","html":"Give a tip for avoiding each pitfall.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5:<\/strong> Get a <strong>launch plan<\/strong> from AI. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"If I decide to start AI avatar livestreaming, give me a 30-day launch plan:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Week 1: Choose tools and build the avatar","Week 2: Write scripts and test","Week 3: Official launch and data monitoring","Week 4: Optimize and improve"]},{"t":"p","html":"Tell me exactly what to do at each step.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Which one would you recommend most right now?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"If you want good value for money, try <strong>Synthesia<\/strong> (a great budget-friendly option) or <strong>HeyGen<\/strong> (very realistic). If you need strong interaction for e-commerce, <strong>D-ID's<\/strong> real-time conversational avatars do a good job. But remember, the tool is just the shell, the script is the soul. Even the best avatar is useless if it's reading a bad script."},{"t":"ms","items":["The core of choosing an avatar tool: <strong>scenario match<\/strong> + <strong>controllable cost<\/strong> + <strong>platform compatibility<\/strong>","Four main traps: <strong>traffic limits<\/strong>, <strong>stiff interaction<\/strong>, <strong>unnatural look<\/strong>, <strong>hidden costs<\/strong>","Recommendation: <strong>Synthesia<\/strong> for beginners, <strong>HeyGen/D-ID<\/strong> for advanced users","Key: spend <strong>70% of your effort<\/strong> writing a great script, and only <strong>30%<\/strong> choosing the tool"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":83,"title":"How can I use AI tools to analyze customer emotions?","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I heard there are AI tools that can read a customer's emotions, like telling if they're happy or angry just from their text. Is that really a thing? Would it help in sales?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Yes, and it's very useful. When a customer says \"let me think about it,\" the meaning changes completely depending on their mood. AI can help you <strong>hear what's behind the words<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's my <strong>AI Emotion Analysis Action Guide<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Pick the right tool.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"What AI tools can do sentiment analysis right now? Please recommend a few good for sales use:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. Text sentiment analysis (from chats or emails)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Voice sentiment analysis (from call recordings)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Video sentiment analysis (from meeting recordings)"},{"t":"p","html":"Give 1-2 tools for each, with pricing and features.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Have AI study past customers.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I have chat logs from 10 customers who bought and 10 who walked away. Please analyze:"},{"t":"ul","items":["What emotional keywords showed up in the last 3 conversations with customers who bought?","What emotional keywords showed up in the last 3 conversations with customers who left?","Are there any warning signs? (like words such as 'annoyed' or 'never mind')"]},{"t":"p","html":"Give me a comparison report.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Set up real-time monitoring.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I have a lot of conversations every day on a messaging app. How do I set up real-time emotion monitoring? Give me a plan:"},{"t":"ul","items":["What tool can connect to my messaging app","What keywords should trigger an alert","How should I get notified after an alert","How to track the emotion trend over time\""]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI create response scripts.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"If AI detects negative emotion from a customer (like 'angry' or 'disappointed'), how should I respond? Please write 3 types of responses:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Comfort type (empathize first)","Solution type (give a direct fix)","Mood-shift type (change the subject)"]},{"t":"p","html":"Keep them natural, not robotic.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Have AI do a weekly emotion review.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Review customer emotions once a week:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Which customer had the worst mood this week? Why?","Which customer had the best mood this week? What did I do right?","Is the overall trend going up or down?"]},{"t":"p","html":"Give me suggestions for next week.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"This kind of feels like spying. Won't customers feel offended?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"It's not about spying on customers, it's about <strong>understanding them better<\/strong>. It's like a doctor using a machine to monitor a patient's heart rate so they can treat them better. One of my students used this and noticed an old customer's replies getting shorter and colder. The AI flagged it as a <strong>churn risk<\/strong>. He immediately set up a lunch with the client and found out the company had a new boss and he was being pushed out. He stepped in right away and saved the account."},{"t":"ms","items":["Emotion is the <strong>\"ECG\"<\/strong> of sales","<strong>Five-step method<\/strong>: choose tools + historical analysis + real-time monitoring + response scripts + weekly review","Recommended tools: <strong>ChatGPT or Claude<\/strong> (via API) for text, <strong>Gong.io or CallMiner<\/strong> for voice","Goal: spot the <strong>signal<\/strong> before the customer walks away"]}],"minutes":4},{"n":84,"title":"Which AI tool writes the most human-sounding sales emails?","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Ethan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, when I use AI to write emails, customers reply saying, \"This was written by a machine, right?\" How do I get AI to write emails that sound like a real person?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"AI writes like a machine because your instructions are too \"machine-like.\" You need to teach it <strong>how to sound human<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's my <strong>six-step method for writing emails with a human touch<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Pick the right tool.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Which AI tool writes the most natural, human-sounding sales emails? Please compare:"},{"t":"ul","items":["ChatGPT (strong all-around, great natural tone)","Claude (excellent at sounding human and empathetic)","Gemini (good for long-form writing, integrates with Google Workspace)","Microsoft Copilot (great for professional tone, integrates with Outlook)"]},{"t":"p","html":"Give me your recommendation.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Give AI a persona.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I want you to act as a salesperson in the [XX industry], with a [sincere/funny/professional] personality, writing to [client name]. Remember these personal traits of mine: [for example, 'likes to use analogies', 'likes using respectful language']. Recall this persona before writing every email."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Give AI the background.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"The client is Morgan, a director at [XX company]. We previously talked about [topic]. He's recently been focused on [topic]. My goal for this email is [for example, 'set up a call']. Please write the email based on this background."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI write in a conversational tone.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please write this in a conversational way, like I'm chatting with him. Don't use formal or stiff language. Use natural, friendly connectors. Keep every sentence short."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Add personal touches.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please naturally work in these details:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Mention something he said last time","Mention something we both care about","Match his usual tone (if he likes being brief, keep it brief)"]},{"t":"p","html":"Make the email feel like it was written just for him.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 6: Fine-tune it yourself.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Here's the AI's first draft: [paste it]. Please point out what still sounds robotic, and how to make it sound more human."},{"t":"d","who":"Ethan","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Can you give me an example?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Instruction: \"Write an email to set up a call with the client, Leo. We previously talked about his company wanting to adopt a CRM system.\""},{"t":"p","html":"AI's first draft: \"Dear Mr. Leo, hello! I am a sales representative from XX Company. Regarding the CRM system we discussed previously, have you had a chance to consider it further? Looking forward to your reply.\""},{"t":"p","html":"After improving the instructions: \"Hi Leo! After we talked last week, I went back and really thought about your company's situation. You mentioned that messy sales data was your biggest headache, and we actually have a solution for exactly that. If you're free, how about 15 minutes next week so I can show you how it would work? Does Wednesday or Thursday work better for you?\""},{"t":"p","html":"Customer's reply: \"Wednesday afternoon works.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["AI writing with a <strong>human touch<\/strong> = persona + background + conversational tone + personal details","<strong>Six-step method<\/strong>: choose tool + give persona + give background + go conversational + personalize + fine-tune","Recommended tools: <strong>ChatGPT<\/strong> (all-around) + <strong>Claude<\/strong> (natural tone)","The key: make AI sound <strong>like you<\/strong>, not like AI"]}],"minutes":4},{"n":85,"title":"How to use AI tools for sales data visualization","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I have to put together sales reports every month, and honestly, Excel makes me want to scream. Is there any AI tool that can just generate charts for me automatically?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Data visualization isn't about making things \"look nice.\" It's about being able to spot problems at a glance. AI can turn boring numbers into charts that actually \"talk\" to you."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's an <strong>AI Data Visualization Five-Step Method<\/strong> for you:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Pick the right tool.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"What AI tools can I use for data visualization? Please recommend a few good options for sales work:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. Tools that auto-generate charts (like the AI features in <strong>Tableau<\/strong> or <strong>Power BI<\/strong>)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Tools that build charts from a single sentence (like <strong>ChatGPT with Code Interpreter<\/strong>)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Online tools (like <strong>Flourish<\/strong>, <strong>Datawrapper<\/strong>)"},{"t":"p","html":"4. Cloud-based BI tools (like <strong>Looker Studio<\/strong>, <strong>Power BI<\/strong>)"},{"t":"p","html":"Compare the pros, cons, and pricing of each.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Have AI analyze your data. Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Here's this month's sales data: [paste Excel table]. Please help me analyze:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Overall completion rate","Month-over-month or year-over-year changes","Best and worst performing salesperson","Best and worst performing product","Best and worst performing region"]},{"t":"p","html":"Summarize <strong>3 core insights<\/strong> in plain language.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Ask AI to suggest the right charts.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Based on these insights, please suggest which charts to use:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Performance trends: <strong>line chart<\/strong>","Product share: <strong>pie chart<\/strong>","Sales rankings: <strong>bar chart<\/strong>","Regional breakdown: <strong>map<\/strong>"]},{"t":"p","html":"Give a title and key focus for each chart.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI generate the visualization code or steps.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please write Python code using <strong>matplotlib<\/strong> to create a 'Monthly Performance Trend Chart' with this data: [data]. Or, if I'm using <strong>Flourish<\/strong>, walk me through the steps instead."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Have AI turn it into a data story.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please combine the charts and insights above into a <strong>one-page Sales Data Brief<\/strong> that I can send straight to my boss. It should include:"},{"t":"ul","items":["A one-sentence conclusion","3 key charts","3 action recommendations"]},{"t":"p","html":"Keep the layout clean and easy to read.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"What if I don't know how to code in Python?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"You don't need to. You can use drag-and-drop online tools like <strong>Looker Studio<\/strong> or <strong>Flourish<\/strong>. Or just use <strong>ChatGPT's Code Interpreter<\/strong>. Upload your Excel file, and it'll generate the charts for you directly."},{"t":"ms","items":["The point of data visualization isn't \"making pretty pictures,\" it's <strong>finding problems<\/strong>","The five-step method: <strong>pick a tool + AI analysis + chart suggestions + generate output + build a report<\/strong>","Recommended tools: <strong>Flourish<\/strong> for beginners, <strong>ChatGPT Code Interpreter<\/strong> for advanced users","Goal: Produce a chart that \"speaks for itself\" in <strong>5 minutes<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":86,"title":"Speech-to-text tool recommendations for logging client calls fast","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I make a ton of calls every day, but I can never remember the key points. Is there an AI tool that can turn calls into text and pull out the main takeaways automatically?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"There is, and honestly, these tools are pretty solid now. You can just focus on the conversation and let AI handle the note-taking."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's an <strong>AI Call Recording Five-Step Method<\/strong> for you:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Pick the right tool.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"What speech-to-text tools work well for sales calls? Please compare:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. <strong>Otter.ai<\/strong> (excellent accuracy, popular for meetings and calls)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. <strong>Fireflies.ai<\/strong> (great for call recording and CRM integration)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. <strong>Zoom's built-in transcription<\/strong> (convenient if you already use Zoom)"},{"t":"p","html":"4. <strong>Microsoft 365 Copilot<\/strong> (good if you're in the Microsoft ecosystem)"},{"t":"p","html":"5. <strong>Rev.com<\/strong> (very high accuracy, good for professional transcription)"},{"t":"p","html":"Compare accuracy, price, real-time transcription support, export options, and whether it can pull out key points.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Set up automatic recording.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I mostly take calls through a messaging app and my phone. How do I set up automatic recording and transcription? Please give me a simple plan:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Phone calls: what app can auto-record (like a call recorder app)","Messaging app calls: how to record them (screen recording plus microphone)","How to auto-upload the recordings to a transcription tool"]},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it simple and quick, nothing time-consuming.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI pull out the key points.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Here's the transcript from a call: [paste text]. Please help me extract:"},{"t":"ul","items":["What the client said (pain points, needs, concerns)","What I said (promises, proposals)","Next steps (to-do items)","Key emotional moments"]},{"t":"p","html":"Put it in list form so it's easy to scan.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI draft a follow-up email.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Based on what we just pulled out, please write a follow-up email to the client confirming what we discussed today and the next steps. Keep it conversational, like it's actually me talking."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Archive it for learning.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Every week, archive my call recordings and key takeaways. At the end of the month, have AI analyze:"},{"t":"ul","items":["The questions clients ask most often","Where I tend to get stuck","What successful calls have in common"]},{"t":"p","html":"Generate a <strong>Call Skills Improvement Report<\/strong>.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So I wouldn't have to take notes while I'm on the phone anymore?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. One of our students uses <strong>Otter.ai<\/strong> plus an AI note-taking app. After every call, AI automatically transcribes it, pulls out the key points, and builds a to-do list. He told me, \"I used to spend half an hour organizing notes after each call. Now it takes five minutes, and I use that extra time to make three more calls.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["The point of call recording: <strong>free up your attention<\/strong> so you can focus on the conversation","The five-step method: <strong>pick a tool + auto-record + AI summary + generate follow-up + archive for learning<\/strong>","Recommended tools: <strong>an accurate transcription app<\/strong> + <strong>a free AI note-taking tool<\/strong>","Goal: By the time the call ends, <strong>your to-do list is already done<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":4},{"n":87,"title":"How can I use AI tools to automatically generate a weekly sales report?","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Frank","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, writing a weekly report is so painful. I have to remember what I did, who I met, and how many deals I closed. Is there an AI that can just generate this for me?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"The real purpose of a weekly report is to <strong>report upward<\/strong>, not to keep a diary. AI can help you turn a \"list of things I did\" into a \"report that shows value.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Here's a <strong>Five-Step Method for Automating Weekly Reports with AI<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Set up your data sources.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"What data sources do I need to automatically generate a weekly report? Please list them:"},{"t":"ul","items":["CRM system (client follow-up records)","Call logs (how many calls made)","Messaging app history (key conversations)","Calendar (scheduled meetings)","Performance data (sales closed)"]},{"t":"p","html":"How can I sync all this data into one place automatically?\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Have AI combine the data.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please help me design an automated process:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Every Friday at 5 PM","Export this week's follow-up records from the CRM","Export this week's call time from the phone tool","Export this week's meetings from the calendar","Export this week's closed deals from the sales system"]},{"t":"p","html":"Combine all of this into one data package.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI write the first draft.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Here's this week's data package: [paste]. Please generate a weekly report with this structure:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. This week's key results (numbers and highlights)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Progress on 3 key clients"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Problems encountered"},{"t":"p","html":"4. Next week's plan"},{"t":"p","html":"Use language my boss likes: short, backed by data, and clear on conclusions.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI polish the wording.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please rewrite this report in three styles:"},{"t":"p","html":"A. Upward report style (formal, data-heavy)"},{"t":"p","html":"B. Team sharing style (relaxed, experience-based)"},{"t":"p","html":"C. Personal reflection style (honest, thoughtful)"},{"t":"p","html":"I'll pick whichever fits the situation.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Set up auto-sending.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"How do I set this up to auto-generate and send every Friday? For example, using Zapier or a workflow automation tool to connect my CRM, AI, and email. Give me specific steps."},{"t":"d","who":"Frank","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So I never have to write weekly reports on Sunday night again."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our teams uses <strong>Zapier + ChatGPT<\/strong>. Every Friday afternoon, it automatically pulls the data, writes the report, and sends it to the boss's inbox. The salesperson just spends two minutes checking it, and if it looks good, they send it as is. They told me, \"The weekly report went from being a burden to just something that happens on its own.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["The point of a weekly report: not to <strong>list what you did<\/strong>, but to <strong>show your value<\/strong>","Five-step method: <strong>build data sources<\/strong>, <strong>combine data<\/strong>, <strong>generate a draft<\/strong>, <strong>polish the wording<\/strong>, <strong>automate sending<\/strong>","Automation tools: <strong>Zapier<\/strong>, <strong>workflow automation platforms<\/strong>, <strong>low-code data platforms<\/strong>","Goal: get your weekly report done in <strong>5 minutes<\/strong>"]},{"t":"p","html":"---"}],"minutes":3},{"n":88,"title":"Which AI tool works best for managing a sales calendar?","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I have to remember to call clients, send emails, and book meetings every day, and I keep forgetting things. Is there an AI calendar that can schedule and remind me automatically?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Time management for salespeople isn't about <strong>memory<\/strong>, it's about <strong>having a system<\/strong>. An AI calendar can take all your scattered tasks and organize them for you automatically."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's an <strong>AI Smart Calendar Selection Guide<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Figure out what you need.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"What kind of calendar tool does a salesperson need? Please list the core features:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Auto-scheduling meetings (based on both sides' free time)","Smart reminders (advance notice, priority levels)","CRM sync (linked to client info)","History tracking (who, when, what was discussed)","Easy to use on mobile"]},{"t":"p","html":"Rank these by importance.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Compare the main tools.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please compare these calendar tools and score them for sales use:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. Google Calendar (global standard)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Microsoft Outlook Calendar (integrated with Office)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Calendly (built for booking meetings)"},{"t":"p","html":"4. Built-in CRM calendars (like HubSpot or Salesforce)"},{"t":"p","html":"Compare on: auto-scheduling, smart reminders, CRM sync, price, and ease of use.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Ask AI to recommend a combination.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I do a lot of communication on a messaging app and also use a CRM. Please recommend a calendar setup:"},{"t":"ul","items":["What should I use for my own schedule?","What should I use to book meetings with clients?","How do I connect it to my messaging app?","How do I sync it with my CRM?\""]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI build a usage SOP.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Say I'm using Google Calendar plus Calendly. Please give me an SOP:"},{"t":"ul","items":["How to set my free time","How to send clients a link to book a meeting","How to sync it to the CRM","How to set reminders (1 day before, 1 hour before)","How to review how efficiently I'm using my calendar\""]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Have AI find your time black holes.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please look at my calendar from the past month and tell me:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Which clients I spent the most time on","Which times of day I'm most productive","Which meetings were a waste of time","How to improve next week\""]},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"I'm just using my phone's default calendar right now. Is that good enough?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"It's good enough, but it's not <strong>smart<\/strong> enough. For example, a basic calendar won't tell you \"this client needs a follow-up today,\" and it won't schedule meetings around both sides' availability. Our team now uses <strong>Google Calendar + Calendly<\/strong>. Clients click a link, pick a time, and it syncs to the calendar and sends reminders automatically. Booking a meeting used to take five back-and-forth emails. Now it takes one minute."},{"t":"ms","items":["The core of a smart calendar: <strong>automation<\/strong>, <strong>reminders<\/strong>, and <strong>syncing<\/strong>","Recommended combo: <strong>Google Calendar<\/strong> (daily use) + <strong>Calendly<\/strong> (for booking meetings)","The key shift: from <strong>\"I need to remember\"<\/strong> to <strong>\"the system reminds me\"<\/strong>","Goal: never miss a follow-up again"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":89,"title":"How Can I Use AI Tools to Monitor Competitors?","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I want to know what my competitors are doing at all times, but I don't have time to check their websites every day. Is there an AI tool that can monitor them automatically?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Competitor monitoring isn't about \"watching your rivals.\" It's about \"catching opportunities.\" AI can watch them for you 24 hours a day. All you need to do is check the results."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's a <strong>five-step method to build an AI competitor monitoring system<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Make a monitoring checklist.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I have the following competitors: [list]. Please help me list what I should monitor for each one:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Website updates (new products, case studies)","Content channels and social media (activity)","Job postings (what roles they're hiring for, to spot direction)","Funding news (to track capital moves)","Customer reviews (to see how reputation is shifting)","Price changes"]},{"t":"p","html":"Suggest a monitoring frequency for each channel.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Pick your monitoring tools.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"What tools can I use for competitor monitoring? Please recommend:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. Public sentiment monitoring tools"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Website monitoring tools"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Social media monitoring tools"},{"t":"p","html":"4. AI aggregation tools (RSS feeds plus AI summaries)"},{"t":"p","html":"Compare their price and features.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI set up monitoring keywords.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please help me set up monitoring keywords, including:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Competitor brand names (full name and short name)","Competitor's core product names","Names of the competitor's founder/CEO","Industry keywords combined with competitor names"]},{"t":"p","html":"Set an alert rule for each keyword, for example, trigger an alert if it shows up three times in one day.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI generate a daily/weekly report.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Every morning at 8 AM, have AI summarize yesterday's competitor activity into a brief report that includes:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Important updates (marked in red)","Impact on us (one sentence)","Suggested response (optional)"]},{"t":"p","html":"Keep the format short, something I can read in one minute.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Have AI analyze trends.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Once a month, have AI analyze competitor trends:"},{"t":"ul","items":["What are they pushing hard right now?","How are customer opinions of them changing?","What might their next move be?","Where's our opportunity?"]},{"t":"p","html":"Generate a strategy reference report.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"With all these tools, won't it get expensive?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"You can start cheap. Use RSS to follow competitor websites and content channels, then have AI summarize it once a week. One of our students used this exact method. She noticed a competitor was heavily hiring for a certain technical role, guessed they were about to launch a new product, prepared ahead of time, and signed several big clients before the competitor even released it."},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>Core of competitor monitoring<\/strong>: it's not about \"watching rivals,\" it's about \"finding opportunities\"","<strong>Five-step method<\/strong>: monitoring checklist + choosing tools + setting keywords + daily/weekly reports + trend analysis","<strong>Low-cost option<\/strong>: RSS feeds plus AI summaries","<strong>Goal<\/strong>: know the moment a competitor makes a move"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":90,"title":"Can AI Tools Help Review Sales Contracts?","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, a client sent over a contract, and I don't understand some of the terms. I'm scared to sign it blindly. Can AI help me review it?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Salespeople aren't lawyers, but you still need a feel for the key terms. AI can act as your \"legal assistant\" and help you spot the landmines."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's a <strong>five-step AI contract review method<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Choose the right tool.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"What AI tools can help review contracts? Please recommend:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. Legal AI platforms (like Ironclad, LawGeex, Lexion)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Writing assistants for proofreading (like Grammarly)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Specialized contract review AI tools (like Spellbook, ClauseBuddy)"},{"t":"p","html":"4. ChatGPT/Claude (general purpose, needs specific instructions)"},{"t":"p","html":"Compare them on: whether they understand legal language, price, and ease of use.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Have AI review key clauses.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Here's a contract [paste the key terms]. Please review the following:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. Payment terms (Are they favorable to us? Any hidden traps?)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Delivery terms (Are the timelines and standards clear?)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Breach of contract clauses (Is the compensation reasonable?)"},{"t":"p","html":"4. Confidentiality terms (Are there excessive demands?)"},{"t":"p","html":"5. Dispute resolution (Where would a lawsuit be filed? Is that favorable to us?)"},{"t":"p","html":"Mark each clause's risk level as red, yellow, or green, and give me revision suggestions.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI generate a revised version.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Based on the review above, generate revised clauses. Use professional wording, but try to keep the original intent. Add notes next to each change explaining why it was made."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI prepare talking points for explanation.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"If the client asks 'why do you want to change this clause,' help me prepare an explanation. Frame it from the client's point of view (for example, 'this protects both sides'), so we don't come across as nitpicking."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Have AI do a final check before signing.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Before signing, help me run a final checklist:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Is the other company's name correct?","Do the written and numerical amounts match?","Is there any ambiguity about where to stamp the seal?","Is the date correct?","Are all attachments included?"]},{"t":"p","html":"Make sure nothing's missing.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"That way I can review it myself first."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our students used Grammarly plus ChatGPT to review contracts before sending them to legal. The legal team told him, \"The contracts you send now are much better quality. It saves me half the time.\" Remember: AI doesn't replace your legal team. It just helps you clear the landmines first."},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>Core of contract review<\/strong>: it's not about \"understanding everything,\" it's about \"clearing landmines\"","<strong>Five-step method<\/strong>: choose tools + review clauses + generate revisions + prepare explanation talking points + pre-signing check","<strong>Recommended tools<\/strong>: professional legal databases (like Ironclad or LawGeex) plus AI writing assistants","<strong>Goal<\/strong>: get your legal team to say you \"know your stuff\""]}],"minutes":3},{"n":91,"title":"How can I use AI tools for sales training?","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, our new team members take forever to get up to speed, and training costs are eating us alive. Is there an AI tool that can help with sales training?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"The core of AI training is <strong>practice anytime, feedback right away<\/strong>, not sitting through long lectures. You can build an <strong>AI sales sparring partner<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you a <strong>five-step AI sales training system<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Build a case library.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"We have 50 past sales cases, both successes and failures. Please help me organize them into training material:"},{"t":"p","html":"Break down each case into: background, customer problem, sales actions, results, and review."},{"t":"p","html":"Sort them by scenario (lead generation, handling objections, closing, etc.)."},{"t":"p","html":"Pull out the <strong>key winning move<\/strong> from each case."},{"t":"p","html":"Put it all together into a case library.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Build a script library.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"We have scripts for common situations. Please organize them into a trainable format:"},{"t":"p","html":"Scenario: The customer says it's too expensive."},{"t":"p","html":"Give 3 standard scripts."},{"t":"p","html":"List 2 common mistakes."},{"t":"p","html":"Practice points: pay attention to tone and timing."},{"t":"p","html":"Put it together into a script library.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI play the customer.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please act as a <strong>difficult customer<\/strong> who is suspicious by nature. A new hire is going to try to sell you a product. Start the conversation. After each thing the new hire says, give feedback on:"},{"t":"p","html":"What they did well."},{"t":"p","html":"What they could improve."},{"t":"p","html":"What a <strong>top performer<\/strong> would say instead."},{"t":"p","html":"Let the new hire learn by doing.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI run scenario simulations.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please generate 20 sales scenario questions. Each one should include:"},{"t":"p","html":"A description of the scenario."},{"t":"p","html":"What the customer actually says."},{"t":"p","html":"3 options (A/B/C)."},{"t":"p","html":"The correct answer with an explanation."},{"t":"p","html":"Use this to test new hires.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Have AI generate a personal growth report.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"New hire Taylor just finished one week of training. Based on their practice records, generate a growth report covering:"},{"t":"p","html":"Their strengths (which scenarios they handle well)."},{"t":"p","html":"Their weak spots (which scenarios they keep messing up)."},{"t":"p","html":"Specific suggestions for improvement (what to practice and how)."},{"t":"p","html":"A training plan for next week.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Jamie","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"Can this replace real human training?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Not completely, but it can take a huge load off your shoulders. One team I know used an AI sparring partner, with new hires spending 30 minutes a day practicing with it. Within a week, their real-world performance jumped noticeably. They told me, \"Before, I was too scared of messing up to even ask questions. Now that I've practiced with AI so much, real customers don't rattle me anymore.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>Core of AI training:<\/strong> practice anytime plus instant feedback","<strong>The five-step system:<\/strong> case library, script library, AI roleplay, scenario simulations, growth report","<strong>The key:<\/strong> let new hires make mistakes in a <strong>safe environment<\/strong>","<strong>The goal:<\/strong> cut new hire ramp-up time by <strong>50 percent<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":92,"title":"Which AI tool works best for sales team collaboration?","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, our team runs everything through a messaging app, but there are so many messages that we keep missing important stuff. Is there an AI tool that can make team collaboration more efficient?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"The core of team collaboration is <strong>keeping information in sync<\/strong> and <strong>making tasks clear<\/strong>. AI can turn the chaos in your group chats into something organized."},{"t":"p","html":"Let me give you a guide for choosing the right <strong>AI collaboration tool<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Identify your team's pain points.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"What are the common pain points in sales team collaboration? Please list things like:"},{"t":"p","html":"Important messages getting buried in the flood."},{"t":"p","html":"Unclear tasks (nobody knows who's responsible for what)."},{"t":"p","html":"Progress falling out of sync (nobody knows where a deal stands)."},{"t":"p","html":"Files getting messy (too many versions floating around)."},{"t":"p","html":"Meetings that go nowhere (might as well not have happened)."},{"t":"p","html":"Rank these by how serious they are.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Compare the major tools.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please compare these team collaboration tools and score them for how well they fit a sales team:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. Microsoft 365 (Teams, Docs, Outlook, Copilot)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Google Workspace (Docs, Meet, Gmail, Gemini)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Slack (chat-based collaboration, integrates with CRM)"},{"t":"p","html":"4. HubSpot (built-in collaboration for sales teams)"},{"t":"p","html":"5. Trello/Asana (task management)"},{"t":"p","html":"6. Notion (knowledge base and collaboration)"},{"t":"p","html":"Compare them on price, ease of use, AI features, whether they connect with a messaging app, and CRM integration.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI design a collaboration SOP.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Let's say we go with Google Workspace. Please design a collaboration SOP for a sales team:"},{"t":"p","html":"Daily communication: what to use (team groups)."},{"t":"p","html":"Customer follow-ups: how to keep everyone updated (shared docs/sheets)."},{"t":"p","html":"Task assignment: how to manage it (shared task boards)."},{"t":"p","html":"Meetings: how to run them (video meetings plus transcripts)."},{"t":"p","html":"Knowledge base: how to build it (cloud docs)."},{"t":"p","html":"Be specific for every part of this.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI create a daily information summary.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Before everyone logs off each day, have the AI scan through all the team's communication records and put together a 'Today's Highlights' report covering:"},{"t":"p","html":"Key customer updates."},{"t":"p","html":"Issues that need my attention."},{"t":"p","html":"Reminders for anything still pending."},{"t":"p","html":"Post it in the group so nothing slips through the cracks.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Have AI analyze collaboration efficiency.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Each week, have the AI analyze the team's collaboration data and offer suggestions like:"},{"t":"p","html":"Who's slowest to reply (might be overloaded)."},{"t":"p","html":"Which group chats have too much noise (might need to be split up)."},{"t":"p","html":"Which tasks keep getting delayed (a sign of a process problem)."},{"t":"p","html":"Whether meeting times are actually reasonable.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"Sales Manager","sifu":false,"html":"We're using a messaging app right now. Should we switch to something else?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"A messaging app is good for <strong>chatting<\/strong>, but it's not built for <strong>collaborating<\/strong>. I'd suggest using WhatsApp Business (or your CRM's built-in messaging) for client-facing chats, paired with Google Workspace or Microsoft 365 for internal document collaboration. My own team uses WhatsApp Business for clients, and Google Docs for everything internal. With AI pulling together a summary every day, nobody has to ask \"so what's going on with that customer\" anymore."},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>Core of team collaboration:<\/strong> synced information plus clear tasks","<strong>Recommended combo:<\/strong> business messaging (external) plus cloud docs (internal) plus AI summaries","<strong>The key:<\/strong> let AI act as your <strong>information secretary<\/strong>","<strong>The goal:<\/strong> boost team efficiency by <strong>30 percent<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":4},{"n":93,"title":"How to Use AI Tools for Sales Forecasting","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Lina","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, we do sales forecasts every quarter, but honestly we're just guessing. It's never accurate. Are there AI tools that can help us make better predictions?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Sales forecasting isn't fortune-telling, it's <strong>deduction based on data<\/strong>. AI can help you turn \"guessing\" into \"calculating probability.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Here's my <strong>five-step AI sales forecasting method<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Organize your historical data.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"We have sales data from the past three years, including monthly revenue, lead volume, conversion rates, average order value, and industry breakdown. Please help me organize this into a format suitable for forecasting. What fields do I need?"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Choose a forecasting tool.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"What AI tools can do sales forecasting? Please recommend:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. CRM built-in AI (like major CRM platforms)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Data analysis tools (like the forecasting features in Tableau or Power BI)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. General AI (ChatGPT Code Interpreter, requires uploading data)"},{"t":"p","html":"4. Professional forecasting tools (like IBM SPSS or cloud-based machine learning)"},{"t":"p","html":"Compare them by: whether coding is needed, price, and accuracy.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI build a prediction model.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"I have 36 months of sales data: [Paste]. Please help me with:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. <strong>Time series forecasting<\/strong> (next quarter's sales)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. <strong>Factor analysis<\/strong> (what factors affect sales the most)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. <strong>Range prediction<\/strong> (minimum and maximum range)"},{"t":"p","html":"4. <strong>Confidence level<\/strong> explanation"},{"t":"p","html":"Explain everything in plain language anyone can understand.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI generate a prediction report.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please turn the prediction results into a report for my boss, including:"},{"t":"ul","items":["<strong>Core conclusion<\/strong>: Projected next quarter sales of XX, plus or minus 10%","<strong>Main basis<\/strong>: Historical trends plus seasonal factors","<strong>Risk alert<\/strong>: If XX happens, the target may need to be lowered","<strong>Action recommendation<\/strong>: What to do right now"]},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it to one page, clear at a glance.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Have AI handle rolling updates.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Once new data comes in each month, update the prediction automatically. Please design an automated workflow:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Pull data from the CRM on the 1st of each month","Feed it to AI for a new prediction","Generate a new report","Send it to the management group chat\""]},{"t":"d","who":"Lina","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So we don't need quarterly forecasting meetings anymore?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"You'll still need the meetings, but now you're discussing \"AI's prediction\" and \"market changes\" instead of \"I guess this, you guess that.\" One of our clients used AI for forecasting and their accuracy jumped from <strong>60% to 85%<\/strong>. The sales director told me, \"Finally, I don't have to explain to the boss why the numbers are so far off.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["The core of sales forecasting: it's not about <strong>guessing<\/strong>, it's about <strong>calculating<\/strong>","<strong>Five-step method<\/strong>: organize data, choose a tool, build a model, generate a report, roll it forward","<strong>Recommended tools<\/strong>: CRM built-in AI + ChatGPT Code Interpreter","<strong>Goal<\/strong>: boost prediction accuracy by <strong>20%<\/strong>"]},{"t":"p","html":"---"}],"minutes":3},{"n":94,"title":"Which AI Tool Is Best for Managing Sales Leads?","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, the leads we get every day come from all over, some fill out forms, some add us on a messaging app, some call in. It's a mess. How can I use AI to manage all of this in one place?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"The core of lead management is <strong>don't lose them, don't mess them up, don't duplicate them<\/strong>. AI can turn that \"messy flow\" into an \"orderly pipeline.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Here's an <strong>AI Lead Management Tool Selection Guide<\/strong> for you:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Identify your lead sources.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"What are our lead sources? Please help me classify them:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Online channels (website forms, content channels, ads)","Offline channels (exhibitions, events, business cards)","Social channels (messaging apps, business messaging, social feeds)","Referrals"]},{"t":"p","html":"What are the characteristics of each source? How should each be handled?\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Compare lead management tools.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please compare these lead management tools and score them for sales team suitability:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. CRM systems (Salesforce, etc.)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Lightweight tools (low-code platforms)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Spreadsheet tools plus AI (Excel or online docs plus AI)"},{"t":"p","html":"4. Marketing automation tools (HubSpot, etc.)"},{"t":"p","html":"Compare them on: price, ease of use, automation, integration with a messaging app, and AI features.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI design a lead scoring system.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please help me design a lead scoring model:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Company size (large company: +10 points)","Job title (decision-maker: +20 points)","Source (referral: +15 points)","Behavior (opened email: +5 points, multiple visits: +10 points)","Clarity of need (asked for a quote: +20 points)"]},{"t":"p","html":"Total score out of 100. AI scores each lead automatically. Anything above 80 points gets followed up on immediately.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI remove duplicate leads.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"How can I use AI to automatically remove duplicate leads? For example, if the same customer comes in through multiple channels, they should be merged into one. Please give me a plan."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Have AI generate a daily lead report.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Every morning, have AI generate a daily lead report with:"},{"t":"ul","items":["New leads from yesterday (total count plus high-score leads)","Leads needing follow-up (no contact in over 24 hours)","Dormant leads to wake up (no interaction in over 30 days)","Today's suggestions (who to prioritize)"]},{"t":"p","html":"Send it to the sales group chat.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Mia","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"We're still using Excel right now. Can we upgrade?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"You can start with a low-code tool like Airtable, or the smart tables built into your office apps, both come with some automation features already. Once your team grows, you can move up to a full CRM. One of our teams switched to Airtable plus AI, with automatic scoring, assignment, and reminders, and their lead follow-up rate <strong>tripled<\/strong>."},{"t":"ms","items":["Core of lead management: <strong>don't lose, don't mess up, don't duplicate<\/strong>","<strong>Recommended tools<\/strong>: Airtable (entry-level) + a professional CRM + AI scoring","Key move: let AI help you <strong>set priorities<\/strong>","<strong>Goal<\/strong>: boost lead conversion rate by <strong>50%<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":95,"title":"How can I use AI tools to automatically follow up with customers?","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I have too many customers to follow up with every day. I keep forgetting one or missing another. Is there an AI that can follow up automatically for me?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Automatic follow-up doesn't mean letting a robot spam customers randomly. It means reminding the right person, at the right time, in the right way. Think of AI as your <strong>follow-up assistant<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's a <strong>six-step system for AI automatic follow-up<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Set your follow-up rules.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Help me design a set of follow-up rules:"},{"t":"ul","items":["<strong>New leads<\/strong>: Send a welcome message within 1 hour","<strong>Interested customers<\/strong> (score 80+): Follow up once a day","<strong>General customers<\/strong> (score 60 to 80): Send valuable content every 3 days","<strong>Dormant customers<\/strong> (no contact for 30 days): Send a re-engagement message every 2 weeks","<strong>Closed deals<\/strong>: Follow up once a month"]},{"t":"p","html":"Also specify the follow-up method (messaging app, email, or phone) for each scenario.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Pick your automation tools.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"What tools can automate follow-ups? Please recommend:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. <strong>Enterprise messaging apps with helper tools<\/strong> (for auto-replies and tag-based triggers)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. <strong>Email automation<\/strong> (Mailchimp, Sendinblue)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. <strong>CRM built-in workflows<\/strong> (standard CRM platforms)"},{"t":"p","html":"4. <strong>Marketing automation platforms<\/strong> (HubSpot, ActiveCampaign)"},{"t":"p","html":"5. <strong>RPA tools<\/strong> (like UiPath, which can mimic manual actions)"},{"t":"p","html":"Compare the pros and cons of each.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI write the follow-up content.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please generate follow-up content templates for these situations:"},{"t":"ul","items":["<strong>New customer welcome message<\/strong> (3 different styles)","<strong>Holiday greetings<\/strong> (New Year, Mid-Autumn, Christmas, etc.)","<strong>Value sharing<\/strong> (industry news, useful tips)","<strong>Re-engagement message<\/strong> (haven't talked in a while)","<strong>Birthday wishes<\/strong>"]},{"t":"p","html":"Each template should be easy to personalize with the customer's name and company.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Set up your trigger conditions.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"In my automation tool, how do I set up these automatic triggers:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Send a welcome message automatically when a customer adds me","Send matching content when a customer's tag changes","Trigger a re-engagement message if a customer goes silent for XX days","Alert the sales rep when a customer clicks a link"]},{"t":"p","html":"Give me the exact steps to set this up.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Have AI set up manual intervention alerts.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"When a customer does any of the following, alert the sales rep to step in personally:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Asks a complicated question","Shows negative emotion","Shows strong buying intent","Asks for a phone call"]},{"t":"p","html":"Each alert should include the customer's background and a suggested response.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 6: Have AI review how well the follow-ups are working.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Every month, have AI analyze the results of the automated follow-ups:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Which messages had the highest open rates","Which customers got reactivated","Which rules need adjusting"]},{"t":"p","html":"Then generate suggestions for improvement.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So I won't have to wake up every day wondering who I need to contact."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our teams uses an enterprise messaging app plus a lead management tool and runs more than 50 automatic follow-up rules. Salespeople just check the <strong>high-value tasks<\/strong> AI picks out for them each day. They told me, \"Before, customers used to chase us. Now we're faster than they are.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["The core of automatic follow-up: <strong>rules + content + triggers + human backup<\/strong>","The six-step method: <strong>set rules, choose tools, write content, set triggers, manual alerts, review and improve<\/strong>","Recommended tools: <strong>enterprise messaging app + lead management tool<\/strong>","The goal: let AI <strong>remember<\/strong> every single customer for you"]},{"t":"p","html":"---"}],"minutes":4},{"n":96,"title":"How do I use AI tools to write a sales review report?","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, the hardest part of every month is writing the sales review report. I have to dig through piles of data and write thousands of words. Is there an AI that can just generate it for me?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"A review report isn't really about \"writing.\" It's about <strong>thinking clearly<\/strong>. AI can turn your raw data into insights. All you need to do is figure out what to do next."},{"t":"p","html":"Here's a <strong>five-step method for generating AI review reports<\/strong>:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 1: Pull together your data sources.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"What data do I need for a review report? Please list:"},{"t":"ul","items":["<strong>Performance data<\/strong> (this month's sales, target completion rate)","<strong>Process data<\/strong> (lead volume, conversion rate, average order value)","<strong>Team data<\/strong> (individual performance)","<strong>Customer data<\/strong> (ratio of new to existing customers, industry breakdown)","<strong>Market data<\/strong> (competitor moves, industry trends)"]},{"t":"p","html":"Tell me how to pull this data out of my CRM and Excel sheets.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 2: Have AI analyze the data.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Here's this month's data: [Paste]. Please help me analyze:"},{"t":"ul","items":["<strong>Overall performance<\/strong> (compared with last month and the same period last year)","<strong>Highlights<\/strong> (what went well)","<strong>Weak spots<\/strong> (what stood out as problems)","<strong>Root causes<\/strong> (why things went well or poorly)"]},{"t":"p","html":"Back everything up with data and facts.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 3: Have AI write the first draft.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Based on the analysis above, write a full review report with this structure:"},{"t":"p","html":"1. Core conclusions for the month (3 sentences)"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Performance overview (charts and text)"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Highlights (2 to 3 points)"},{"t":"p","html":"4. Problems (2 to 3 points)"},{"t":"p","html":"5. Root cause analysis"},{"t":"p","html":"6. Improvement plan for next month"},{"t":"p","html":"Make it look professional, something I can send straight to my boss.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 4: Have AI pull out the \"golden lines.\"<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Pull out 3 headline-worthy lines from the report that I could put on the cover page. For example:"},{"t":"ul","items":["'This month's growth mainly came from repeat business with existing clients'","'The new channel outperformed expectations, let's invest more next month'","'The drop in conversion rate points to gaps in training'"]},{"t":"p","html":"Make sure the boss can spot the key points at a glance.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Step 5: Have AI create individual reports.<\/strong> Use this prompt:"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please create a personal review report for each salesperson, covering:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Their performance ranking","What they did well","What they need to improve","Their goal for next month"]},{"t":"p","html":"Keep it personal and motivating.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Sam","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So now I won't have to pull all-nighters to finish my report."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One of our sales directors uses this exact method. He now delivers his report on the 10th of every month, without fail. It used to take him two full days, now it takes just 2 hours. His boss told him, \"Your report is the clearest one I get.\""},{"t":"ms","items":["The core of a review report: it's not about <strong>writing<\/strong>, it's about <strong>thinking<\/strong>","The five-step method: <strong>pull data, analyze it, draft the report, extract golden lines, build individual versions<\/strong>","The key: let AI be the <strong>data analyst<\/strong>, while you play the <strong>strategist<\/strong>","The goal: a high-quality report done in <strong>2 hours<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":4},{"n":97,"title":"10 Most Useful AI Sales Prompt Templates","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Pat","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, you've given me so many prompts already. Can you just give me a full \"collection of common prompts\" that I can copy and use right away?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Of course. Let me put together an <strong>\"Essential AI Sales Prompt Toolbox\"<\/strong> for you, organized by scenario. You can just copy and paste these directly."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Scenario 1: Writing a cold email<\/strong>"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please help me write an email to [Client Name], who works at [Company, Title]. We [have/have not] interacted before. Our company sells [Product], which can help solve their [Pain Point]. Make the email conversational, sincere, and engaging. End with a suggestion for a next step (a call or meeting). Don't use generic phrases."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Scenario 2: Handling a client who says \"You're too expensive\"<\/strong>"},{"t":"prompt","html":"The client said, 'You're too expensive.' Our price is [X], and the competitor's price is [Y]. Our advantages are [list 3 points]. Please generate 3 different responses: 1. <strong>Value comparison<\/strong>; 2. <strong>Risk avoidance<\/strong>; 3. <strong>Cost breakdown<\/strong>. Keep it conversational, not like a sales pitch."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Scenario 3: Analyzing a client's social media posts<\/strong>"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Here's client [Name]'s recent social media content: [Paste]. Please analyze their interests, concerns, and personality traits, and suggest 3 topics I could use to start a conversation."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Scenario 4: Writing a thank-you message<\/strong>"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Client [Name] just [did something, e.g., referred a new client/signed a deal]. Please write a thank-you message that's sincere and specific, mentioning [a shared memory or detail] between us. Keep it around 200 words."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Scenario 5: Writing a short video script<\/strong>"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please write a 60-second short video script on the topic of [Pain Point]. The target audience is [Description]. Structure: grab attention in the first 3 seconds ('Still struggling with XX?'), talk about the pain point and lead into the solution, then end by encouraging people to follow or message me. Keep it conversational and vivid."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Scenario 6: Practicing client objections<\/strong>"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please act as a [difficult/hesitant] client. I'm going to try selling you [Product]. Start the conversation. After each of my responses, tell me what I did well and what I could improve, and show me how a top salesperson would say it instead."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Scenario 7: Asking for referrals<\/strong>"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Client [Name] is very happy with our service. Please write a script asking them for a referral that doesn't feel awkward. It should: acknowledge their satisfaction, explain why a referral matters, make a low-pressure request (like 'just share my contact with a friend'), and promise to thank them."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Scenario 8: Improving a sales presentation<\/strong>"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Here's my presentation outline: [Paste]. Please improve the structure using the <strong>Problem, Cause, Solution, Evidence, Action<\/strong> framework. Give me the key point and transition line for each slide."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Scenario 9: Writing a social media post<\/strong>"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Please write a social media post about [product/industry insight/personal reflection]. Make it feel natural and warm, not like a hard sell. Keep it around 100 words, and suggest an image to go with it."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Scenario 10: Spotting a customer at risk of leaving<\/strong>"},{"t":"prompt","html":"Client [Name] has recently [described behavior, e.g., stopped opening emails, gone quiet]. Please analyze whether they might be at risk of leaving, and suggest ways and scripts to win them back."},{"t":"d","who":"Pat","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"This is great. I can just copy and use these right away."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Just remember, a prompt is a <strong>half-finished product<\/strong>. You still need to tweak it based on the real situation, like adding the client's name or specific details. AI is your assistant, not your replacement."},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>Prompt toolbox<\/strong> = ready-to-use \"ammo\" for any situation","<strong>10 golden scenarios<\/strong>: cold emails, price objections, social posts, thank-you notes, short videos, mock clients, referrals, presentations, social content, churn warnings","<strong>The key<\/strong>: always <strong>personalize<\/strong> after copying","<strong>Goal<\/strong>: generate a solid first draft in <strong>1 minute<\/strong>"]}],"minutes":4},{"n":98,"title":"Building Your AI Sales System from Scratch: The Tool Combo","part":4,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I've learned so many tools now, but I don't know how to combine them. Can you give me a plan for building an AI sales system from zero to one?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Sure, let me give you the <strong>\"AI Sales System Pyramid.\"<\/strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Bottom Layer: Data Foundation<\/strong>"},{"t":"ul","items":["<strong>CRM system<\/strong>: all customer data and follow-up records","<strong>Messaging app<\/strong>: all customer communication","<strong>Cloud documents<\/strong>: knowledge base and materials"]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Middle Layer: AI Tools<\/strong>"},{"t":"ul","items":["<strong>ChatGPT/Claude<\/strong>: writing copy, analyzing customers","<strong>Gemini<\/strong>: handling long documents, reviewing contracts","<strong>Meeting transcription tools<\/strong>: transcribing calls, pulling out key points","<strong>CRM assistant<\/strong>: automatic follow-ups, customer tagging","<strong>Low-code platforms<\/strong>: building a lead management system with no coding needed"]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Top Layer: Human-AI Collaboration SOP<\/strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Let me walk you through an <strong>AI-powered sales day<\/strong>:"},{"t":"d","who":"9:00 AM","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Open your AI-generated to-do list."},{"t":"ul","items":["AI tells you which clients to follow up with today, ranked by priority","Each client comes with a note on your last conversation and a suggested script"]},{"t":"d","who":"10:00 AM","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Make your first call."},{"t":"ul","items":["Before the call: have AI generate key talking points","During the call: record it using a transcription tool (let the client know)","After the call: AI transcribes it, pulls out action items, and drafts a follow-up email"]},{"t":"d","who":"2:00 PM","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Write cold emails."},{"t":"ul","items":["Use ChatGPT to generate a first draft","Personalize it","Send and track it using your email tool"]},{"t":"d","who":"4:00 PM","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Post to social media or short video platforms."},{"t":"ul","items":["Use AI to generate the copy or script","After posting, AI tracks engagement and reminds you to reply"]},{"t":"d","who":"6:00 PM","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Review your day."},{"t":"ul","items":["AI generates a daily work summary","Tomorrow's plan gets created automatically"]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Every Friday:<\/strong> AI generates your weekly report."},{"t":"ul","items":["Data gets pulled together automatically","Insights get summarized automatically","Next week's plan gets suggested automatically"]},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"How much would a system like this cost?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"You can start really cheap:"},{"t":"ul","items":["<strong>ChatGPT<\/strong>: free tier is enough","<strong>Gemini<\/strong>: free tier is enough","<strong>Otter.ai<\/strong>: free tier is enough","<strong>WhatsApp Business<\/strong>: free","<strong>CRM helper tool<\/strong>: basic version is a few hundred dollars a year","<strong>Data management software<\/strong>: free version is enough","<strong>Team collaboration platform<\/strong>: free"]},{"t":"p","html":"All together, it might cost you less than <strong>$2,000 a year<\/strong>. As your team grows, you can upgrade step by step."},{"t":"ms","items":["<strong>AI sales system<\/strong> = data foundation + AI tools + human-AI SOP","<strong>Daily flow<\/strong>: to-do list, calls, copy, content, review, weekly report","<strong>Starting cost<\/strong>: <strong>$2,000/year<\/strong>","<strong>Goal<\/strong>: let AI free up <strong>2 extra hours<\/strong> for you every day"]}],"minutes":3},{"n":99,"title":"Will Sales Be Replaced by AI?","part":5,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I still want to ask that very first question again. Will sales really not be replaced by AI?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Remember Question 1? I answered that back then. Now, after 99 questions, I want to give you a deeper answer."},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Please tell me."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"AI will replace a salesperson's <strong>repetitive actions<\/strong>, but it will never replace a salesperson's <strong>soul<\/strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"What are a salesperson's \"actions\"? Writing emails, sending messages, taking notes, analyzing data, generating reports. AI can do all of this, and faster and more accurately than you."},{"t":"p","html":"What is a salesperson's \"soul\"? It's the <strong>confidence<\/strong> you give a client when they're hesitant. The <strong>empathy<\/strong> you offer when they're struggling. The <strong>genuine joy<\/strong> you show when they succeed. The <strong>understanding<\/strong> you give when they make mistakes. AI will never learn any of that."},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So what should we focus on?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Turn everything you've learned in these 99 questions into <strong>muscle memory<\/strong>. Let AI handle the repetitive, time-consuming, boring stuff. Then use the time you save on things only you can do:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Have one more meal with a client and really listen to them talk about their family.","Spend an extra 10 minutes sending a heartfelt voice message to a discouraged client.","Think harder about whether this plan is truly best for the client.","Share one more lesson from your failures or wins with your team."]},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"So AI is here to free us?"},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"Exactly. AI isn't here to take your job. It's here to pull you out of the grunt work, so you can go back to being human: connecting, empathizing, creating."},{"t":"d","who":"Alex","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Thank you, Sifu Yik. I get it now."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"One last thought before you go. The more powerful the tools, the more powerful you need to become. The smarter AI gets, the smarter the person driving it needs to be."},{"t":"p","html":"The end of these 100 questions is really just the start of your growth. I hope you become the version of yourself that no one can replace in the AI era."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>[Final Revelations]<\/strong>"},{"t":"ul","items":["AI replaces <strong>actions<\/strong>, not the <strong>soul<\/strong>.","Your real value is <strong>empathy, connection, creativity, and judgment<\/strong>.","Use AI to <strong>free up your time<\/strong>, and use that time to build yourself.","The stronger the tools get, the stronger you need to be."]}],"minutes":3},{"n":100,"title":"Beyond AI, What Is the \"One\" Thing in Your Life?","part":5,"section":null,"blocks":[{"t":"p","html":"(Scene: a study. Sifu Yik and their partner sit across from each other. On the table lies a copy of *100 Questions on AI Sales Monetization*, just closed.)"},{"t":"d","who":"Casey","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"Sifu Yik, I finished the whole book. It feels like I just came out of a big battle, fully armed, plenty of ammo. But once the excitement faded, I felt kind of empty. AI is so powerful, and I've learned so many techniques. So what now? Where is my life actually supposed to go?"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Sifu Yik<\/strong> (looking into the distance, as if speaking to every reader): Casey, that question matters more than the other 99 combined. The *Tao Te Ching* says: \"The Tao gives birth to one. One gives birth to two. Two gives birth to three. Three gives birth to all things.\" In the first 99 questions, we showed you the \"all things\" of the sales world: the methods, the skills, the tools. Those are just the endless variations that come after \"three.\""},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"But if you only live in \"all things,\" it's easy to lose your way. You can learn every move in the book, but without a deeper logic underneath, you'll never become a true master. That's why we built this book around 100 questions: we wanted to help you find your \"one\" before you head back out into the world."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"This \"one\" is your life's <strong>operating system<\/strong>. Every technique in this book is just an app running on top of it. So what is your \"one\"? It's the reason you started in the first place. It's the values you won't compromise on. It's the unique value you want to bring to the world."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"This reminds me of what my mentors always say about \"passing on happiness.\" They never taught us tricks for getting happy. They taught us how to become a light, how to help others see clearly. They came from humble beginnings, and their lives showed us that the highest level of sales isn't selling, it's helping people cross to a better place. And to help others cross over, you first have to work on yourself. When you've fully shaped your own \"one,\" everything you say and do becomes your best business card. You yourself become the product."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"The financial wisdom we've shared isn't just about making money either. Behind it is a deeper understanding of how the world works, the logic of cause and effect. It takes years to turn that respect for how things work, and that commitment to real value, into your own \"one.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Sifu Yik<\/strong> (eyes lighting up): So Casey, these 100 questions aren't an ending. They're a beginning. The first 99 were the supplies we packed for your journey. This 100th question is your North Star."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Sifu Yik<\/strong> (standing, facing the reader, speaking slowly): We hope you take these 100 tools and go find your own \"one.\" Then spend your whole life writing it. One day, when you've found your own path and become a light for someone else, you'll understand: everything we did here was just to wait for you to truly begin, in the AI era."},{"t":"d","who":"Sifu Yik","role":"","sifu":true,"html":"And when that day comes, we and everyone else building alongside AI will be cheering for you. Because you'll have grown from a good salesperson into someone who genuinely helps others move forward in life."},{"t":"d","who":"Together","role":"","sifu":false,"html":"In the AI era, we're waiting for you to find your \"one.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Conclusion<\/strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Waiting for You to Begin in the AI Era<\/strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Hey, friend."},{"t":"p","html":"You've made it through all 100 questions. From the worry of \"Will AI replace me?\" to the practical steps of \"How do I use AI to write a cold email.\" From years of trial and error to thousands of livestreams putting it all to the test, these 100 questions are the tools we can hand you."},{"t":"p","html":"But here's the thing: the moment you close this book, your real learning starts."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>About the times we live in<\/strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"We've lived through four major shifts in technology. Every single time, people said, \"This one's different,\" or \"I don't think I can keep up.\" And every single time, we made it through."},{"t":"p","html":"Not because we were smarter than everyone else. Just because we had one extra thought: let's try it."},{"t":"p","html":"Try livestreaming, even if only 13 people show up."},{"t":"p","html":"Try building your own network, even if nobody responds at first."},{"t":"p","html":"Try AI, even if what it writes at first isn't very good."},{"t":"p","html":"The times never leave behind the people who are willing to try."}],"minutes":5}],"afterword":[{"t":"h","html":"About AI"},{"t":"p","html":"People often ask us: is AI hard to learn?"},{"t":"p","html":"Our answer: learning AI isn't hard. Starting is."},{"t":"p","html":"Once you begin talking to AI, you'll notice it's like a friend with endless patience. Ask it anything, and it answers. Tell it to change something, and it changes right away. Get frustrated with it, and it never pushes back."},{"t":"p","html":"Slowly, you'll come to like the feeling of it:"},{"t":"ul","items":["When you can't come up with copy, there's someone thinking it through with you.","When you're trying to understand a client, there's someone helping you sort out your thoughts.","When you're reviewing your numbers, there's someone building the report for you."]},{"t":"p","html":"AI isn't a cold, lifeless tool. It's a partner you can actually talk to."},{"t":"h","html":"About prompts"},{"t":"p","html":"Sifu Yik often says this: if you know how to ask AI good questions, you know how to ask the world good questions."},{"t":"p","html":"The prompt templates in this book aren't meant to be copied word for word. They're meant to teach you <strong>how to ask<\/strong>:"},{"t":"ul","items":["How to turn a vague idea into a clear instruction.","How to break a complicated problem into simple steps.","How to let AI work with you, not think for you."]},{"t":"p","html":"People who know how to ask sharp questions never get left behind by the times."},{"t":"p","html":"One last thing before we go: reading these 100 questions, understanding them, remembering them, that's only 10 percent of the work. The other 90 percent happens outside this book."},{"t":"p","html":"It happens the moment you open your phone or laptop tomorrow."},{"t":"p","html":"The first time you let AI draft a cold email for you."},{"t":"p","html":"The moment you cringe at what AI hands you, then fix it yourself."},{"t":"p","html":"A month later, when you've kept using AI to review your work, and your numbers have actually gone up."},{"t":"p","html":"It took us thirteen years and four major shifts, and more than 1,400 livestreams, to test every path in this book. But here's what we want you to know: you don't need thirteen years."},{"t":"p","html":"All you need is:"},{"t":"ul","items":["10 hours to really learn one tool.","10 hours to get comfortable with a set of prompts.","10 hours to run through one full process."]},{"t":"p","html":"Those 30 hours might be worth more than the 10,000 hours you've already spent working hard but working blindly. Because AI doesn't just help you work faster, it helps you work differently."},{"t":"p","html":"So here's our final question for you:"},{"t":"p","html":"What's your first AI action today?"},{"t":"p","html":"Just one. Keep it simple. It could be:"},{"t":"ul","items":["Using AI to write a cold email.","Using AI to analyze a client's social media.","Using AI to generate a short video script.","Using AI to review your work from this week."]},{"t":"p","html":"One action is enough. Tomorrow, do a second one. The day after, a third."},{"t":"p","html":"A hundred days from now, you'll notice:"},{"t":"ul","items":["The stuff that used to give you headaches, AI is handling it.","The clients who used to make you anxious, AI is helping you understand them.","The reports that used to keep you up at night, AI is putting them together."]},{"t":"p","html":"And finally, you'll have time for the things only you can do: caring for a client, spending time with your family, thinking about your bigger goals and what really matters."},{"t":"p","html":"We've walked this road. We've felt that same anxiety. And we've enjoyed these same rewards."},{"t":"p","html":"So now, we want to watch you get there too."},{"t":"p","html":"The AI era is here. Don't be afraid."},{"t":"p","html":"You're not alone in this."},{"t":"p","html":"Now close the book. Open your phone or laptop."},{"t":"p","html":"Go try it."},{"t":"sig"},{"t":"p","html":"Waiting to walk this road with you, in the AI era."}]};
